2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Komnena Angelina (c. 1176 - 1212) was a daughter of the Byzantine Emperor Alexios III Angelos and of Euphrosyne Doukaina Kamatera.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her first marriage was to the sebastokratōr Isaac Komnenos, a great-nephew of the emperor Manuel I Komnenos. They had one daughter, Theodora Angelina. Soon after Anna's father became emperor, in 1195, Isaac Komnenos was dispatched
2 CONC  to combat the Vlach-Bulgarian Rebellion. He was captured, became a pawn between rival Bulgarian and Vlach factions, and died in chains.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her second marriage to Theodore Laskaris, eventually emperor of Nicaea, was celebrated in a double wedding in early 1200 (the other couple was Anna's sister Eirene and Alexios Palaiologos). Anna and Theodore had three daughters an
2 CONC d two sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Nikolaos Laskaris (d. c. 1212)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Iōannēs Laskaris (d. c. 1212)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Eirene Dukaina Komnene Laskarina, who married first the general Andronikos Palaiologos and then John III Doukas Vatatzes
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Maria Laskarina, who married King Béla IV of Hungary
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Eudokia Laskarina, engaged to Robert de Courtenay, married bef. 1230 Anseau de Cayeux, Governor of Asia Minor
2 CONT
