1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodora_Angelina_Palaiologina
2 CONT
2 CONT From the union of the despot Alexios Palaiologos and Irene Komnene was born an only daughter; her first name of Theodora and the patronymic of Comnena that she seems to have used are known to us by the typikon drawn up by her son 
2 CONC Michael VIII for the monastery of Saint-Michel on Mount Saint-Auxentius. The despot Alexios Palaeologus having married Irene Comnena in the spring of 1199, the birth of Theodora will be fixed with probability at the year 1200. Sti
2 CONC ll very young, ca. 1213 she was given in marriage to Andronikos Palaiologos, the future great domestic, with whom she had at least four children: Maria, Irene, Michael and John.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodora put on the monastic habit at the last minute and changed her first name to that of Theodosia. She died at an unknown date but apparently before her husband who died at the beginning of 1247.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean-Claude Cheynet, Jean-François Vannier. Etudes prosopographiques (1986) (pp 178–79)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.ru/books?id=x7a1cRMNz3UC&printsec=frontcover&hl=ru#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2012611453.htm#TheodoraPborn1200
2 CONT
2 CONT i)         ''' THEODORA Palaiologina''' ([1200]-).  Georgios Phrantzes records that "reliquit Alexius Palaeologus unam filiam" by his wife "Alexius Angelus Comnenus imperator…filia…Irene" and that she married "Androniko Palaeologo
2 CONC "[27].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([1216]) as his first wife, ANDRONIKOS Doukas Komnenos Palaiologos, son of ALEXIOS Palaiologos & his wife --- ([1190]-Thessaloniki [1248/52]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
