1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://finnholbek.dk/getperson.php?personID=I61794&tree=2
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2010571204.htm#AnnaDMGeorgiosPalaiologos
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.        ''' ANNA Doukaina''' (-[1110/35]).  The Alexeiad names Anna as the wife of Georgios Palaiologos, her origin being deduced from the text stating that "the protovestiaria" was his mother-in-law and making it clear that the
2 CONC  couple married before the Komnenoi plot against Emperor Nikeforos Botaneiates[583].  It is likely that she was older than her brother Ioannes, who was described in the same source as "only a young boy" around the same time.  The 
2 CONC typikon of Theotokos Kecharitomenes (dated to [1110]) provides for the future commemoration of "la...sœur de ma Majesté, la pansébaste sébaste kyra Anna Doukaina" on the date of her death[584].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 1081) GEORGIOS Palaiologos, son of NIKEFOROS Palaiologos & his wife [--- Kurtikina] ([1110/36]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
