2 CONT 2.         THEODORA Komnene.  Her betrothal is shown in Europäische Stammtafeln[58] but the primary source on which this is based has not been identified  The betrothal was terminated because of the church's objections[59]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Europäische Stammtafeln[60] suggests that Theodora was the same person as '''[https://www.geni.com/people/Ana-Komneni-Angelina/6000000003493086926 Anna Komnene Angelina], possible wife''' of Maio [II] Count of Kefalonia.  The ba
2 CONC sis for this speculation is not known.  As noted above, it would be chronologically more acceptable for Maio's wife to have been the daughter of Mikhael [I] Lord of Epirus than his half-sister.  However, the only source as yet ide
2 CONC ntified points the other way.  ''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed''' (before 1217) to --- of Serbia, son of STEFAN Grand Župan of Serbia.  Her betrothed has not been identified, although he may have been Stefan Radoslav of Serbia, son of Stefan Grand Župan of Serbia & his first wife
2 CONC  Evdokia Komnene Angelina ([1191/1201]-after 1235), who succeeded his father in [1224/27] as Radoslav "Krapalo" King of Serbia.  If this is correct, the betrothal would have been agreed at the same time as that of Theodora's siste
2 CONC r Maria to Radoslav's father.
