1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivanko_(Bulgarian_boyar)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ivanko''' (Bulgarian: Иванко) killed [https://www.geni.com/people/Ivan-Asen-I-tsar-of-Bulgaria/375693712960012610 Ivan Asen I], ruler of the renascent Second Bulgarian Empire, in 1196. The murder occurred when Asen angrily summ
2 CONC oned Ivanko to discipline him for having an affair with his wife's sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1197 Ivanko, who was a Vlach according to the terminology used by Niketas Choniates, married* Theodora Angelina, the daughter of Anna Angelina and the sebastokrator Isaac Komnenos. Theodora's father had died in Bulgarian captiv
2 CONC ity not many months earlier.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ivanko, who adopted the Greek name '''Alexios''', fought at first for his grandfather-in-law, the Byzantine emperor [https://www.geni.com/people/Alexios-III-byzantine-emperor/6000000000515214098 Alexios III Angelos], but afterward
2 CONC s turned against him. He captured the general Manuel Kamytzes in 1198; Kamytzes was ransomed by his son-in-law, Ivanko's rival, [https://www.geni.com/people/Dobromir-Chrysos/6000000184448459930 Dobromir].
2 CONT
2 CONT The emperor's sons-in-law [https://www.geni.com/people/Alexios-III-Komnenos-Angelos-Byzantine-Emperor/359296347560011021 Alexios Palaiologos] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodoros-I-Emperor-of-Nicaea/6000000001501010534 Theod
2 CONC ore Laskaris] marched against Ivanko in 1200, and he was eventually captured when Alexios promised not to harm him in a peace council but then took him prisoner.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT  *if there was a marriage, it was not consummated
2 CONT ------
