2 CONT This family started with two men who are believed to have been brothers and somehow related to the family of Khan Krum: 
2 CONT *A1. Samuel, who became Tsar of the Bulgarians (997-1014), and moved the capital to Ochrida, he conquered Diocleia, Trebinje and Zahumlje, and made Bosnia and Raska (Serbia) vassals of Bulgaria, +Prilep 1014; m.ca 970 Agathe, dau.
2 CONC of Joannes Chryselios, Lord of Durazzo
2 CONT ** ...
2 CONT *A2. Aaron, ruler of western Bulgaria (976-987/8), +murdered 987/8
2 CONT ** B1. Iwan Wladislaw, Tsar of the Bulgarians (1015-18), +k.a.Durazzo 1018, after which Bulgaria became a Byzantine province; m.Marija N
2 CONT *** C1. Fruschin, in 1029 he was blinded and banished to a monastery
2 CONT *** C2. Alusian; m.an Armenian lady
2 CONT **** D1. Basileios Alusianos
2 CONT **** D2. Samoel Alusianos; m.N Delassene, sister of the Empress Eudoxia
2 CONT **** D3. Anna, +ca 1065; m.Romanos IV Diogenes, Emperor of Byzantium (+1072)
2 CONT *** C3. Aaron, Duke of Vaspurakan, of Edessa and of Macedonia
2 CONT **** D1. Theodoros Aaron, strategos of Taron, +k.a.against the Turks 1055/56
2 CONT *****D2. Radomir, a Byzantine official
2 CONT *** C4. '''Trojan'''
2 CONT **** D1. Maria, +after 1089; m.before 1063 Andronikos Dukas, co-emperor of Byzantium (+1077)
