2 CONT
2 CONT i)         ''' THEODORA Palaiologina Komnene Kantakouzene''' ([1240]-6 Dec 1300).  Pachymeres records the marriage of "Theodoram e Cantacuzanorum gente, Palaeologi neptam ex sorore" and "Georgium Muzalonem Atramyttinum"[479].  Pac
2 CONC hymeres records that "Ioannem…Raulem, protovestiarii Raulis filium" married "vidua protovestiarii Muzalonis…Theodora, neptis…imperatoris Palaeologi, eius sororis Eulogiæ ex Cantacuzeno filia" (in [1261/62])[480].  She became a nun
2 CONC  after the death of her second husband[481].  Pachymeres names "Theodora" as daughter of Eulogia[482].  She became a nun after the death of her second husband[483].  She was imprisoned in [1277] for opposing Emperor Mikhael VIII's
2 CONC  policy of pursuing the reunion of the Orthodox and Roman churches[484].  "Theodora niece of Mikhael Palaiologos" was accused of "magical machinations against the emperor's health" and, according to Pachymeres, was tested by being
2 CONC  put into a bag with some cats[485].  After the accession of Emperor Andronikos II she was released.  She restored the church of St Andrew of Crete at Krisis in Constantinople and lived in the convent there for the rest of her lif
2 CONC e, during which she amassed a library and acquired a reputation for learning.  She wrote hagiographies of the 9th century Theophanes the Confessor and his brother Theodore[486].  She made an unsuccessful attempt to negotiate with 
2 CONC Alexios Philanthropenos who in 1295 rebelled in Asia Minor and was proclaimed emperor[487].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (1256) GEORGIOS Mouzalon, son of --- (-murdered Sosandra Sep 1258).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ( [1261/62] ) IOANNES Raoul Komnenos Doukas Angelos Petraliphas, son of ALEXIOS Raoul & his wife --- Batatzaina (-[1273/74]).  Protobestiarios 1261. 
