1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexios_Angelos_Philanthropenos
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexios was married to Maria Angelina Radoslava (born late 1356 or after, if she is the daughter of Irene Asanina), a daughter of the Serbian general Radoslav Hlapen, and was supported by the powerful local magnates. Around 1382, 
2 CONC Alexios sought the protection of the Byzantine Empire, recognizing the suzerainty of the prince Manuel Palaiologos, who at the time governed Thessalonica as an appanage. Alexios is lastly recorded in 1388, and must have died by c.
2 CONC  1390, when he was succeeded by his son (or perhaps brother), Manuel.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radoslav_Hlapen
2 CONT
2 CONT Radoslav Hlapen married Irina (Irene), the widow of caesar Preljub. They had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  Maria Angelina Radoslava, married Alexios Angelos Philanthropenos
