1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jadwiga of Greater Poland
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jadwiga of Greater of Poland (1266 – 10 December 1339) was the second of three daughter, born to Boleslaw the Pious and Jolenta of Poland. Her paternal grandparents were Ladislaus Odonic Plwacz and Jadwiga of Pomerania, her matern
2 CONC al grandparents were Béla IV of Hungary and Maria Laskarina. Her elder sister was Elisabeth of Greater Poland. In 1293, Jadwiga married Władysław I the Elbow-high,[1] son of Casimir I of Kuyavia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband was a bitter rival with Wenceslaus II of Bohemia who was King of Poland between 1291–1305. Life was dangerous for Jadwiga and her family during this time, she and three of her children had to go into hiding for a while
2 CONC  during 1300. In 1305, Wenceslaus II died and was succeded by his son, Wenceslaus III of Bohemia. Wenceslaus III reigned for a year before he was assasinated under mysterious circumstances so his campaign of Poland ended. His wife
2 CONC , Viola Elisabeth of Cieszyn had not bore him any children so his successor was Władysław.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1318, Władysław embarked on a coronation campaign. The pope, though initially unwilling, finally granted his approval and Władysław and Jadwiga were crowned King and Queen of Poland on 30 January 1320 in Kraków. The coronation 
2 CONC was a sign that he had overcome Poland's internal fragmentation and re-united and re-instated the country as an independent kingdom under his rule. Poland now needed friends abroad; so in 1320, Jadwiga and Władysław's daughter Eli
2 CONC sabeth married Charles I of Hungary, son of Charles Martel of Anjou and Klementia of Habsburg. Their son was Louis I of Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband died in 1333. Jadwiga lived until 1339.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Jadwiga had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen of Poland (d. 1306)
2 CONT
2 CONT Władysław of Poland (d. 1311/1312)
2 CONT
2 CONT Kunigunde of Poland (c. 1298 – 9 April 1331). Married first Bernard of Świdnica. Their children included Bolko II of Świdnica. Married secondly Rudolf I, Elector of Saxony.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth of Poland (1305 – 29 December, 1380). Married Charles I of Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Casimir III of Poland (30 April 1310 – 5 November 1370)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jadwiga of Poland (d. 3 June 1320/1322)
