2 CONT
2 CONT Piroska of Hungary (1088 – 13 August 1134) was a daughter of Ladislaus I of Hungary and Adelaide of Swabia. Her maternal grandparents were Rudolf of Rheinfeld and his second wife Adelheid of Savoy. Adelheid was a daughter of Otto 
2 CONC of Savoy and Adelaide of Turin.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Esztergom of the modern Komárom-Esztergom administrative county. Her mother died in 1090 when Piroska was about two years old. Her father died on 29 July 1095. Ladislaus was succeeded by his nephew Coloman of Hunga
2 CONC ry who apparently was the new guardian of orphaned Piroska.
2 CONT
2 CONT In an effort to improve relations with Alexius I Comnenus of the Byzantine Empire, Coloman negotiated the marriage of Piroska to John II Comnenus. John II was the eldest son of Alexius I and Irene Ducaena. He was already co-ruler 
2 CONC of his father since 1 September 1092 and was expected to succeed him. The negotiations were successful and Piroska married John in 1104. The marriage was recorded by Joannes Zonaras and John Kinnamos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following her conversion to the Eastern Orthodox Church and settlement in Constantinople, Piroska was renamed Irene. She and John had eight children. The primary source about their order of births is the chronicle of Niketas Choni
2 CONC ates:
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Alexios Komnenos, co-emperor from 1122 to 1142. His birth is recorded in the Alexiad by Anna Komnene.  -2. Maria Komnene (twin to Alexios), who married John Roger Dalassenos.  -3. Andronikos Komnenos (died 1142).  -4. Anna Kom
2 CONC nene, married Stephanos Kontostephanos.  -5. Isaac Komnenos (died 1154).  -6. Theodora Komnene (d. 12 May, 1157). , who married Manuel Anemas.  -7. Eudokia Komnene, who married Theodoros Vatatzes.  -8. Manuel I Komnenos (died 1180
2 CONC ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Source / Forrás: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irene_of_Hungary In hungarian: http://hu.wikipedia.org/wiki/Szent_Piroska
2 CONT
