1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =====  Not the same as his maternal  grandfather   https://www.geni.com/people/Alexios-Philanthropenos/6000000009251421370 (...-1275)
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexios_Philanthropenos
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexios Doukas Philanthropenos''' (Greek: Ἀλέξιος Δούκας Φιλανθρωπηνός) was a Byzantine nobleman and notable general. A relative of the ruling Palaiologos dynasty, he was appointed commander-in-chief in Asia Minor in 1293 and f
2 CONC or a time re-established the Byzantine position there, scoring some of the last Byzantine successes against the Turkish beyliks.[1] In 1295 he rose up in revolt against Andronikos II Palaiologos, but was betrayed and blinded. Noth
2 CONC ing is known of him until 1323, when he was pardoned by Andronikos II and sent again against the Turks, relieving a siege of Philadelphia, allegedly by his mere appearance. He was then named briefly governor of Lesbos in 1328, and
2 CONC  again in 1336, when he recovered the island's capital from Latin occupation. He ruled the island thereafter, probably until his death in the 1340s. .. ... .... 
