2 CONT Chapter 4.    ARANITI
2 CONT
2 CONT This family's lands extended from behind Valona towards the north east to Mokro on the western shore of Lake Ohrid[188].  The primary sources which confirm the parentage and marriages of the members of this family have not yet bee
2 CONC n identified, unless otherwise stated below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         COMINO Araniti .  m ---, daughter of NIKOLA Sakati Lord of Sendir & his wife ---.  Comino & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT *a)         '''GJERGJ Araniti (-after 1456)'''.  He raised a large rebellion among his own tribesmen against the Ottomans in 1433, which quickly spread throughout Albania from Valona to Skadar and defeated three major Ottoman atta
2 CONC cks between 1433 and 1436.  The rebellion was finally suppressed in 1436[189].  He was established by Venice as Grand Vojvoda between Skadar and Dürres in 1456, at which time his daughter married the son of Stefan Crnojević, previ
2 CONC ously appointed Grand Vojvoda in Zeta[190].  m firstly MARIA Musaki, daughter of ANDREA Musaki & his wife Ana Zenevesi (-before 1444).  A manuscript which records details of the Musaki family notes the marriage of "signor Arainiti
2 CONC  Comnino…signor de Cerminica et de Mochino e de Spatennia" and "signora Maria [Musachi]"[191].  m secondly (before 1449) as her second husband, PIETRINA Franco, widow of --- Sarmazza from Corfu, daughter of OLIVIERO Franco Barone 
2 CONC di Taurisano & his wife --- (-in Italy after 11 Jul 1489).  The name of Gjergj's wife is not known.  '''Gjergj & his first wife had nine children:'''
2 CONT **i)          ANDRONIKA (-after 1500).  A manuscript which records details of the Musaki family names "la prima signora Andronica, la seconda signora Goysava, la terza signora Chiranna, la quarta signora Helena, la quinta signora 
2 CONC Despina, la sesta signora Angelina, la settima signora Comita, l´ottava signora Caterina" as the eight daughters of "signor Arainiti Comnino…signor de Cerminica et de Mochino e de Spatennia" and his wife "signora Maria [Musachi]",
2 CONC  adding that Andronika married "il signor Scanderbego Castrioto…signor de Dibra e de Matia e de Croya…"[218].  m (26 May 1451) GJERGJ Kastriot, son of GJON Kastriot & his wife --- ([1404]-17 Jan 1468). 
2 CONT **ii)         GOJSAVA (-before Jul 1469).  A manuscript which records details of the Musaki family names "la prima signora Andronica, la seconda signora Goysava, la terza signora Chiranna, la quarta signora Helena, la quinta signo
2 CONC ra Despina, la sesta signora Angelina, la settima signora Comita, l´ottava signora Caterina" as the eight daughters of "signor Arainiti Comnino…signor de Cerminica et de Mochino e de Spatennia" and his wife "signora Maria [Musachi
2 CONC ]", adding that Gojsava married "signor Giovanni Cernovichi…signore de Cernagora e de Ceta"[219].  m as his first wife, JOVAN [Ivan] Crnojević, son of STJEPAN Crnojević Djurašević & his wife Mara Castriota (-early Jul 1490). 
2 CONT **iii)        THOMAI [Tomaso] (-after 11 Jul 1489).  Papal protonotary. 
2 CONT **iv)       KYRANA .  A manuscript which records details of the Musaki family names "la prima signora Andronica, la seconda signora Goysava, la terza signora Chiranna, la quarta signora Helena, la quinta signora Despina, la sesta 
2 CONC signora Angelina, la settima signora Comita, l´ottava signora Caterina" as the eight daughters of "signor Arainiti Comnino…signor de Cerminica et de Mochino e de Spatennia" and his wife "signora Maria [Musachi]", adding that Kyran
2 CONC a married "il signor Giorgio Ducaguino" by whom she had two sons[220].  m NIKOLLA Dukagjin, son of --- (-after 25 Jun 1462). 
2 CONT **v)        ELENA .  A manuscript which records details of the Musaki family names "la prima signora Andronica, la seconda signora Goysava, la terza signora Chiranna, la quarta signora Helena, la quinta signora Despina, la sesta s
2 CONC ignora Angelina, la settima signora Comita, l´ottava signora Caterina" as the eight daughters of "signor Arainiti Comnino…signor de Cerminica et de Mochino e de Spatennia" and his wife "signora Maria [Musachi]", adding that Elena 
2 CONC married "il signor Giorgio Ducaguino" and had several children who all converted to Islam, of whom "Scanderbego et…Sangiacco" were living [when the manuscript was written][221].  m GJERGJ Dukagjin, son of --- (-before 1462). 
2 CONT **vi)       DESPINA .  A manuscript which records details of the Musaki family names "la prima signora Andronica, la seconda signora Goysava, la terza signora Chiranna, la quarta signora Helena, la quinta signora Despina, la sesta
2 CONC  signora Angelina, la settima signora Comita, l´ottava signora Caterina" as the eight daughters of "signor Arainiti Comnino…signor de Cerminica et de Mochino e de Spatennia" and his wife "signora Maria [Musachi]", adding that Desp
2 CONC ina married "il signor Tanusso Ducaguino" by whom she had one son and one daughter "signora Theodora" who had two sons "il signor Blasio e lo signor Jacobo"[222].  m TANUSO Dukagjin, son of ---. 
2 CONT **vii)      ANGELJINA (-Krušedol 1516).  A manuscript which records details of the Musaki family names "la prima signora Andronica, la seconda signora Goysava, la terza signora Chiranna, la quarta signora Helena, la quinta signora
2 CONC  Despina, la sesta signora Angelina, la settima signora Comita, l´ottava signora Caterina" as the eight daughters of "signor Arainiti Comnino…signor de Cerminica et de Mochino e de Spatennia" and his wife "signora Maria [Musachi]"
2 CONC , adding that Agneljina married "signor Stefano…figliolo del signor Despoto de Servia…Giorgio"[223].  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names Angelina Arianiti as the wife of Stephen[224].  She became a nun at Krušedol in Hungary[2
2 CONC 25].  The manuscript Vaticanus latinus 4789 records that “Etienne”, son of “le seigneur Georges Cantacuzène...[sa sœur] Irène” and her husband “[le] despote de Serbie”, married “la fille de l´Albanais, la sœur du seigneur Constant
2 CONC in”[226].  Theodoros Spandounes records that "Stefano Despoto" married "Angelina figliola del signor Golemo Araniti"[227].  m (Skutari 1461) STEFAN Branković, son of DJURADJ Branković Despot of Serbia & his wife Eirene Kantakouzen
2 CONC e ([1417]-Belgrado in Friulia 9 Oct 1476). 
2 CONT **viii)     COMITA (-[1461]).  A manuscript which records details of the Musaki family names "la prima signora Andronica, la seconda signora Goysava, la terza signora Chiranna, la quarta signora Helena, la quinta signora Despina, 
2 CONC la sesta signora Angelina, la settima signora Comita, l´ottava signora Caterina" as the eight daughters of "signor Arainiti Comnino…signor de Cerminica et de Mochino e de Spatennia" and his wife "signora Maria [Musachi]", adding t
2 CONC hat Comita married "il signor Colco Balsichi…signor de Misia" by whom she had one son and one daughter "signora Maria" who married "lo signor conte de Muro" and had two daughters "la signora donna Beatrice e…signora donna Isabella
2 CONC ", of whom the former married "signor Don Ferrante Orsino duca de Gravina" and the latter "signor Luise de Gesualdo conte de Conza"[228].  m GOJKO Stresi Balšić Lord of Misja, son of --- (-after 1478). 
2 CONT **ix)       KATERINA .  A manuscript which records details of the Musaki family names "la prima signora Andronica, la seconda signora Goysava, la terza signora Chiranna, la quarta signora Helena, la quinta signora Despina, la sest
2 CONC a signora Angelina, la settima signora Comita, l´ottava signora Caterina" as the eight daughters of "signor Arainiti Comnino…signor de Cerminica et de Mochino e de Spatennia" and his wife "signora Maria [Musachi]", adding that Kat
2 CONC erina married "lo signor Nicolò Bocali" by whom she had two sons "lo signor Manoli e lo signor Constantino Boccalj" and two daughters[229].  m firstly ANDREA Span, son of ---.  m secondly NIKOLA Bochalis Barone della Morea, son of
2 CONC  --- (-[1519]).  m thirdly ([1519]) MERCURIO Bua-Spata Signor de Viano e Cerveteri, son of ---.                     .... '''Gergj & his second wife had four children:''' 
2 CONT **x)        KONSTADINI [Constantino] COMINO Araniti ([1456/57]-Montefiore 8 May 1530).  He was called "Principe di Macedonia, Duca di Acaja" in 1490.  Regent of Monferrato 1495-1499.  Imperial Vicar General in Italy.  Signor di Oz
2 CONC ano e Terugia 1492-1521.  Signor di Fano 1515.   m ([1495/99]) [as her first husband,] FRANCESCA Paleologo di Monferrato, illegitimate daughter of BONIFAZIO IV Marchese di Monferrato & his mistress --- (-after 27 Dec 1561).  She m
2 CONC aybe married secondly ([1535]) --- Caracciolo.  Konstadini & his wife had seven children[230]. 
