2 CONT '''Barnim I von Pommern''', Herzog
2 CONT
2 CONT Barnim I "the Good" was born around 1210, from the Griffin dynasty and became the Duke of Pomerania (ducis Slauorum et Cassubie) from 1220 until his death on November 13th, 1278 at the age of 68.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Life==
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Duke Bogislaw II and Miroslawa, daughter of Duke [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mestwin_I,_Duke_of_Pomerania Mestwin I of Pomerelia], he succeeded to the Duchy of Pomerania-[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stettin Stettin] upon
2 CONC  his father's death in 1220; he had however to share the rule of Pomerania with his cousin [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wartislaw_III,_Duke_of_Pomerania Wartislaw III], who resided at [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demmin Demmin].
2 CONC  A minor when his father died, his lands until about 1226 were under regency of his mother Miroslawa from the Pomerelian [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samborides Samboriden] dynasty. At first still a [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/
2 CONC Kingdom_of_Denmark Danish] fief, the Pomeranian lands fell back to the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Roman_Empire Holy Roman Empire] after the victory of several North-German princes at the 1227 [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/
2 CONC Battle_of_Bornh%C3%B6ved_%281227%29 Battle of Bornhöved]. Emperor [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_II,_Holy_Roman_Emperor Frederick II of Hohenstufen] in 1231 put the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duchy_of_Pomerania Duchy o
2 CONC f Pomerania] under the suzerainty of the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Ascania Ascanian] margraves of [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margraviate_of_Brandenburg Brandenburg], disregarding the tenure of the Griffin dynasty a
2 CONC nd thereby fueling the long-term [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandenburg%E2%80%93Pomeranian_conflict Brandenburg–Pomeranian conflict].
2 CONT
2 CONT After his cousin Wartislaw III had formally accepted the Brandenburg overlordship by the 1236 Treaty of Kremmen, Duke Barnim I came to terms with the mighty Ascanian margraves in the 1250 [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_La
2 CONC ndin Treaty of Landin]: he confessed himself a Brandenburg vassal and had to renounce the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uckermark Uckermark] region, nevertheless he reached the consent, that the fief of his cousin Wartislaw would 
2 CONC remain with the Griffin dynasty upon his death. When Duke Wartislaw III died in 1264, Barnim I was able to unite the whole Duchy of Pomerania under his rule. He promoted the ''[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostsiedlung Ostsiedlung]
2 CONC '' by introducing [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germans German] settlers and customs into the duchy, established many [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_town_law towns], among them [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prenzlau Prenzlow
2 CONC ], [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Szczecin Stettin], [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gartz Gartz], [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anklam Anklam], [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stargard_Szczeci%C5%84ski Stargard], [http://en.wikipedia.
2 CONC org/wiki/Gryfino Greifenhagen], [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyrzyce Pyritz], [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ueckerm%C3%BCnde Ueckermünde] and [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goleni%C3%B3w Goleniów]. He was also known for his genero
2 CONC us ecclesiastical foundations and supported the extension of the secular reign of the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bishopric_of_Cammin Cammin bishops] in the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ko%C5%82obrzeg Kołobrzeg] area.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Barnim died at the town of Altdamm (German) [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C4%85bie,_Szczecin Dąbie], today part of Szczecin. The Minnesinger [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meister_Rumelant Meister Rumelant] wrote a dirge in 
2 CONC his honour.
2 CONT
