1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Roman Danilovich (c. 1230 (?) - 1288) - Prince of Slonim, Lutsk (until 1254), Prince of Novogrudok (1254-1258). The fourth son of the Galician king Daniel Romanovich.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1252, under an agreement with the Hungarian king Bela IV, Daniel married his son, Prince Roman of Lutsk, to the niece of the Austrian Duke Friedrich Babenberg, the daughter of his brother Henry, Gertrude (d. 1299). Gertrude was
2 CONC  the heir to the Austrian throne, which gave Roman the right to make claims to Austria and Styria.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Czech prince Ottokar, who entered Austria with an army at the end of 1251, forced the Austrian barons to elect him as a duke. Ottokar believed he had some dynastic claim to the Austrian throne since Gertrude was first married 
2 CONC to his brother Vladislav, who died in 1247. In February 1252, Ottokar formally secured his position in Austria by marrying the already elderly Margarita Babenberg, the eldest among the sisters of the late Duke, who was also the wi
2 CONC dow of the German king Henry VII of Hohenstaufen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Soon, Roman was besieged by the superior forces of the Czech king Ottokar in the Gimberg castle located not far from Vienna. Convinced that the cause of Roman was lost, the Hungarian king Bela IV himself began to claim those Austr
2 CONC ian lands that still remained under the rule of Gertrude. At the end of 1253, Roman had to hastily flee from Austria and return to Novgorodok.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1254 Prince Voyshelk gave Roman Novogrudok from Mindovg, Volkovysk, and Slonim from himself.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1258, Voyshelk and Tovtivil entered into a conspiracy and captured Roman Danilovich, from which he was soon released. In 1259, he helped Boleslav the Shy and Zemovit of Mazovia against Casimir of Kuyavia, and then, with his unc
2 CONC le Vasilko and brother Leo, participated in Burundai's campaign against Sandomierz.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family and Children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Father: Daniil Romanovich (1201-1264), Grand Duke of Kyiv (1240), Prince (1238-1264), 1st King of Galicia (1254-1264)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Mother: Anna, daughter of Mstislav Udatny, (d. 1252)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Wives:
2 CONT ** Elena Glebovna Volkovskaya
2 CONT ** Gertrud Babenberg (d. 1299), daughter of Henry of Austria (1208-1228)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sons:
2 CONT ** Mikhail (c. 1252 -?) - there is an assumption that Mikhail Romanovich - the son of Roman and his wife Elena Volkovskaya - the princely family of Drutsky traces the history. This is one of the versions of the origin of the Druts
2 CONC ky family.
2 CONT ** Vasilko (mid-XIII century) - Prince of Slonim
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter:
2 CONT ** Maria (b. 1253), married from 1270 to Joachim Gutkeled, son of Ban Stephen IV of Zagreb, former Hungarian governor of Styria
