2 CONT *G8. István V King of Hungary
2 CONT **H3. a daughter; m.'''Sventislav Jakab'''(?), Tsar of Bulgaria 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BULGARIA.htm#JakovSvetoslavdied1275
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         JAKOV SVETOSLAV, son of --- (-murdered [1275/77]).  Of Russian origin, he was created despot in Bulgaria in 1261 (although by which rival Tsar is not known) and granted land south of Vidin province.  He was granted Vidi
2 CONC n under a treaty agreed with Hungary, which had invaded to drive Byzantine forces from Jakov's lands in 1263.  From the time of a second Hungarian invasion in 1266, he was referred to in Hungarian documents as JAKOV SVETOSLAV Tsar
2 CONC  of the Bulgarians[377].  He was able to assert his independence from Hungary after the accession of the minor King László IV in 1272, and negotiated a settlement with his rival Tsar Konstantin Tih, who adopted him as his second s
2 CONC on in 1273.  He was poisoned by Maria, third wife of Konstantin Tih[378].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([1273]) as her second husband, THEODORA Laskarina, widow of MATHIEU de Mons Baron of Veligosti, daughter of THEODOROS II Emperor in Nikaia & his wife Elena Asanina of Bulgaria (-after 1273).  Georgius Akropolites names "I
2 CONC oannem…Theodoram et Eudociam" as the three remaining unmarried children of Emperor Theodoros II[379].  Ephræmius names "parvulum Ioannem…duasque virgunculas, Eudociam…ac Theodoram" as the three children still remaining at home whe
2 CONC n "Theodorus" died[380].  Pachymeres records that "pueri Ioannis sorores germanas…unam" married "nobili Latino Malo de Belicarto" and that "tertiam" married "Bulgaro Sphentisthlabo…circa Hæmum regionis in Mysia principi"[381].  As
2 CONC  Georgius Akropolites (a contemporary) only names four sisters in total, it is likely that two of the three marriages recorded by Pachymeres relate to the same daughter.  As Evdokia left south-eastern Europe after her marriage (se
2 CONC e below), it is more likely that Theodora's (first) husband died early and that she was the daughter who married the Bulgarian prince.  The primary source which confirms that this is correct has not been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
