1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ana-Neda
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ana-Neda''' (Bulgarian Анна-Неда and Serbian Cyrillic: Ана-Неда[a]; fl. 1323–1324) was the Empress consort of Bulgaria briefly in 1323–1324 as the spouse of "Despot of Vidin" Michael Asen III "Šišman" who was elected as Emperor
2 CONC  of Bulgaria in 1323.[1][2] Later, she acted, for a short period of time, as regent for her son.[3] She was the daughter of Serbian King [https://www.geni.com/people/Stefan-Milutin-king-of-Serbia/6000000002187576521 '''Stefan Uroš
2 CONC  II Milutin'''] and Princess Elizabeth Arpad, [4][5] daughter of King Stephen V of Hungary and Elizabeth the Kuman, a daughter of Köten. From the marriage with Michael Asen III, Anna had at least four sons, one of whom was Ivan St
2 CONC ephen of Bulgaria, later briefly the Emperor of Bulgaria (1330–1331).[5] 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ana-Neda En]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ana-Neda#Life Life]====
2 CONT
2 CONT Ana was the daughter of Serbian King [https://www.geni.com/people/Stefan-Milutin-king-of-Serbia/6000000002187576521 '''Stefan Uroš II Milutin'''] and his third wife, Elizabeth of Hungary.[4][1] She was therefore possibly born some
2 CONC time before 1284, when her father appears to have divorced Elizabeth to marry Anna of Bulgaria.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her marriage with Michael Asen III produced:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Michael, despotes (in Vidin?), probably the eldest son, died before 1330[7]
2 CONT * Ivan Stephen of Bulgaria, emperor of Bulgaria in 1330–1331, died between 1339 and 1357[8][5]
2 CONT * Šišman, potential pretender to the Bulgarian throne at Constantinople in 1341[9]
2 CONT * Lodovico, pretender to the Bulgarian throne in the Kingdom of Naples, died after 1363, probably distinct from any of the above[10]
2 CONT
