1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleanor_of_Anjou
2 CONT ------
2 CONT Eleanor of Anjou (August, 1289 - 9 August 1341) was the Queen consort of Frederick III of Sicily.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the third daughter of Charles II of Naples and Maria Arpad of Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her paternal grandparents were Charles I of Sicily and Beatrice of Provence. Her maternal grandparents were Stephen V of Hungary (d. 1272) and his wife, queen Elisabeth, who was daughter of Zayhan of Kuni, a chief of the Cuman tri
2 CONC be and had been a pagan before her marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT On 17 May 1302, Eleanor married Frederick III of Sicily. Her father and her new husband had been engaged in a war for ascendancy in the Mediterranean Sea and especially Sicily and the Mezzogiorno. The marriage was part of a diplom
2 CONC atic effort to establish peaceful relations which would lead to the Peace of Caltabellotta (19 August, 1302).
2 CONT
2 CONT The peace divided the old Kingdom of Sicily into an island portion and a peninsular portion. The island, called the Kingdom of Trinacria, went to Frederick, who had been ruling it, and the Mezzogiorno, called the Kingdom of Sicily
2 CONC  contemporaneously, but called the Kingdom of Naples by modern scholarship, went to Charles II, who had been ruling it. Thus, the peace was formal recognition of an uneasy status quo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor and Frederich had nine children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter II of Sicily (1304 – 1342), successor
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger (born 1305), died young
2 CONT
2 CONT Manfred, Duke of Athens and Neopatria (1306 – 1317), Duke of Athens and Neopatria
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance, married on December 29, 1331 to Leo IV of Armenia
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth,(1310 – 1349), married (1328) Stephen II of Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT William, Prince of Taranto (1312 – 1338), Prince of Taranto, Duke of Athens and Neopatria
2 CONT
2 CONT Giovanni di Randazzo (1317 – 1348), Duke of Randazzo, Duke of Athens and Neopatria, Regent of Sicily (from 1338)
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine (1320 – 1342)
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (1331 – 1360), married (1348) Rudolf II of the Palatainate
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/capet/capet19.html#LC2
2 CONT
2 CONT A2. King Charles II "le Boiteux" of Naples and Jerusalem (1285-1309), Ct of Provence, *1254, +Casanova 6.5.1309, bur Aix-en-Provence; m.1270 Maria of Hungary (*ca 1257 +25.3.1323)
2 CONT *B12. '''Leonora, *VIII.1289, +Monasterio de San Nicola, Arene 9.8.1341, bur Catania'''; m.Messina 17.5.1302 King Federigo I of Sicily (*1272 +Panterno 25.6.1336, bur Catania)
