1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Excellent in family, character and education, incomparable in appearance, very lovely in body but more so in soul, with the character of a man in a woman's form, best of empresses and sebastokratorissas  βελτίστη β
2 CONC ασιλίδων καὶ σεβαστοκρατορισσῶν σέβας ὁμοῦ καὶ κράτος.   (Prodromos, Historische Gedichte XLIV.20-28 )
2 CONT
2 CONT She was an enthusiast for literature, always thirsty for reading and education, always devoted to books and delighted by them; her whole life has become literature  ψυχὴ ... φιλολογωτάτη, ἀεὶ διψῶσα γνώσεως καὶ λόγου καὶ παιδείας,
2 CONC  βίβλοις ἀεὶ προστέτηκας, ἐπεντρυφᾷς τοῖς λόγοις, καὶ γίνεταί σοι τῆς ζωῆς ἅπας ὁ χρόνος λόγος.   (Manasses, Chronicle 3-6 )
2 CONT
2 CONT Richly generous ... high-born, beautiful descendent of powerful kings, shining brighter than the moon ...  ὀλβιόδωρε ... ἀριστοτόκεια, νυὲ χαριτοπρόσωπε μεγασθενέων βασιλήων ... πλέον ἀστράπτουσαν ... σελήνης.   (Manasses, Chronic
2 CONC le: Dedication 2-4 )
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Irene Aineidasa nacida después de 1100 y fallecida en Protocrator, Grecia, en 1152, casó en 1124, con Andrónico Comnene, que nació en Balalista, Grecia, en 1108, y murió en 1142. Tuvieron por hijos a Eudoxia Comnene (desp. de 1128
2 CONC ; casó con Andrónico I Comnene -1110 a 1185-, y tuvieron por hija a Irene Comnene, esposa de Isaac II Angelos, emperador de Bizancio: ver Dinastía Angelos)
