2 CONT Brother [and sister], whose parents are not known: 
2 CONT * ...
2 CONT *7.         '''MANUEL Anemas''', son of --- (-[1146/47]).  It is not known how Manuel Anemos was related to the previous family group, if at all.  From a chronological point of view, it is likely that there were two intervening ge
2 CONC nerations between the four brothers Anemos shown above and Manuel.  Panhyperprotosebastypértatos.  m THEODORA Komnene, daughter of Emperor IOANNES II & his wife [Piroska] [Eirene] of Hungary ([1116]-12 May 1157[56]).  The obituary
2 CONC  of the typikon of the Pantocrator (dated Oct 1136) records (among the list of living persons) “tis kaisarisses kyras Marias, tis kyras Annes, tis kyras Theodoras, kai tis kyras Eudokias”, after “tou sebastokratoros kyrou Manouel 
2 CONC tov filtaton mou thigateron”, implying that all four were his daughters[57].  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.  She became a nun after her husband died.  Manuel Anemas & his wife had at l
2 CONC east four children:
