2 CONT ==The Komnenos family==
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel Komnenos, +1020, in 978 defended Nicaea against Skloros; m.two women whose names are unknown and had issue: 
2 CONT * A1-A2
2 CONT * A3. Ioannes Komnenos, *1015, +1067; m.ca 1042 Anna Dalassene, dau.of Alexios Charon, Prefect of Italy
2 CONT ** B3. ALEXIOS I Komnenos, Emperor of Byzantium (1081-1118), *1048/57, +15.8.1118; 1m: ca 1075 Argyropulina N (+ca 1077); 2m: ca 1078 Eirene Dukaina (*1066 +1123/36) 
2 CONT *** C1. IOANNES II Komnenos Dukas, Emperor of Byzantium (1118-43), *1087, +8.4.1143; m.1104/5 Piroska=St.Eirene of Hungary (+13.8.1134) 
2 CONT **** D4. MANUEL I Komnenos, Emperor of Byzantium (1143-80), *1118, +24.9.1180; 1m: 1146 Bertha=Eirene von Sulzbach (+1159/60); 2m: 1161 Maria de Poitiers (*1145 +27.8.1182) 
2 CONT ***** E1. [1m.] '''Maria Komnene, *1152, +of poisoning 1182'''; she had been engaged to King Bela III of Hungary and to King William II of Sicily, but Byzantine politics kept those matches from being consummated; m.1180 Rainer de 
2 CONC Montferrat (*1163 +1182) 
