2 CONT Ioannes & his wife had [six] children:
2 CONT *1.         '''MIKHAEL Doukas Komnenos Angelos (-murdered Constantinople 1307)'''.  Pachymeres records that "Michaeli Ioannis Ducæ Occiduorum…sebastocratoris filio" was tricked by the offer of marriage to the daughter of "Annæ reg
2 CONC inæ consobrinæ suæ…ex Eulogia natæ", but was kidnapped and sent to Constantinople where he was imprisoned[70].  This must presumably be dated to after his betrothal to the daughter of the Bulgarian Tsar.  Pachymeres, in a later pa
2 CONC ssage, records that "maximus natu frater Michael [referring to "in partibus Occiduis Ioannis sebastocratoris filio…Ioannis"] detinebatur" in Constantinople[71].  Betrothed ([1283, contract broken 1283/84]) to --- Asanina, daughter
2 CONC  of IVAN ASEN III Tsar of the Bulgarians & his wife Eirene Palaiologina.  Pachymeres records the betrothal of "Michaeli Ioannis Ducæ Occiduorum…sebastocratoris filio" to "filiam ex Asane natam"[72].  The dating of this betrothal i
2 CONC s unclear from the text, but it presumably predated Mikhael's capture and imprisonment in Constantinople.  The identity of the daughter of Tsar Ivan Asen is not known, but she was probably either Maria or Theodora, daughters of th
2 CONC e Tsar known from other sources. 
2 CONT *2. ...
