2 CONT
2 CONT This family's lands lay between the upper Mati and upper Drin Rivers, eastwards to Debar[233].  The primary sources which confirm the parentage and marriages of the members of this family have not yet been identified, unless other
2 CONC wise stated below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         GJON Kastrioti (-[1437/40]).  He accepted Venetian suzerainty and citizenship in 1413.  He held Tirane, and the territory north to the Mati River, by 1415.  He submitted to Ottoman suzerainty in 1417[234].  He took cont
2 CONC rol of the coastal territory between the Mati and Erzen Rivers [1417/20], taking advantage of the decline of the Thopia family after the death in 1415 of Nikola Thopia.  m VOISAVA Tripalda, daughter of ---.  Gjon & his wife had ni
2 CONC ne children:
2 CONT *a)         REPOSH (-after 1426).  He died as a monk at the monastery on Mount Sinai. 
2 CONT *b)         STANISHA (-after 1445).  Lord of Matja and Dibra.  Citizen of Venice 1438.  m ---, a Turk.  -        SCANDERBEGH CASTRIOTA, DUKES of FERRANDINA[235]. 
2 CONT *c)         KONSTADINI (in Turkey before 1438). 
2 CONT *d)         GJERGJ Kastrioti ([1404]-Jan 1468).  ...
2 CONT ** ... 
2 CONT *e)         MARIJA .  m STJEPAN Crnojević Voivode of Zeta, son of DJORDJE Djurašević Lord of Zenta, Budva and part of Sclavonia & his wife --- (-1465). 
2 CONT *f)          JELA .  m GJIN Musaki, son of ---. 
2 CONT *g)        ''' ANGJELINA''' .  m VLADEN GOLEM Araniti Lord of Biasca and Çermenica, son of COMINO Araniti & his wife ---. 
2 CONT *h)         VLAICA .  m STEFAN Maramonte Stresi Balšić Lord of Dulcigno (-after 1444). 
2 CONT *i)          MAMICA .  m (26 Jan 1445) [KARLO] Musachi Thopia, son of --- (-killed in battle 1455). 
2 CONT
