2 CONT Pal Dukagjini (1411–1458) participated in the League of Lezhë and was an ally of Scanderbeg. On 21 October 1454 Alphonso V of Naples informed Skanderbeg that Pal Dukagjini sent his envoys and declared his loyalty and vassalage to 
2 CONC the Kingdom of Naples. Based on that Alphonso V awarded Pal Dukagjini with 300 ducats of annual provisions.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pal had four sons, Lekë, Nikollë, Progon and Gjergj Dukagjini.
2 CONT
