1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ulrich I von Sonnegg is first mentioned in a deed dated 1262, where he is mentioned alongside his brother Leopold. Both get mentioned again in a deed dated 1278. Next he is mentioned on his own in deeds dated 1262 
2 CONC and 1301. In 1303 he appears in another deed which also involves Ulrich, count of Pfannenberg, as a counterparty. Further references in 1306 and 1309 prove that he was still alive then, whereby he is recorded to have assisted Fred
2 CONC eric, duke of Styria, in quelling a local rebellion. He was married twice: first to Katharina von Heunburg and secondly to Agnes von Baden (according to a document dated 1302).
2 CONT
2 CONT Please note that there may be additional information in the Slovenian-language version of this profile.
