2 CONC 1260[215].  "Arnaldus Rogerii comes Pallariensis" confirmed a donation by "dominus Raimundus comes Pallieriensis" to Santa Maria de Gerri by charter dated 16 Sep 1260[216].  "Dominus Arnaldus Rogerii…comes Pallariensis et uxor nos
2 CONC tra domina Sanxa Pallierensi comitissa" donated property to Santa Maria de Gerri by charter dated 8 Aug 1270, subscribed by "Raimundi Rogerii fratris domini comitis"[217].  The testament of Arnau Roger Conde Pallars, dated 1 Oct 1
2 CONC 288, appointed executors including “Bort de Pallars hijo ilegitimo del testador” but does not name his wife or children[218].  
2 CONT
