1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Klementia_of_Habsburg
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Klementia of Habsburg
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Klementia of Habsburg (1262 - February 1293) was a daughter of Rudolf I of Habsburg and Gertrude of Hohenberg. She was a member of the House of Habsburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 8 January 1281 Klementia married Charles Martel of Anjou. She could have became Queen of Hungary but her husband died before his father did in 1295.
2 CONT
2 CONT Klementia and Charles Martel had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles I of Hungary, became King of Hungary in 1308, married three times, his second wife was Beatrix of Luxembourg and his third wife was Elisabeth of Poland. All of his surviving children were with Elisabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice of Hungary (1290-1343), the wife of John II of Viennois
2 CONT
2 CONT Klemetina of Hungary, the second wife of Louis X of France and mother of John I of France, the baby king. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]A chance to be Queen of Hungary
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Martel was set up by Pope Nicholas IV and the ecclesiastical party as the titular King of Hungary (1290–1295) as successor of his maternal uncle, the childless Ladislaus IV of Hungary against whom the Pope had already earl
2 CONC ier declared a crusade.
2 CONT
2 CONT He never managed to govern the Kingdom of Hungary, where an agnate of the Árpád dynasty, his cousin Andrew III of Hungary actually ruled that period. Charles Martel was, however, successful in asserting his claims in parts of Croa
2 CONC tia, a kingdom then in personal union with Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Martel died young in Naples, during the lifetime of his parents. Charles Martel and Klementia's son, Charles would ultimately succeed where he had failed in winning the throne of Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Klementia was the eighth of nine children, her younger sister was Judith of Habsburg. Judith who married Wenceslaus II of Bohemia was the mother of ten children, among them were Wenceslaus III of Bohemia, Anna I of Bohemia, duches
2 CONC s of Carinthia and Elisabeth I of Bohemia, duchess of Luxembourg. Klementia's daughter Clemence was the mother of John I of France, the baby king. John I died when he was only five days old so was succeded by his paternal uncle Ph
2 CONC ilip.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]
