2 CONC sociated with the omnipotence of the Church and its "moral" (see the Tour de Nesle more later) suggest that there were severe conditions.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip the Fair banned Helen seemed likely that the Court about this liaisont should be taboo. It is also likely that the King demanded that Helen and her children are installed discreetly in a neutral and why not, for example in 
2 CONC this small Hotel that Charles had acquired in 1285 in St Ouen ...
2 CONT
