1 OCCU комит на Средец, Governor of West Bulgaria, He ruled Serdica. He was a governor of regions in the western part of the First Bulgarian Empire., Count Of West Bulgaria
1 TITL Count
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comitopuli
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Cometopuli dynasty==
2 CONT
2 CONT The Cometopuli dynasty (Bulgarian: Династия на комитопулите; Byzantine Greek: Κομητόπουλοι) was the last royal dynasty in the First Bulgarian Empire, ruling from ca. 976 until the fall of Bulgaria under Byzantine rule in 1018. The
2 CONC  actual name of the dynasty is not known, “Cometopuli” is merely the nickname which is used by Byzantine historians to address rulers from the dynasty as its founder, boyar Nikola, was a comes (governor, cognate to "count"; Byzant
2 CONC ine Greek Κóμης, from the Latin; Bulgarian Комита Komita) probably of the region of Sredetz (the present-day capital of Bulgaria, Sofia).
2 CONT
2 CONT In view of his position and status, count Nikola is most likely to have been a member of the Slavonized Bulgar aristocracy and at least distantly related to the royal family of Tsar Peter I. According to other theories, the dynast
2 CONC y was of Slavic, or even Armenian[1][2] or Vlach origin. In 969 AD and following the Russian conquest of northwestern Bulgaria, count Nikola assumed control of the Bulgarian lands west of the Iskar. By the time of the Byzantine co
2 CONC nquest of Preslav and the dethronement of Tsar Boris II in 972, Nikola had been killed and the rule assumed by his four sons, David, Aaron, Moses, and Samuil. David led the defence of southwestern Bulgaria and resided in Prespa, M
2 CONC oses of southeastern Bulgaria residing in Strumica, Aaron ruled over the region of Sredetz, whereas Samuel was in charge of northern Bulgaria with the town of Bdin (Vidin).
2 CONT
2 CONT Both David and Moses lost their lives early – David was murdered by wandering Vlachs, whereas Moses died during the siege of Serres. A conflict broke out between Samuil and Aaron as the latter grew more and more pro-Byzantine and 
2 CONC on June 14, 976 Aaron was executed near Dupnitza. Later the same year, the dethroned Boris II and his brother, Romanus, managed to escape from captivity in Constantinople and reached the borders of Bulgaria. Boris II was, however,
2 CONC  killed by mistake by the border guards. As a result, it was Romanus who was crowned as Bulgarian Tsar although real power and the control of the army lay in the hands of Samuel. It was not until the death of Roman in 997 that Sam
2 CONC uel officially was crowned as Tsar in the absence of any other direct heirs to the throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Samuel in 1014, the crown passed on to his son, Gavril Radomir (1014 – 1015). In 1015, he was murdered by his first cousin and son of Aaron, Ivan Vladislav. With his own death in 1018 the First Bulgarian Empire 
2 CONC came to an end. An attempt at restoration of Bulgarian independence was made some 20 years later by Peter (II) Delyan (1040-1041), son of Gavril Radomir. He, aided by his cousin Alusian of Bulgaria organised an uprising and manage
2 CONC d to push away the Byzantines from Ochrid for a short period, but was eventually betrayed by Alusian. Alusian's heirs were given noble titles and land in the Byzantine Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Nikola the Comes was a father of counts David and Samuel. His son Samuel ruled as emperor of the First Bulgarian Empire from 997 to 1014.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''NOTE FROM DEBBIE GAMBRELL:
2 CONT
2 CONT I have searched and been unable to find ANYTHING documenting ANYONE in this line from here back.  There are no profile notes, no references, sources or anything to indicate real people or accurate connections.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cometopuli_dynasty
2 CONT
2 CONT https://translate.google.com/translate?hl=en&sl=pl&u=https://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Komitopuli&prev=search
2 CONT
2 CONT Bulgarian boyar from the time of Tsar Peter I (927-969), commune governing the province in the southwestern part of the Bulgarian tsarism
2 CONT
2 CONT https://pl.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Komitopuli
2 CONT
2 CONT Political history of the dynasty
2 CONT
2 CONT The first known representative of the family was Nikola, the administrator (Bulgarian Kommit , hence committeopuli - "sons of the comit") of Macedonia on behalf of the Bulgarian tsar. His four sons (Dawid, Mojżesz, Aron and Samuel
2 CONC  in the face of the collapse of the Bulgarian state in the clash with Byzantium in 971 formed a new Bulgarian power center in the western part of the state (in today's Northern Macedonia ), resisting Byzantium's efforts to include
2 CONC  these territories. Initially Roman , the last of the representatives of the Krum dynasty , became the tsar of the state created in this way, but the actual power was exercised from the very beginning by one of the brothers, Samue
2 CONC l Radzieopul (of the others, two died in fighting, the last, Aron, posing a threat to Samuel's position, was ordered) the latter murdered with his family.) When Roman in 991 got into Byzantine captivity, and then died in it in 997
2 CONC  Samuel crowned himself Tsar of Bulgaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicholas_(komes)_
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Armenian chronicler Stephen of Taron, the family originated in the Armenian region of Derdjan.[1][2] He was married to Ripsime or Hripsime, possibly (NOT) a daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Ashot-II-the-Ir
2 CONC on-king-of-Armenia/6000000002187821487?through=6000000002187821500 King Ashot II of Armenia] .[3][4][5] The couple had four sons, David, Moses, Aron, and Samuel, who are collectively known as the Cometopuli (from Greek Kometopoulo
2 CONC i, "sons of the komes"; Armenian կոմսաձագ Komsajagk)
