1 NOTE Theophano, 2nd wife of Emperor Leo Romanus II, was of low birth, but very beautiful.  It was thought Theophano poisoned her young and dissoulate husband, Romanus II.   Ruled as Empress 959-963.  She was the mother of emperors Basi
2 CONC l II and Constantine VIII.  She was regent alone in 963, then married General Nicephorus Phocas, who became emperor.  She was exiled in 970.  and died sometime after 976.
