2 CONT
2 CONT '''Andronikos Doukas''' (Greek: ''Ἀνδρόνικος Δούκας'', c. 1057 - c. 1077 or after 1081), Latinized as '''Andronicus Ducas''', was the third son of Byzantine emperor Constantine X Doukas (r. 1059–1067) and younger brother of Byzant
2 CONC ine emperor Michael VII Doukas (r. 1071–1078). Unlike his other brothers, he was not named junior co-emperor by his father, and was raised to the dignity only by Romanos IV Diogenes (r. 1068–1071). He is otherwise relatively insig
2 CONC nificant, and was not involved in the affairs of state to any degree.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2010571204.htm#KonstantinosXdied1067B
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.     '''    ANDRONIKOS Doukas''' ([1057]-after 1081).  Mikhael Glykas names "Michaelum, Andronicum et Constantinum purpurigenam" as the sons of Emperor Konstantinos & his wife[653].  Nikeforos Bryennios names "eius coniuge Eudoc
2 CONC ia, cum Michaele, Andronico et Constantino filiis" as survivors of "Ducas"[654].  Psellos records that "Michael and the younger son Andronicus" were born before their father's accession[655].  Psellos writes that "Andronicus, brot
2 CONC her of the Emperor Michael Ducas…is just past his boyhood"[656].  He was crowned co-emperor by his brother Emperor Mikhael VII after the latter assumed sole rule in Oct 1071.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (1068) --- of Hungary, daughter of BÉLA I King of Hungary & his wife [Ryksa] of Poland.  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not so far been identified.  She adopted the name MARIA in Byzantium
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
