2 CONT 8.         [daughter .  According to Miller[24], Emperor Theodoros bestowed the hand of his sister on Marco Sanudo after the latter was captured while attempting to take Smyrna.  He quotes Laurentius de Monachis and several Italia
2 CONC n chronicles which do not appear to be contemporary.  According to Sturdza[25], "it is certain" that this marriage did not take place.  It does seem surprising that Emperor Theodoros, the main opponent of the Latins, should have a
2 CONC rranged the marriage of his sister to one of the newly arrived Latin rulers, assuming that he had any marriageable sisters at all[26].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (1213) MARCO I Sanudo Duke of Naxos, son of MARCO Sanudo & his wife --- Dandolo (-1227).]  
