2 CONC o domino Joanne Cantacuzeno...”[449].  The record of the synod of 6 Mar 1166 records the presence of “...pansebasto sebasto et genero...nostri regis domino Joanne Cantacuzeno...”[450].  m ([1145/50]) as her second husband, MARIA K
2 CONC omnene, widow of THEODOROS Dasiotes, daughter of ANDRONIKOS Komnenos, sébastokrator & his wife Eirene [Aineiadissa] ([1126]-).  Ioannes Kinnamos records that "Ioannes cognomento…Cantacuzenus" married "Andronici sebastocratoris fil
2 CONC iam"[451].  Ioannes Kantakouzenos & his wife had [two] children:
2 CONT
2 CONT >a)         MANUEL Kantakouzenos .  Ioannes Kinnamos records that "Ioanni Contacuzene…filius erat Manuel"[452].  He was imprisoned and blinded by Emperor Manuel I before 1175[453].  Niketas Choniates names "Manuel Cantacuzenus"[45
2 CONC 4].  According to Sturdza[455], he was blinded in 1180. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >b)         ['''EIRENE Komnene .  The wife of Alexios Doukas Palaiologos is named Eirene Komnene, and a poem discloses that Eirene Komnene, daughter of Ioannes Kantakouzenos & his wife Maria Komnene daughter of sébastocrator Andro
2 CONC nikos married an unnamed Palaiologos.  It is assumed that the two women are the same person[456].  She is not mentioned by Nicol[457] or Trapp[458].  m (c1165)  ALEXIOS Doukas Palaiologos, son of [MIKHAEL Doukas Palaiologos, sébas
2 CONC tos & his wife ---].]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT but
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTINE%20NOBILITY.htm#TheodorosDasiotesdied1143
2 CONT
2 CONT THEODOROS Dasiotes (-Iconium [1143/44]).  He died in prison.  (1139) as her first husband, MARIA Komnene, daughter of ANDRONIKOS Komnenos sébastokrator & his wife Eirene [Aineiadissa] ([1126]-).  Niketas Choniates names "Maria…And
2 CONC ronici sebastacrator…filia" as wife of "Dasiotes"[204].  Theodoros Dasiotes & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >a)         '''EIRENE Komnene Dasiotissa.  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  m ALEXIOS Palaiologos Doukas, son of ---.  The connection between this individual and either the
2 CONC  Palaiologos or Doukas families has not been found.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2012611453.htm#PalaiologosM1165EireneKantakuzene
2 CONT
2 CONT ALEXIOS Doukas Palaiologos ([1140]-before 1203).  Megadux.  He became a monk as ANTONIOS.  
2 CONT m ( [1165] ) EIRENE Komnene, daughter of IOANNES Kantakouzenos & his wife Maria Komnene.  '''The wife of Alexios Doukas Palaiologos is named Eirene Komnene, and a poem discloses that Eirene Komnene, daughter of Ioannes Kantakouzen
2 CONC os & his wife Maria Komnene daughter of sébastocrator Andronikos married an unnamed Palaiologos.  It is assumed that the two women are the same person'''[31].  She is not mentioned by Nicol[32] or Trapp[33].  She became a nun as E
2 CONC UGENIA.     Alexios Palaiologos & his wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT >*a)         MIKHAEL Palaiologos (-in prison after 1257).  ... ... '''m''' ---.  The name of Mikhael's wife is not known.  Mikhael & his wife had one child:
