2 CONC ].  The Gestis Comitum Barcinonensium names "Constantia" as oldest of the three daughters of "Ildefonsi", specifying that she married "Regi Ungariæ" but returned childless to Aragon after his death[773].  The Chronicle of Alberic 
2 CONC de Trois-Fontaines names "Constantia regina" as wife of "Hemericus filius [regis Hungarie Bela]", specifying that she later married "Frederico imperatori"[774].  The Continuatio Admuntensis records that she took her son to Vienna 
2 CONC and, after his death, Leopold Duke of Austria arranged her repatriation to "fratri suo Hyspaniarum regi"[775].  She married secondly (Feb 1210) as his first wife, Friedrich King of Sicily, who was elected Friedrich II King of Germ
2 CONC any 5 Dec 1212 at Frankfurt-am-Main, and crowned Emperor in Rome 22 Nov 1220.  The Ryccardus de Sancti Germano Annales record the marriage in 1209 of "Fredericus rex Sicilie" and "Constantiam sororem regis Arragonum"[776].  The Co
