2 CONT a)         [IOANNES Angelos (-[1348/50]).  It is not certain that Ioannes was the son of the above, but it looks likely.  Ioannes Kantakouzenos names "magno domestico…Ioanni Angelo eius consobrino", "magnus domesticus" apparently 
2 CONC referring to the future Emperor Ioannes VI Kantakouzenos, in a passage dated to [1330][91].  Ioannes Kantakouzenos names "Ioannes Angelus pincerna, magni domestici consobrinus", in a passage dated to [1341][92].  Ioannes Kantakouz
2 CONC enos records that "consobrinum Ioannem Angelum" was appointed to "Thessaliæ præfecturam", in a passage dated to [1342][93].  Kephale of Kastoria, Epirus and Megalovlachia.  Ioannes Kantakouzenos records that "Angelo consobrino meo
2 CONC " had died earlier, in a passage dated to [1350][94].  He died of plague.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' --- Angelina, daughter of ANDRONIKOS Palaiologos Angelos & his wife --- Kokala.  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not been identified.]   
