1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2012611453.htm#MariaPdied1401
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.      '''   MARIA Palaiologina''' (-[1401]).  Georgios Phrantzes records that "Andronicus" had two daughters by his second wife, of whom the younger married "Orchanes"[279], which is not corroborated by other primary sources.  T
2 CONC he Historia Byzantina of Michælis Ducæ Nepotis records the marriage of "Franciscus Gateluzus" and "Mariam sororem meam [=Iohannis imperatoris]", with the island of Lesbos as her dowry[280].  Her brother Emperor Ioannes V bought su
2 CONC pport from Francisco Gattilusio, a Genoese corsair, to help restore him to the throne in return for marriage with Maria, with the island of Lesbos as her dowry.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([1355]) FRANCESCO Gattilusio patrician of Genoa, son of --- (-6 Aug 1384).  He reigned from 17 Jul 1355 as FRANCESCO I Lord of Lesbos. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irene_Paleologa_(signora_di_Lesbo)
2 CONT '''Irene Paleologa''' (ribattezzata '''Maria''' in greco Μαρία Παλαιολογίνα?; ... – 6 agosto 1384) era un principessa bizantina e Signora di Lesbo. Era la figlia dell'imperatore bizantino Andronico III Paleologo e di Anna di Savoi
2 CONC a. I suoi fratelli erano Giovanni, Michele e Maria.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Irene (renamed Maria) Palaiologina''', who married Francesco I Gattilusio.
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andronikos_III_Palaiologos#Family
2 CONT
2 CONT
