2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amadeus_VI,_Count_of_Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Amadeus VI''' (4 January 1334 – 1 March 1383), nicknamed '''the Green Count''' (Italian: ''Il Conte Verde'') was Count of Savoy from 1343 to 1383. He was the eldest son of Aymon, Count of Savoy, and Yolande Palaeologina of Mont
2 CONC ferrat. Though he started under a regency, he showed himself to be a forceful leader, continuing Savoy's emergence as a power in Europe politically and militarily. He participated in a crusade against the Turks who were moving int
2 CONC o Europe.  
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amadeus_VI,_Count_of_Savoy#Early_years  Early years]
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amadeus_VI,_Count_of_Savoy#Count_of_Savoy  Count of Savoy]
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amadeus_VI,_Count_of_Savoy#Crusade,_1366  Crusade, 1366]
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amadeus_VI,_Count_of_Savoy#Later_years Later years]
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amadeus_VI,_Count_of_Savoy#Marriage_and_children Marriage and children]
