1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2012611453.htm#EudokiaKantakouzenosMKomnenos
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         EUDOKIA .  The Masarelli Vatican manuscript names Andreas and Eudokia as the children of Manuel & his wife, stating that Eudokia married a grandson of the emperor of Trebizond but died without issue[592].  Her marriage 
2 CONC appears to be confirmed by Georgios Phrantzes who records an incident during the siege of Patras, dated to 29 Mar 1429, when he rescued Konstantinos Palaiologos [the future Emperor Konstantinos XI] but was captured after falling f
2 CONC rom his horse, a thoroughbred which "ameras" [the emir, unspecified] had given to “Isaacio Asani” who had later given it to “Georgio Philanthropeno genero [γαμβρω] suo” who, in turn had given it to “Comneno consobrino [ανεψιω], Ca
2 CONC ntacuzeni protostratoris genero [γαμβρω]”[593].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 29 Mar 1429) --- Komnenos, son of [Emperor in Trebizond & his second wife Anna Philanthropena. 
