1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =MAGNUS von Braunschweig=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Magnus I, Duke of Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel and Sophia von Brandenburg 
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRANDENBURG,%20PRUSSIA.htm#JohannIdied12661267  Project MedLands, Prussia, Brandenburg]
2 CONT
2 CONT ([1328]-killed in battle near Leveste 26 Jul 1373, bur Braunschweig Cathedral).  Co-regent of Braunschweig 1345.  Co-regent in Lüneburg 1367.  '''He succeeded in 1368 as MAGNUS II "Torquatus/mit der Kette" Herzog von Braunschweig-
2 CONC Lüneburg.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRUNSWICK.htm#MagnusIILuneburgdied1373B Project MedLands, BRUNSWICK]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''MAGNUS von Braunschweig, son of MAGNUS I "dem Frommen" Herzog von Braunschweig in Braunschweig und Göttingen & his wife Sophie von Brandenburg''' ([1328]-killed in battle near Leveste 26 Jul 1373, bur Braunschweig Cathedral).  
2 CONC Co-regent of Braunschweig 1345.  Co-regent in Lüneburg 1367.  '''He succeeded in 1368 as MAGNUS II "Torquatus/mit der Kette" Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg.''' '''married  (before 6 Oct 1356) as her first husband, KATHARINA von 
2 CONC Anhalt, daughter of BERNHARD III Fürst von Anhalt-Bernburg & his second wife Mathilde von Anhalt in Köthen und Zerbst (-30 Jan 1390, bur Lüneburg St Michaelis).'''  She married secondly (Hannover 10 Nov 1373, Celle 11 May 1374) Al
2 CONC brecht III Herzog von Sachsen-Wittenberg Herzog von Lüneburg.  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum records that “Hertoghe Albrecht to Sassen unde to Lunenborch” married “Hertoghen Magnus weddeven to Brunswick”, calling her
2 CONC  “ein Marggrevinne to Brandenborch” [presumably confusing her with the widow of Duke Magnus I][341]. Magnus II & his wife KATHARINA von Anhalt had twelve children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnus_II,_Duke_of_Brunswick-L%C3%BCneburg#Family Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus (1324–1373), called Magnus with the Necklace (Latin: Magnus Torquatus) or Magnus II, was Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg, ruling the Brunswick-Lüneburg principalities of Wolfenbüttel (colloquially also called Brunswick) and, tem
2 CONC porarily, Lüneburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus married Catherine, daughter of Bernhard III, Prince of Anhalt-Bernburg, who married Magnus' enemy, Albert, Duke of Saxe-Wittenberg, after his death. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Elisabeth ∞ Herzog Gerhard VI. von Schleswig-Holstein († 1404)
2 CONT *Friedrich (1357-1400) ∞ Anna von Sachsen († 1440)
2 CONT *Bernhard († 1434) ∞ Margarete von Sachsen (vor 1370-1418)
2 CONT * Heinrich der Milde († 1416)
2 CONT *Agnes I. († 1410) ∞ Herzog Albrecht I. von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen (1339-1383)
2 CONT *Helene ∞ Graf Erich I. von Hoya
2 CONT *Elisabeth († 1420) ∞ Graf Moritz IV. von Oldenburg (1380-1420)
2 CONT *Agnes II. (vor 1356-vor 1434) ∞ Herzog Albrecht III. von Mecklenburg, ab 1363 König von Schweden
2 CONT *Sophie (1358-1416) ∞ Herzog Erich IV. von Sachsen-Lauenburg (1354-1411)
2 CONT *Maud (1370-??) ∞ Graf Otto III. von Hoya († 1428)
2 CONT *Otto (um 1364-1406)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Magnus II Herzog von Braunschweig1
2 CONT M, #4732, b. circa 1328, d. 26 July 1373
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus II Herzog von Braunschweig was born circa 1328. He was the son of Magnus I Herzog von Braunschweig and Sophie von Brandenburg.2 He married Catherine von Anhalt-Bernburg, daughter of Bernhard III Prinz von Anhalt-Bernburg an
2 CONC d Matilde von Braunschweig, before 1356. He was murdered on 26 July 1373 at near Leveste by an unknown person.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus II Herzog von Braunschweig was a member of the House of Guelph.2 Magnus II Herzog von Braunschweig also went by the nick-name of Magnus 'the Younger'.2 Magnus II Herzog von Braunschweig also went by the nick-name of Magnus 
2 CONC 'Torquatus'. He succeeded to the title of Herzog von Braunschweig in 1369.2 Children of Magnus II Herzog von Braunschweig and Catherine von Anhalt-Bernburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Wfe: Elisabeth von Braunschweig+ d. bt 1417 - 1422
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard I Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg+2 d. 11 Jun 1434
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich I Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg+2 d. 14 Oct 1416
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto von Braunschweig d. 29 Jun 1406
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes I von Braunschweig+ d. 21 Mar 1410
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes II von Braunschweig1 d. b 22 Dec 1434
2 CONT
2 CONT Helen von Braunschweig+
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth von Braunschweig+ d. 2 Apr 1420
2 CONT
2 CONT Friedrich Herzog von Braunschweig+2 d. 5 Jun 1400
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie von Braunschweig+ b. c 1358, d. b 28 May 1416
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud von Braunschweig b. c 1370, d. bt 1432 - 1434
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 28. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
2 CONT * John Morby, Dynasties of the World: a chronological and genealogical handbook (Oxford, Oxfordshire, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1989), page 132. Hereinafter cited as Dynasties of the World.
2 CONT * Allgemeine Deutsche Biographie, vol. 20, p. 64-66
2 CONT * Zedlers Universal-Lexicon, vol. 19, p. 241-242
2 CONT * Christa Geckler: Die Celler Herzöge - Leben und Wirken 1371-1705. Georg Ströher, Celle 1986, ISBN 3-921744-05-8 (formal falsche ISBN)
2 CONT * Bernd-Ulrich Hergemöller: Magnus II.. In: Neue Deutsche Biographie (NDB). Band 15. Duncker & Humblot, Berlin 1987, S. 662 f
2 CONT * Paul Zimmermann: Magnus II.. In: Allgemeine Deutsche Biographie (ADB). Band 20. Duncker & Humblot, Leipzig 1884, S. 64–66.
2 CONT * Peter Steckhan: Magnus II. Torquatus. In: Horst-Rüdiger Jarck, Dieter Lent et al. (Hrsg.): Braunschweigisches Biographisches Lexikon: 8. bis 18. Jahrhundert. Appelhans Verlag, Braunschweig 2006, S.473f.
