2 CONT g)         BALTHASAR von Braunschweig ([1336]-Castel Sant'Elmo after 14 Jan 1384).  Engelhusius’s Genealogia ducum Brunswicensium names “Ottonem, Balthasar et Thomam” as the three sons of “[Dux] Henricus”[239].  Canon of St Blasiu
2 CONC s at Braunschweig 1354/61.  “Balthasar...Hertoghe to Brunswych” notified various documents to the council of Göttingen, including arrangements benefiting “unses Broder hertoghen Otten”, by charter dated 10 Nov 1370[240].  He was a
2 CONC warded the title Despot of Romania in 1376 by his sister-in-law Jeanne I Queen of Sicily, who also arranged his marriage.  After Queen Jeanne was deposed, Balthasar was captured by her successor Charles III and blinded 5 Aug 1382 
2 CONC in the Market Place of Naples on his orders.  He died in prison[241].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (1379) as her first husband, GIACOBELLA Caetani, daughter of ONORATO Caetani Conte di Fondi & his wife Catarina del Balzo (-after 25 May 1400).  She married secondly Henri de Blois-Châtillon. 
