1 NOTE John of Bohemia (1296-1346), the blind king, was son of Emperor Henry VII, and became king of Bohemia through his marriage with the heiress to the throne. There was a fierce contest between the houses of Austria and Bavaria for th
2 CONC e Bohemian empire, and John achieved the victory for Bavaria in 1322 at Muhldorf. He became an ally of the French king in the war against England, and was slain at Crecy. [World Wide Illustrated Encyclopedia, 1935]
