1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Svyatoslav Ivanovich''' (d. 1386) - '''Grand Duke of Smolensk''' (1359-1386), son of Ivan Alexandrovich of Smolensk.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1359 upon the death of his father, Svyatoslav took the throne of Smolensk. In 1368 Svyatoslav participated in the first campaign of Algirdas against Moscovia, during the so-called [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lithuanian%E2%80
2 CONC %93Muscovite_War_(1368%E2%80%931372) Litovschina]. During the time when Algirdas had to return to the western borders of his principality in order to repel the attack of the Teutons, the Moscovite troops undertook a retaliatory ca
2 CONC mpaign on the Smolensk lands. In 1370, the Smolensk troops took part in the second campaign of Algirdas against Moscovia, after which Svyatoslav received a threatening message from the Patriarch of Constantinople. In 1372, within 
2 CONC the framework of the peace treaty between Moscovia and Lithuania, the peace between Moscovia and Smolensk principality was also signed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Later Svyatoslav together with his nephew Ivan Vasilyevich Vyazemsky fought on the side of Moscovia. In 1375 Smolensk troops participated in Dmitry Ivanovich's campaign against Tver (Algirdas at that time raided Smolensk lands), a
2 CONC nd in 1380 - in the Battle of Kulikovo.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1386 Smolensk troops besieged Lithuanian-controlled Mstislavl, but soon the Polish-Lithuanian troops of Jogaila approached and defeated the Smolensk people (Battle on the Vekhra River). Svyatoslav and his nephew were killed in 
2 CONC battle, Svyatoslav's eldest son Gleb was captured, and his second son Yuri (married to the daughter of Oleg Ivanovich of Ryazan and Evpraxia Olgerdovna) took the throne of Smolensk.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Княжил в Смоленске с1358-1386 г.
