1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Karigaila (Polish: Korygiełło, died on September 16, 1390 in Vilnius) was a son of Algirdas, Grand Duke of Lithuania, and his second wife Uliana of Tver. He became the ruler of Mstsislaw after he captured it from t
2 CONC he Principality of Smolensk. He is sometimes mistaken for his brother Constantine, who was the founder of the House of Czartoryski.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his older brother Jogaila signed the Union of Krewo, Karigaila was baptized as Casimir in Kraków in March 1386. He then left Poland for the eastern part of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania in order to subdue his half-brother And
2 CONC rei of Polotsk, who had renewed his struggle for power against Jogaila. On April 29, 1386, he and his other brother Skirgaila soundly defeated Sviatoslav II of Smolensk, who had allied himself with Andrei and attacked Mstsislaw, i
2 CONC n the Battle of the Vekhra River.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Lithuanian Civil War (1389–92), Karigaila commanded the defense of the Crooked Castle in Vilnius.[1] The castle fell and he was killed. His brother Jogaila, now king of Poland, charged that Karigaila was taken captive a
2 CONC nd executed by decapitation by the Teutonic Knights; the Knights denied this and claimed that Karigaila was killed during the battle. Karigaila was buried at Vilnius Cathedral.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karigaila
2 CONT  a b c d (Lithuanian) Vytautas Spečiūnas, ed. (2004). "Karigaila". Lietuvos valdovai (XIII-XVIII a.): enciklopedinis žinynas. Vilnius: Mokslo ir enciklopedijų leidybos institutas. p. 58. ISBN 5-420-01535-8.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ripley, George; Charles Anderson Dana (1874). "Chartoryski". The American Cyclopaedia: A Popular Dictionary of General Knowledge V. New York: D. Appleton and Company. p. 623.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Urban, William (2006). Samogitian Crusade. Chicago: Lithuanian Research and Studies Center. p. 200. ISBN 0-929700-56-2.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Lithuanian) "Arkikatedra Bazilika". The Directorate of the State Cultural Reserve of Vilnius Castles. Retrieved 2008-07-08.
2 CONT
