1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elizabeth_of_Kuyavia'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth of Kuyavia''' (Polish: Elżbieta, Serbo-Croatian: Elizabeta/Елизабета; 1315/1320 – after 22 August 1345) was a Polish noblewoman of the House of Piast. She was the only daughter of Duke Kazimierz III of Gniewkowo[1] an
2 CONC d his wife, whose name and origins are unknown; her brother, Władysław the White, was later a candidate for the Polish throne.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1323, King Charles I of Hungary wanted to increase influence over Stephen II, Ban of Bosnia. He offered Stephan the hand of Elizabeth, the relative of his own Piast wife Elizabeth. By marrying Elizabeth of Kuyavia, Stephen rece
2 CONC ived from Charles the lands to the west formerly held by Mladen I Šubić of Bribir and Usora and Soli in the north formerly held by Vladislav, King of Syrmia. The marriage was celebrated by 1339. Up to 1339, Stephan was married to 
2 CONC an unknown Bulgarian princess.
2 CONT
2 CONT The only child which can be attributed to Elizabeth of Kuyavia without doubt is Elizabeth of Bosnia, born c. 1340.[2] Some[citation needed] believe that Catherine of Bosnia, Countess of Cilli, was daughter of Elizabeth of Kuyavia 
2 CONC and Stephen II, while others argue that Catherine was daughter of Stephen II's brother Vladislaus and his wife Jelena Šubić. Elizabeth may have also had a son, Vuk who may have survived infancy but he did not outlive his father so
2 CONC  never became Ban of Bosnia. Vuk may have been the son of one of Stephen's previous two wives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen outlived Elizabeth. It is unknown what Elizabeth died of. Judging by the time, it is possible that she died of Black Death, which was sweeping across Europe during the 14th century.[citation needed] Banness Elizabeth was b
2 CONC uried in Bobovac in a tomb which she shared with her husband, brother-in-law Vladislaus and sister-in-law Jelena.[3] After Elizabeth of Kuyavia's death, her daughter Elizabeth was fostered by the Hungarian queen dowager Elizabeth 
2 CONC and this soon led to Elizabeth's marriage to Louis I of Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT  Verkholantsev, Julia (2014-09-30). The Slavic Letters of St. Jerome: The History of the Legend and Its Legacy, or, How the Translator of the Vulgate Became an Apostle of the Slavs. Cornell University Press. ISBN 978-1-5017-5792-1
2 CONC .
2 CONT  Higgins, Sophia Elizabeth (1885). Women of Europe in the Fifteenth and Sixteenth Centuries. Hurst and Blackett. ISBN 978-0-7222-1702-3.
2 CONT  Mandić, Doninik: Franjevačka Bosna: razvoj i uprava Bosanske vikarije i provincije, 1340-1735, Hrvatski povijesni institut, 1968, page 231.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://bs.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elizabeta_Pjast
2 CONT Elizabeta Pjast je bila banica Bosne kao treća supruga bana Stjepana II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeta je bila kćerka kujavskog vojvode Kazimira III Pjasta. Ime njene majke nije poznato. Pripadala je dinastiji Pjast koja je vladala Poljskim kraljevstvom.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brak između Elizabete i Stjepana, koji je već bio dva puta oženjen (ortenburškom groficom i bugarskom carevnom), aranžirao je Karlo I Robert, kralj Ugarske, 1323. godine. Elizabeta je bila imenjakinja i rodica Karlove supruge, kra
2 CONC ljice Elizabete, a Karlo I Robert je želio ovim brakom steći veću kontrolu nad Stjepanom. Kao vjenčani dar, Stjepan je od Karla Roberta dobio zapadne zemlje koje je prethodno kontrolisao Mladen I Šubić Bribirski.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brak je bio ozakonjen 1339. godine. Do tada je Stjepanov brak s kćerkom nekog bugarskog cara još bio smatran validnim. Od njene djece, preživjele su dvije kćerke:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Elizabeta Kotromanić (1339-1387), ugarska i poljska kraljica, koja je imala tri kćerke i jednu unuku, ali danas nema potomaka
2 CONT     Katarina Kotromanić, celjska grofica, koja danas ima potomke na svim evropskim prijestoljima
2 CONT
2 CONT Banica Elizabeta je umrla za vrijeme života svoga muža. Dominik Mandić vjeruje da je sahranjena u Bobovcu, u istoj grobnici kao i njen suprug Stjepan, Stjepanov brat Vladislav i Vladislavova supruga Jelena. [1] Reference [uredi]
2 CONT
2 CONT     ↑ Mandić, Doninik: Franjevačka Bosna: razvoj i uprava Bosanske vikarije i provincije, 1340-1735, Hrvatski povijesni institut, 1968, page 231.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note''': Date and year of marriage as June 1324 is incorrect, correct year of marriage is 1335.
