1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Jelena Gruba==
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://hr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jelena_Gruba Hr], [https://bs.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jelena_Gruba Bs], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helen_of_Bosnia En], [https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elena_di_Bosnia It], [https://de.wikipedia.org/
2 CONC wiki/Jelena_Gruba De], [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jelena_Gruba Fr], [https://hu.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gruba_Ilona_bosny%C3%A1k_kir%C3%A1lyn%C5%91 Hu], [https://sr.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%88%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%93%D1%
2 CONC 80%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%B0_%D0%9A%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%9B Sr], [https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%95%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%93%D1%80%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%B0 Ru]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1395-98 Reigning Queen Jelena Gruba Her husband, Stephen Dabiša, had designated King Sigismund of Hungary, the husband of his relative, Queen Mary of Hungary, as his successor. The Bosnian nobility refuzed to recognize Sigismund a
2 CONC s king and installed her as the new monarch. It was during her reign that the Bosnian nobility grew in power independently from the crown. Amongst them were the famous Dukes Sandalj Hranić and Hrvoje Vukčić and Prince Pavle Radeno
2 CONC vić that ruled their own demesnes independently from the Queen. Her demesne was a small territory in central Bosnia, while she lost the suzeiranity over the territories of Usora in the valley of the river of Sava. Though she lost 
2 CONC some territory and control over nobility, Jelena's reign saw successful trade with the Republic of Dubrovnik.In 1398 she was replaced with Stephen Ostoja. It is unclear why she was replaced. It is possible that her brothers were g
2 CONC aining too much wealth and influence during her reign and the rest of the nobility didn't like it. She continued to reside at the court as queen dowager. Sources refer to her as the most serene and mighty lady Gruba. (d. after 139
2 CONC 9).
2 CONT
2 CONT Rođena je u plemćikoj porodici Nikolića, koji su vladali jednim dijelom Huma.  Udala se za Dabišu, vanbračnog polubrata kralja Tvrtka I.  Jelena Gruba je bila kraljica Bosne kao supruga kralja od 1391. godine do muževe smrti 1395.
2 CONC  godine. Jedino preživjelo dijete rođeno iz njihovog braka bila je kćerka Stana. Stanina kćer, čije se ime navodi kao Vladava  i Vladika , udala se za Juraja Radivojevića još za života svoga djeda Dabiše i nane Grube, što potvrđuj
2 CONC e Dabišina povelja iz 1395. kojom kralj poklanja selo Veljaci na upravu svojoj kćeri Stani, s tim da poslije njene smrti upravu nad selom naslijede Vladava (Vladika) i njen muž.  Jelenina unuka Vladava (Vladika) je imala djecu još
2 CONC  za vrijeme Jeleninog života i vladavine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jelena Gruba se u poveljama na latinskom potpisivala kao Helena, regina Bosniae, Stephani Dabissa[e] uxor (bosanski: "Jelena, kraljica Bosne, supruga Stjepana Dabiše"). Njena puna titula glasila je:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Mi, gospoja kira Jelena, po izvoljenju Božju kraljica Srbljem, Bosne i Primorju i zapadnem stranam i k tomu
