2 NOTE Philippa was born in Valenciennes (then in Flanders, now France) and was the daughter of William I, Count of Hainaut and Jeanne of Valois, the granddaughter of Philip III of France.
3 CONT
3 CONT She married Edward at York Minster, on 24 January 1328, eleven months after his accession to the English throne and, unlike many of her predecessors, she did not alienate the English people by retaining her foreign retinue upon he
3 CONC r marriage or bringing large numbers of foreigners to the English court.
3 CONT Read more about Pillippa in her profile.
