1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charles, Duke of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles,_Duke_of_Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles of Blois (Blois, 1319 – September 29, 1364), claimed the title duke of Brittany, from 1341 to his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles is the son of Guy I of Blois-Châtillon, count of Blois, by Margaret of Valois, a sister of king Philip VI of France. He was a devout man, who took piety to the extreme of mortifying his own flesh. It is said that he placed
2 CONC  pebbles in his shoes, wore ropes tight with knots near his flesh and confessed every night in fear of sleeping in a state of sin. He was nevertheless an accomplished military leader, who inspired loyalty by his religious fervour.
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 4, 1337 in Paris, he married Joanna the Lame, heiress and niece of duke John III. Together, Charles and Joanna fought the House of Montfort in the Breton War of Succession (1341-1364), with the support of the crown of Fran
2 CONC ce. Despite his piety, Charles did not hesitate in ordering the massacre of 2000 civilians after the siege of Quimper. After initial successes, Charles was taken prisoner by the English in 1347. He was released nine years afterwar
2 CONC ds against a ransom of about half a million ecús, and resumed the war against the Montforts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles died in the Battle of Auray which determined the end of the war and the victory of the Montforts. He was canonized as saint for his devotion to religion, but the process was made null by Pope Gregory XI by request of Duke 
2 CONC John V of Brittany. Subsequently, in 1904, he was beatified.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his marriage to Joanna, he had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT John I of Blois-Châtillon (1340–1404)
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry (d. 1400)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie (1345-1404), Lady of Guise, married in 1360 Louis I of Naples
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite, married in 1351 Charles de la Cerda (d. 1354)
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_I,_Duke_of_Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT En mi nuevo libro LA SORPRENDENTE GENEALOGÍA DE MIS TATARABUELOS, encontrarán a este y muchos otros de sus ancestros con un resumen biográfico de cada uno. El libro está disponible en: amazon.com            barnesandnoble.com     
2 CONC         palibrio.com.  Les será de mucha utilidad y diversión.  Ramón Rionda
2 CONT
2 CONT In my new book LA SORPRENDENTE GENEALOGÍA DE MIS TATARABUELOS, you will find this and many other of your ancestors, with a biography summary of each of them. The book is now available at:  amazon.com            barnesandnoble.com 
2 CONC             palibrio.com.  Check it up, it’s worth it. Ramón Rionda
