1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LUIGI of Sicily (Catania [1335]-Iacchi 1355).  He succeeded his father in 1342 as LUIGI King of Sicily, under the regency of his mother from 1348 to 1352, and of his sister Constanza from 1352 to 1354.  King Luigi 
2 CONC had two illegitimate children by unknown mistresses:  
2 CONT
2 CONT a)              don ANTONIO de Aragón ([1350/55]-).  m doña BEATRIZ de Ejérica Baronesa de Cocentaina, daughter of don PEDRO de Aragón Barón de Ejérica & his wife Bonaventura di Arborea ([1355]-after 1373).  
2 CONT
2 CONT b)              don LUIGI de Aragón ([1350/55]-after 1374).  Barone di Tripi.  
