1 NOTE QUEEN OF POLAND 1384-1399
1 NOTE Jadwiga of Poland, 2nd daughter of King Louis the Great of Hungary-Poland, and Elizabeth of Bosnia, was born 1374, the great-granddaughter of Charles "The Hammer" Martel.  Descendant of the kings of France, the Houses of Anjou and
2 CONC  Plantagenet, and others.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jadwiga or Hedviga of Poland became Queen of Poland in 1382, succeeded her father, Louis the Great of Hungary and Poland, of the House of Anjou.  Queen Jadwiga (like her sister Mary who ruled Hungary) became one of the first of th
2 CONC e female Queens to rule.  Jadwiga ruled until her death in 1399.  Her husband, Jagello, then ruled until his death in 1434.
