1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Miroslava (Bulgarian: Мирослава) was one of the daughters of tsar Samuil of Bulgaria and Kosara of Bulgaria. Princess Miroslava fell in love with the Byzantine noble captive Ashot Taronites and threatened to commit
2 CONC  suicide if she was not allowed to marry him. Samuel conceded and appointed Ashot governor of Dyrrhachium.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Later Ashot made contact with the local Byzantines and the influential John Chryselios, Samuel's father-in-law. Ashot and Miroslava boarded one of the Byzantine ships that were beleaguering the town and fled to Constantinople. In 
2 CONC Constantinople the Emperor Basil II granted Ashot the title of patrikios and Miroslava was honoured with the title of zoste patrikia (Lady-in-Waiting).
