2 CONT
2 CONT Nikephorus was the son of Phocas, the oldest confident ancestor of the family, who was initially Tourmarches (commander of a Turma, i.e. a partial province) and was appointed Strategos (military governor) of the Anatolia by Empero
2 CONC r Basil I in 872. Neither the name nor the origin of his mother is known, but it is suspected that she was of Armenian origin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==PHOCAS==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===(An influential Cappadocian family which had originated in Armenia)===
2 CONT
2 CONT * [MAMN181] Hmayeak I m. ?
2 CONT ** . [PHOC211] Prince Artavazd of Georgia m. ?
