2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20LORDSHIPS%20IN%20GREECE.htm#MarcoINaxosdied1227
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         ANGELO Sanudo (-1262).  The Istoria of Marino Sanudo Torsello names "Miser Angelo Sanudo" as son of "Miser Marco Sanudo, ch´ aquistò le Isole"[753].  He succeeded his father in 1227 as ANGELO Duke of Naxos.  His fleet o
2 CONC f ships helped in the defence of Constantinople against the attack by the Nikaian/Bulgarian alliance in 1236, leading the vanguard with Geoffroy II Prince of Achaia on whom the Latin Emperor conferred the suzerainty over Naxos and
2 CONC  the Archipelago as a reward for his services[754].  Vexed by Angelo's support for the Latin empire, Ioannes III Emperor in Nikaia captured the island Amorgos, which he bestowed on Geremia Ghisi[755].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (Constantinople) ---, daughter of MACAIRE de Saint-Ménéhould Seigneur de Charax & his wife ---.  The Istoria of Marino Sanudo Torsello records that "la madre de miser Marco Sanudo" was "figlia de miser Machario de Santo Mo
2 CONC ntalto di Campagna di Francia", adding that she had been married "in palazzo del…Imperator Latino"[756].  "A French dame of high degree",  She welcomed Baudouin ex-Emperor of Constantinople when he attempted to reclaim his throne 
2 CONC in 1262, her husband being awarded the title "king" as a reward for her services[757].  Duke Angelo & his wife had three children:  
