2 CONT '''BALIAN of Ibelin''', son of BALIAN of Ibelin Lord of Rama & his wife Helvis of Rama ([1142/43]-[May 1193/94]).  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "mesire Hue, et mesire Baudoyn, et mesire Belleem" as the three sons of "Be
2 CONC lleem a la Barbe" & his wife[876].  A charter dated 14 Jan 1155 refers to "Barisanus frater Hugonis [de Hybelino] et quedam soror sua Theophanno" in relation to a donation by "Amalricus…comes Ascalonis" to the church of the Holy S
2 CONC epulchre, Jerusalem[877].  "Amalricus…comes Ascalonis" confirmed a donation to the church of the Holy Sepulchre, Jerusalem by "Hugonis de Hybelino et fratrum suorum Balduini et Barisani et Hermengardis sororis sue matrisque sue Al
2 CONC ois…" by charter dated 1158[878].  "Hugo dominus de Hibelini" confirmed that "dominus Rainerius bone memorie avunculus meus" had donated land "in territorio Ramatensi" to St Lazarus of Jerusalem, and now redonated the land as well
2 CONC  as land which "quam habuerunt de domina Eva", with the consent of "Agnetis comitisse uxoris mee, et domini Balduini et domini Barisani fratrum meorum", by charter dated 1169[879].  William of Tyre names him as the brother of Baud
2 CONC ouin Lord of Rama when recording his marriage[880].  Lord of Nablus [1177], by right of his wife.  He succeeded his brother in [1186/88] as Lord of Rama and Mirabel, but these territories, as well as the castle of Ibelin, were con
2 CONC quered in 1187 by Saladin after the battle of Hattin[881].  He went to Jerusalem from Tyre and made preparations to secure it against Saladin's attack but the city fell 2 Oct 1187[882].  Saladin installed him as Lord of Caymont an
2 CONC d Carmel[883].  He was a strong supporter of Corrado di Monferrato against Guy de Lusignan, and a leading proponent of Corrado's marriage to Isabelle of Jerusalem[884].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [1177] ) as her second husband, MARIA Komnene, widow of AMAURY I King of Jerusalem, daughter of IOANNES Komnenos protosébastos & his wife --- Taronitissa (1154-before Oct 1217).  She was given Nablus as her dower by her 
2 CONC first husband[885].  Her second marriage, around the same time as the marriage of Sibylle of Jerusalem with Guglielmo di Monferrato (Oct 1176), is recorded by William of Tyre[886].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines reco
2 CONC rds that "relictam regis Almarici…que fuit de Grecia" married "Bethuliani de Guibelin"[887].  The Lignages d'Outremer name "la reyne Marie…niece de l'empereur Manuel" as wife of "Belleem de Ybelin"[888].  "Hugo…rex Cipri" confirme
2 CONC d the grant to the church of Nicosia by "Philippus de Ybellino" for the soul of "domine Marie regine, matris sue" by charter dated Oct 1217[889].  
2 CONT
2 CONT  Balian of Ibelin & his wife had five children 
2 CONT (as the castle of Ibelin was lost to the family in 1187, the descendants of Balian of Ibelin are referred to as "Ibelin" rather than "of Ibelin".):
