1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anna_Komnene_Doukaina
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Anna Komnene Doukaina''' (died 4 January 1286), known in French as '''Agnes''', was princess-consort of the Principality of Achaea in 1258–1278 and regent between 1259–1262, during the captivity of her husband, Prince William I
2 CONC I of Villehardouin, by the Byzantine emperor Michael VIII Palaiologos. After William II's death in 1278, she re-married to the powerful baron Nicholas II of Saint Omer.
2 CONT
2 CONT   Life
2 CONT Anna was a daughter of the ruler of Epirus, Michael II Komnenos Doukas (r. 1230–1268), and his wife, Theodora.
2 CONT
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anna_Komnene_Doukaina#Marriage_to_William_II_of_Villehardouin Marriage to William II of Villehardouin]
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anna_Komnene_Doukaina#Death_of_William_II_and_second_marriage Death of William II and second marriag]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ALBANIA.htm#AnnaKomnenodukainadied1286
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.         '''ANNA KomnenoDoukaina''' (-4 Jan 1286).  Georgius Akropolites records the marriage of "Michaelis…filia sua Anna" and "Achaiæ principe"[123].  Georgius Phrantzes names "Manfredum Siculorum rege et principem Peloponnesi
2 CONC  et Achaiæ" as the two sons-in-law of "Aetolorum et Epirotarum despota Michaele"[124].  The Livre de la Conqueste de la Morée records the marriage of “le prince Guillerme” and “la suer dou despot”[125].  The Istoria of Marino Sanu
2 CONC do Torsello records that "il principe Guglielmo" married "Nicephoro…sorella" and that her dowry was "il castello della Liconia"[126].  She adopted the name '''AGNES'''.  After her first husband died, she received the castles of Ka
2 CONC lamata and Khlemutsi for life[127].  The Livre de la Conqueste de la Morée records that, after the death of Prince Guillaume, “la princesses a feme…suer…de Quir Niccifore” married “le baron monseignor Nicole de Saint Omer le veill
2 CONC art, li sires de la moitié d’Estives”[128].  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis records that "Nicolaum", son of "Bilas", married "Achayæ principissam"[129].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ( [1258] ) as his third wife, GUILLAUME II de Villehardouin Prince of Achaia, son of GEOFFROY I Prince of Achaia & his wife [Elisabeth de Chappes] (Kalamata Castle after [1208]-Kalamata Castle 1 May 1278, bur Andra
