2 CONT 2.         IOANNES Komnenos Angelos (-1259).  His parentage is not known.  Doux of Thrakesion 1235-[1236/37].  Megas primikerios 1255.  Protostrator of the west 1255/59.  He became a monk as KALLINIKOS.  m ---.  The name of Ioanne
2 CONC s's wife is not known.  She may have been EVDOKIA, assuming that then undated seal, dated to the 13th century, records “Eudoxias Evdokian skepois me [ten] sen oiketen sebastokratorisan ek basi[leon] klad[ov]”[754], refers to her d
2 CONC aughter as suggested below.  Ioannes Angelos & his wife had two children:
2 CONT *a)         [GEORGIOS] Komnenos Angelos.  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Megas primikerios 1259.  1262. 
2 CONT *b)         '''EVDOKIA Angelina ([1222]-[1253])'''.  Georgius Akropolites names "Eudocia Angeli Ioannis filia" as widow of "sebastocratoris filius Ioannes" recording that she died around the time of her daughter's marriage, dated 
2 CONC to the early 1250s from the context of the passage[755].  [An undated seal, dated to the 13th century, records “Eudoxias Evdokian skepois me [ten] sen oiketen sebastokratorisan ek basi[leon] klad[ov]”[756].  It is possible that th
2 CONC is seal refers to the wife of Ioannes Doukas Batatzes as no other Evdokia has been identified whose husband bore the title sebastokrator.]  m IOANNES Doukas Batatzes, son of ISAAKIOS Doukas Batatzes, sébastokrator, pansébastos séb
2 CONC astos & his wife --- (-[1240]). 
