2 TITL https://bg.wikipedia.org/wiki/Иван_Асен_II
1 NOTE Ivan Asen II, known as The Great, succeeded his cousin Boril/Boris to the throne of Bulgaria.    Ivan Asen II died during the Tatar invasion in the Balkans, and the Bulgars had to pay an annual tribute to the Tater ruler. Ivan or 
2 CONC John Asen II was succeeded by his eldest son Kalman I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ivan Asen II The Great succeeded Boril/Boris to rule the Second Kingdom of Bulgaria in 1218.  Ivan Asen was called the greatest ruler of that era in Bulgaria, and Bulgaria reached a new zenith. He shared authoority with the nobili
2 CONC ty and monasteries, whose lands were tilled by free or dependent peasants.  Domestic and foreign trade increased, especially with Genoa and Venice. the arts, archictecture, religious literature all flourish under the Tsar Ivan Ase
2 CONC n II.  His frontiers expanded from Belgrade to the Epirus, and from the Black Sea to the Adriatic Sea.  He defeated Theodore Angelus, ruler of Epirus and Salonika.  And added Macedonia and part of Albania to his holdings.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1230 the forces of Ivan Asen II defeated Theodore Angelus, ruler of Epirus and Salonika, whose territory was added to that of Bulgaria. Weakened by defeat, Theodore Angelus in Servia was forced to transfer his royal perogatives
2 CONC  in Serbia to Vladislav, a brother in law of Ivan Asen II.
