1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Proposed as father of https://www.geni.com/people/Angelina-of-Greece/6000000006789778018
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jovan Uroš Nemanjić''' (Serbian: Јован Урош Немањић / Jovan Uroš Nemanjić) or John Ouresis Doukas Palaiologos or Joasaph of Meteora (Greek: Ιωάννης Ούρεσης Δούκας Παλαιολόγος, Iōannēs Ouresēs Doúkas Palaiologos), was the ruler 
2 CONC of Thessaly from c. 1370 to c. 1373, retiring as a monk for the next half century thereafter. He died in 1422.[1][2]
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Uros
2 CONT
2 CONT John Uroš was the son of Emperor Simeon Uroš Palaiologos by Thomais Orsini. He was born in 1350 and died in 1422.[3]His maternal grandparents were John II Orsini and Anna Palaiologina.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Uroš married a daughter of Radoslav Hlapen, a Serbian lord in Macedonia. According to the manuscript Dell'Imperadori Constantinopolitani, preserved in the papers of Angelo Masarelli, the father of John's wife was "lord of Dri
2 CONC ma" ("l Signor Drimi"). 
2 CONT
2 CONT John had five children:[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Constantine (Konstantin)
2 CONT # Michael (Mihajlo)
2 CONT # Demetrios (Dimitrije)
2 CONT # Helena (Jelena) Ouresina Palaiologina, who married Theodore Kantakouzenos, with whom she had Irene Kantakouzene
2 CONT # Asanina
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radoslav_Hlapen He married Irina (Irene), the widow of caesar Preljub. They had the following issue:  ... Unnamed, married John Uroš[1]
2 CONT *1.  Evans, Charles F. H. (1989). Studies in Genealogy and Family History in Tribute to Charles Evans on the Occasion of His Eightieth Birthday. Association for the Promotion of Scholarship in Genealogy. [https://books.google.com/
2 CONC books?id=pK1pAAAAMAAJ GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Uroš
2 CONT *4.  the Masarelli manuscript, 'Dell'Imperadori Constantinopolitani', from papers of 'Massarellus', Angelo Massarelli (1510-1566), held now in the Vatican Library, reports: "Cesare Urione de Phersali hebbe dui figlioli, Demetrio e
2 CONC t Giovani, il quale prese per moglia da figlia del S'or Drimi, hebbe cinque figlioli, cioe Helena, Constantino, Michel, Asanina, Demetrio. Helena fu maritata in Theodoro Catacusino."
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Kantakouzenos Theodore's wife was Helena Ouresina Doukaina, a daughter of John Uroš, ruler of Thessaly.[10] 
2 CONT *  10.  Williams, Kelsey Jackson (2006). "A Genealogy of the Grand Komnenoi of Trebizond" (PDF). Foundations. 2 (3): 171–89. Archived (PDF) from the original on 8 June 2019. [https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/31300217.pdf PDF] page 
2 CONC 12:
2 CONT ** 16.  Nicol (1968, pp.176-192) published an accurate account of Theodoros’ children but mistakenly attributed them to the sebastokrator Demetrios Kantakouzenos (d.c.1384), an error which Hunger noted in his edition of Chortasmen
2 CONC os and which Nicol corrected in his addenda (1973, pp.312-313). Brook (1989, pp.6-8) establishes that Theodoros’ wife, and consequently '''Theodora’s mother, was Helena Uroš Doukaina, daughter of Ioannes Uroš Doukas, Emperor in Th
2 CONC essaly''', c.1371-1372, and grandson of Stefan Uroš III Dečanski, King of Serbia.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT At present it has been proposed that  https://www.geni.com/people/Angelina-de-Grecia/6000000006789778018  was a his daughter. This affiliation would likely be the one that explains her being known in Spain under the surname de Gre
2 CONC cia (of or from Greece). In the case of the name Angelina, by which she was known in Spain, a Byzantine affiliation has been noted. ''[2]''
2 CONT
2 CONT  [2]^ At present, his house houses the National Distance Education University in Segovia.
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angelina_of_Greece#cite_note-3 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT    The sepulchral inscription was: 
2 CONT
2 CONT AQUI YACE DOÑA [https://www.geni.com/people/Angelina-of-Greece/6000000006789778018 ANGELINA DE GRECIA], HIJA DEL CONDE '''JUAN''', NIETA DEL REY DE UNGRÍA, MUGER DE DIEGO GONZÁLEZ DE CONTRERAS, REGIDOR DESTA CIUDAD
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angelina_de_Grecia#cite_note-1
2 CONT
