2 CONT 3.         BALŠA [II] Balšić (-killed in battle near Berat 18 Sep 1385).  He succeeded his father jointly with his brothers.  He obtained Valona, Berat, Himara and Kanina as dowry on his marriage[196].  “Georgius Balšić…fratrem Ba
2 CONC lša et Georgium juniorem” swore peace to Ragusa by charter dated 30 Nov 1373[197].  He succeeded as Lord of Zeta, in the territories of his older brother Djuradj, on the latter's death in 1379, ignoring the rights of his nephew Ko
2 CONC nstantini.  He captured Durazzo from Karlo Thopia in 1385, calling himself Duke of Durazzo in Apr 1385[198].  He was killed fighting the Turks.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (1372) KOMINIA of Bulgaria, daughter of IVAN Asen Komnenos, despot, Lord of Valona, Kanina and Berat & his second wife Anna Palaiologina Angelina of Epirus (-[5 Oct 1395/Sep 1396]).  She succeeded her husband as Lady of Va
2 CONC lona, Kanina, Berat and Himara.  Regent 1385/95.  Vassal of Venice 1389/90 for the islands of Sasene and Torre di Pirgo.  She became a nun as XENIA[199].  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Balša [II] & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         RUDJINA (-after 1421).  Kraljica.  Lady of Valona 1396, until 1417.  Lady of Berat, Cimera and Pirgi, until 1420.  '''m''' (Mar 1391) MRKŠE Žarković, son of ŽARKO & his wife --- (-Oct 1414).  Lord of Valona 1396. 
