1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Hafize Hafsa Sultan''' [1] (Ottoman Turkish: حفصة سلطان, "the keeper one" and "young lioness"; c. 1492 or before - 10 July 1538) was an Ottoman princess, daughter of Selim I and, presumably, of his favorite Hafs
2 CONC a Hatun. She was therefore the sister or at least half-sister of Suleiman the Magnificent.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hafize_Sultan En]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hafize_Sultan#Origins Origins]===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hafize_Sultan#Marriage Marriage]===
2 CONT
2 CONT Hafize Sultan married twice:
2 CONT
2 CONT * She married for the first time in 1511. Her first husband was Grand Vizier Dukaginzade Ahmed Paşa, executed in 1515.
2 CONT * Her second husband, married in 1522, was Boşnak Mustafa Paşah. From this marriage she had her only child, a son, Sultanzade Kara Osman Şah Paşah.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note:''' At wikipiedia source '''written wrong''' that she was married to Boşnak Mustafa Paşah (Mustafa paša Bošnjak see: [https://digitalna.nsk.hr/?pr=iiif.v.a&id=601954&vwopt=%7B%22pages%22%3A%5B65%5D%2C%22pan%22%3A%7B%22x%22
2 CONC %3A0.513%2C%22y%22%3A0.919%7D%2C%22view%22%3A%22thumbnails%22%2C%22zoom%22%3A1.088%7D&fbclid=IwAR0wERd174xYIntcrP_Ac0VTyIM8K2l8NUdT_OPUqA6IDqpqCCjh8CnDLn8_aem_ATXm2UjevuJbpXKjkQ6htAUvo9X3V5OPvv7V9MmMmQJZeWhdFbldWgC17gytlBkeqFTdcOB
2 CONC TgKXH9ai9ZFbSVry2  Znameniti Hrvati Bošnjaci i Hercegovci u Turskoj Carevini / Safvet-beg Bašagić. str. 55], also not for https://www.geni.com/people/%C3%87oban-Mustafa-Pasha/6000000028526229008 (Mustafa paša Čoban) see: [https://
2 CONC digitalna.nsk.hr/?pr=iiif.v.a&id=601954&vwopt=%7B%22pages%22%3A%5B65%5D%2C%22pan%22%3A%7B%22x%22%3A0.513%2C%22y%22%3A0.919%7D%2C%22view%22%3A%22thumbnails%22%2C%22zoom%22%3A1.088%7D&fbclid=IwAR0wERd174xYIntcrP_Ac0VTyIM8K2l8NUdT_OP
2 CONC UqA6IDqpqCCjh8CnDLn8_aem_ATXm2UjevuJbpXKjkQ6htAUvo9X3V5OPvv7V9MmMmQJZeWhdFbldWgC17gytlBkeqFTdcOBTgKXH9ai9ZFbSVry2  Znameniti Hrvati Bošnjaci i Hercegovci u Turskoj Carevini / Safvet-beg Bašagić. str. 55], also https://www.geni.com
2 CONC /people/%C3%87oban-Mustafa-Pasha/6000000028526229008 was not born in Turkey, he was born in Bosnia and was not died in 1529, he was died in 1528. She was only married to [https://www.geni.com/people/Dukaginzade-Ahmed-Pasha/6000000
2 CONC 205076373823  Dukaginzade Ahmed Pasha ] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Mustafa-pa%C5%A1a-Skenderpa%C5%A1i%C4%87-Juri%C5%A1evi%C4%87/6000000205075888844 Mustafa-paša Skenderpašić Jurišević], who both were sons-in-law of Sultan [h
2 CONC ttps://www.geni.com/people/Selim-I-of-the-Ottoman-Empire/6000000008518541049 Selim I].
2 CONT
