1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Frederick I, Elector of Saxony=
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick I, the Belligerent = Frederick IV, Margrave of Meissen, Landgrave of Thuringia and Elector of Saxony (Frederick the Belligerent (the Warlike) (11 April 1370 – 4 January 1428) was Markgraf of Meißen, Landgraf of Thuringia
2 CONC  and Elector of Saxony from 1381 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the eldest son of Frederick III, Landgrave of Thuringia and Katharina von Henneberg. After the death of his uncle William II, Margrave of Meissen in 1407, he governed the Margraviate of Meissen together with his brother Wil
2 CONC liam III as well as with his cousin Frederick (son of Balthasar). After secession in 1410 and 1415 he received the Mark Meissen to autocracy.
2 CONT
