2 CONT
2 CONT D.      DUKES of ATHENS (ACCIAIUOLI)
2 CONT
2 CONT The Acciaiuoli family originated in Brescia, and moved to Florence in [1160] where they established a steelworks from which their name derives.  Later enterprising biographers provided them with a fabricated pedigree showing their
2 CONC  alleged descent from Angelo, supposed brother of Emperor Justin II.  The steelworkers made money, lent it out at interest and became bankers[316].  The family operated a flourishing bank which lent funds to the kings of England, 
2 CONC the Knights of St John of Jerusalem, the Pope and the Angevin kings of Sicily[317].    
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         NICOLÒ Acciaiuoli .  “Nicolaus de Acciaiolis de Florentia, miles, Corynthi dominus, Melfie et palatinus comes, ac magnus senescalcus regni Sicilie” names “dominus Nicolaus avus suus” in his testament dated 30 Sep 1358[3
2 CONC 18].  m ---.  The name of Nicolò´s wife is not known.  Nicolò & his wife had one child:  
2 CONT *a)         --- Acciaiuoli .  He settled in Naples where he was appointed chamberlain and privy councillor by King Robert I[319].  m ---.  The name of his wife is not known.  He & his wife had three children:  
2 CONT **i) ...
2 CONT **ii)         LAPA Acciaiuoli .  “Nicolaus de Acciaiolis de Florentia, miles, Corynthi dominus, Melfie et palatinus comes, ac magnus senescalcus regni Sicilie” names “domine Lape de Accajolis sorori sue” and “Franciscus et Esau na
2 CONC ti…dicte domine Lape” under his testament dated 30 Sep 1358[321].  m MANENTE Buondelmonti, son of ---.  Manente & his wife had three children:  
2 CONT ***(a)       FRANCESCO Buondelmonti .  “Nicolaus de Acciaiolis de Florentia, miles, Corynthi dominus, Melfie et palatinus comes, ac magnus senescalcus regni Sicilie” names “domine Lape de Accajolis sorori sue” and “Franciscus et E
2 CONC sau nati…dicte domine Lape” under his testament dated 30 Sep 1358[322].  
2 CONT ***(b)       ESAU Buondelmonti .  “Nicolaus de Acciaiolis de Florentia, miles, Corynthi dominus, Melfie et palatinus comes, ac magnus senescalcus regni Sicilie” names “domine Lape de Accajolis sorori sue” and “Franciscus et Esau n
2 CONC ati…dicte domine Lape” under his testament dated 30 Sep 1358[323].  
2 CONT ***(c)       '''MADDALENA Buondelmonti (-after 11 Mar 1401)'''.  m (before autumn 1361) LEONARDO I Count of Kefalonia, son of GUGLIELMO Tocco Governor of Corfu & his [second] wife Margherita Orsini of Kefalonia (-[20 Mar 1375/25 A
2 CONC ug 1377]).  
2 CONT **iii)        ANDREA Acciaiuoli .  “Nicolaus de Acciaiolis de Florentia, miles, Corynthi dominus, Melfie et palatinus comes, ac magnus senescalcus regni Sicilie” names “domina Andrea, consors viri…domini Carlotti Artus comitis mon
2 CONC tis Odorisii, soror sua” under his testament dated 30 Sep 1358[324].  m CARLO Artus Conte di Monte Odorisio, son of ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=207888471-3-509046&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-59e761a071fb47cbd27c5357b202ef7d&mrid=1e676d4bc8e8415745b2e6eb819a1238 My
2 CONC Heritage Match] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 29 2014, 10:59:51 UTC''
