1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Yuri (George) Svyatoslavich (died September 14, 1407) was the last Grand Duke of Smolensk (1386-1392, 1401-1404), with whom the history of Smolensk statehood ended. The second son and successor of Svyatoslav Ivanovich.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to '''Alyona''', daughter of Oleg Ivanovich, Grand Duke of Ryazan[8], taken prisoner after the capture of Smolensk. From this marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Fyodor
2 CONT # Anastasia, husband - Yuri Dmitrievich
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Yury had two daughters: Anastasia, wife of Grand Duke Švitrigaila of Lithuania, and Elena, wife of Yury of Zvenigorod (and mother of the famous Dmitry Shemyaka). He also had a son (Fyodor) who joined the Order of Saint John of Jer
2 CONC usalem in 1412.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT #https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yury_of_Smolensk
2 CONT # Brockhaus and Efron Encyclopedic Dictionary (in Russian). 1906
2 CONT #Kogan V. M. History of the Rurikovich House. - S. 200
