1 NOTE Also grand duke of Lithuania, third ruler of the Jagiellon dynasty.  
2 CONT Casimir succeeded his brother Wladyslaw III. Unpopular in Poland, where he 
2 CONT was thought to be too favorable to Lithuanians, he courted the support of 
2 CONT the lower nobility by giving them the right to refuse taxation. He fought 
2 CONT a long war against the Teutonic Knights, winning a great victory over them 
2 CONT at Zarnowiec (Puck) in 1462. Four years later, by the second treaty of 
2 CONT Torun (Thorn), he regained from the knights the extensive territory on the 
2 CONT Baltic coast that became known as West Prussia; the order also 
2 CONT acknowledged him as its overlord in East Prussia. From 1485 to 1489 
2 CONT Casimir aided his vassal, Prince Stephen of Moldavia, in his struggle 
2 CONT against the Ottoman Turks. Casimir's son Wladyslaw was elected king of 
2 CONT Bohemia in 1471 and of Hungary in 1490.
