1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Chronology of life events:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1357 Birth of Anastasia of Ryazan
2 CONT
2 CONT c. 1376 Age 19:  Marriage of duke Dmitry Drutski and Anastasia of Ryazan	
2 CONT
2 CONT c. 1377 Age 20: Birth of duke Andrey Drutski
2 CONT
2 CONT c. 1379 Age 22: Birth of duke Vasily Drutski
2 CONT
2 CONT 1384 Age 25: Anastasia of Ryazan	was widowed: death of duke Dmitry Drutski
2 CONT
2 CONT c. 1385 Age 26:   Marriage of Kaributas-Dmitry and Anastasia of Ryazan	
2 CONT
2 CONT c. 1386 Age: 27 Birth of prince Sigismund Korybut	
2 CONT
2 CONT c. 1386 Age: 27 Birth of Fedor Korybut, prince of Nesvizh and Podole	
2 CONT
2 CONT c. 1386 Age: 27 Birth of princess Helena Korybut Poland 
2 CONT
2 CONT c. 1386 Age: 27 Birth of princess Anastasia Korybut Новгород-Северсий, Северское Княжество 
2 CONT
2 CONT c. 1386 Age: 27 Birth of prince Andrew ??? Korybut	
2 CONT
2 CONT 1390 Age: 33 Birth of prince Ivan Korybut	
2 CONT
2 CONT 1397 Age: 40 Birth of princess Maria Korybut Новгород-Северский, Северское Удельное Княжество 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1399 Age: 42 Death of Anastasia of Ryazan 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------- 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Anastasia Olgovna of Ryazan''' (? - d. after 1399) - Grand Duchess of Ryazan, the eldest daughter of Oleg Ivanovich, Grand Duke of Ryazan, from her first marriage. Presumably the grandmother of the Queen of Poland Sophia, the f
2 CONC ourth wife of Jagiello. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was probably born between 1357 and 1363 in Ryazan. There is little information about Anastasia Olgovna. It is known that she was married twice: first with Dmitry Vasilyevich, the unmanageable prince of Drutsk, vassal of the Gr
2 CONC and Duke of Lithuania Algirdas; then with Dmitry (before baptismal known as Kaributas / Korybut) Olgerdovich, the prince of Seversk, son of Algirdas. In other sources, Prince Dmitry Semenovich Drutsky, a cousin of Dmitry Vasilyevi
2 CONC ch, is named Anastasia's first husband. Anastasia Olgovna is mentioned on August 12, 1399; on this day, her eldest son Andrey died in the battle on the Vorskla River. Her further fate is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anastasia entered into her first marriage around 1376, Prince Dmitry Drutsky died in 1384. In this marriage she gave birth to two sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Andrey Dmitriyevich (died August 12, 1399), killed in the battle with Tokhtamysh on the Vorskla River.
2 CONT * Vasily Dmitriyevich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably Anastasia from her first marriage had a daughter:
2 CONT * Alexandra Dmitriyevna (1380? -1426), mother of the Queen of Poland Sophia Golshanska, the progenitor of the Jagiellonian dynasty. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Anastasia Olgovna entered into a second marriage with Dmitry Olgerdovich (Algirdas' son) in 1386/1388. In this marriage Anastasia had the following children:
2 CONT * Ivan Korybut (d. after 1431), was mentioned only once, in 1431. A number of sources believe that the widow of Ivan Korybut married Prince Boris Ivanovich Glinsky.
2 CONT * Sigismund Korybut (c. 1395-1435), was brought up at the royal court of his uncle Jagiello (King Jogaila). Participated in the Battle of Grunwald. Later he showed himself as a commander, participated in the Hussite wars, was the 
2 CONC governor of the Bohemian kingdom. He died in the battle of Vilkomir in 1435.
2 CONT * Fedor (Fyodor, Teodore) Korybut (c. 1390-1442), mentioned since 1422. He participated in the Vilkomir battle, in which he was captured. The princes Zbarazhsky and Vishnevetsky (who used the coat of arms "Korybut") considered the
2 CONC mselves the descendants of Fedor, and therefore Korybut descendants, but no information about the sons of Fedor has survived.
2 CONT * Maria Korybut (Dmitriyevna) - married to Prince Fyodor Lvovich Vorotynsky.
2 CONT * Elena (Yelena) Korybut (d. after 1449) - from 1407 the wife of Jan II Zhelezny (about 1365-1424), Prince of Ratiborsk-Krnovsky.
2 CONT * Anastasia Korybut (Dmitriyevna) - the second wife of Vasily Mikhailovich (1364-1426), Prince of Kashin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Literature''' 
2 CONT * Kogan V.M., Dombrovsky-Shalagin V.I. Prince Rurik and his descendants: Historical and genealogical code. - SPb .: "Parity", 2004. - 688 p. - 3000 copies. - ISBN 5-93437-149-5.
2 CONT * A.A. Kosiński, A Heraldic Guide, Volume 1. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes''' 
2 CONT * Lavrent'ev A.V. After the Battle of Kulikovo. Essays on the history of the Oka-Don region in the last quarter of the 14th - first quarter of the 16th centuries. - Quadriga, 2012 .-- 254 p.
2 CONT * LITHUANIA. fmg.ac. Retrieved 13 August 2017.
2 CONT * RUSSIA RURIKID. fmg.ac. Retrieved 13 August 2017.
2 CONT * Drutsk (princes).
2 CONT * V. Nasevich Karybutavichy // Slow Princes of Lithuania. Entsyklapedyya at 3 vol. - Minsk: BelEn, 2005. - Vol. 2: Kadetskі corps - Yatskevich. - S. 64-65. - 788 p. - ISBN 985-11-0378-0.
2 CONT * Genealogy of the princes Glinsky. Russian-Lithuanian nobility of the 15th – 17th centuries. 
