2 CONT ==Primary Sources
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000073398223239& Inquisitions Post Mortem] for Robert Holand, knight, Writ, 20 March, 47 Edward III [1373]. <br>
2 CONT He died on 16 March [1373]. Maud, aged 17 years and more, wife of John Lovel, knight, and daughter of Robert son of the deceased, was his next heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Robert Holand, 2nd Baron Holand''', was born about 1312 in Upholland, Lancaster, England and died 26 December 1360 in .  He married Margaret Hetton in 1337, born 1314 in Buthel, Lancashire, England, a daughter of Alan Hetto
2 CONC n, (born 1288).  The couple had two daughters, Jane  Holand born in 1338 and died 1372 in Lancaster, England. and Margaret Holand (1340-1375) 
2 CONT *Jane Holand born about 1335 in Lancaster, England.  She married William Molyneux in 1359.  They had two sons, Richard Molyneux, born about 1360 in Sefton, Lancashire, England and Thomas Molyneux.
2 CONT www.celtic-casimir.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert IV DE HOLAND 2nd Baron Holand
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: Abt 1312, Thorpe Waterville, Thrapston, Northamptonshire, England   
2 CONT Died: 16 Mar 1372-1373, Hawes, Brackley, Northamptonshire, England   
2 CONT Buried: St James Chapel, Brackley, Northamptonshire, England  
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: Robert de Holand, 2nd Lord (Baron) Holand; b. c 1312; knighted by 1336, served in Hundred Years War (thought to have been at Crecy); m. Elizabeth, and d. 16 March 1372/3. [Burke's Peerage]    BARONY OF HOLAND (II)  
2 CONC ROBERT (DE HOLAND), LORD HOLAND, son and heir, was under age at his father's death, being then aged 16. His marriage was quickly granted to his mother, who offered 500 marks. He received the custody of Chelveston, Northants, in 13
2 CONC 33 in reward for his services in the war with Scotland. He proved his age and had livery of his lands in 1335, and next year is described as a knight. He fought in the wars with France, and, being in the retinue of the Earl of War
2 CONC wick in April 1346, was probably present at Crécy, 26 August 1346, and in Nov. 1347 he is stated to have served in the King's retinue. In March 1347 he assisted Sir John de Dalton to abduct Margery de la Beche from Beaumes Manor, 
2 CONC near Reading. In 1355 he again went overseas. He was summoned to a Council 25 February 1341/2, and to Parliament from 1 June 1363 till his death. He appears to have resided chiefly in Northants, where he was appointed on various C
2 CONC ommissions judicial and military, and in 1360 was a guardian of Garendon Abbey. He added to the endowment of Upholland Priory in 1367.  He married Elizabeth, who appears to have predcceased him. He died 16 March 1372/3, at Halse o
2 CONC r Hawes, Brackley, and was buried in St. James's Chapel, Brackley. [Complete Peerage VI:531, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]  Note: Elizabeth has been tentatively identified --see notes under her.   Sir Robert Holand, 2nd baron, s
2 CONC ummoned to parliament from 25 February, 1342, to 6 October, 1372. This nobleman was engaged for several years in the French wars of King Edward III, part of the time under Thomas de Beauchamp, Earl of Warwick, and the remainder in
2 CONC  the retinue of his brother, Thomas Holland. His lordship d. in 1373, leaving his grand-dau (dau. and heir of his eldest son Robert, who had predeceased him), Maud Holland, then seventeen years of age, his sole heir, who m. John L
2 CONC ovel, 5th Lord Lovel, of Tichmersh, and carried the Barony of Holland into that family. [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant and Extinct Peerages, Burke's Peerage, Ltd., London, 1883, p. 279, Holand, Barons Holand]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information: Robert married Elizabeth D' AVESNES of Hainault, daughter of Willem III D' AVESNES Comte de Hainault and Trude VAN DER POELE. (Elizabeth D' AVESNES of Hainault was born about 1315 in Mons, Hainault, Belgium a
2 CONC nd died before 16 Mar 1372-1373.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT www.wikipedia.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert de Holand (born c.1311–12 [aged 16 in 1328, aged 30 and more in 1349] – died 16 March 1372/3), 2nd Baron Holand. He married before 25 June 1343 (date of fine) Elizabeth _____.
2 CONT
2 CONT About Sir Robert Holland, Lord of Enreston
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert Holand, 2nd Baron Holand, was born about 1312 in Upholland, Lancaster, England and died 26 December 1360 in. He married Margaret Hetton in 1337, born 1314 in Buthel, Lancashire, England, a daughter of Alan Hetton, (born
2 CONC  1288). The couple had two daughters, Jane Holand born in 1338 and died 1372 in Lancaster, England. and Margaret Holand (1340-1375) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Holand born about 1335 in Lancaster, England. She married William Molyneux in 1359. They had two sons, Richard Molyneux, born about 1360 in Sefton, Lancashire, England and Thomas Molyneux.
2 CONT
2 CONT www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert de Holand 
2 CONT BIRTH 1312
2 CONT England
2 CONT DEATH 16 Mar 1373 (aged 60–61)
2 CONT Brackley, South Northamptonshire Borough, Northamptonshire, England
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT St. Peter's Churchyard
2 CONT Brackley, South Northamptonshire Borough, Northamptonshire, England
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID 102806229
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight of Thorpe Waterville, Northamptonshire, of Broughton Parva in Bierton, Buckinghamshire, of Upholland and Orrell in Wigan, Hale in Childwall, Haydock in Winwick, Nether Kellet and Samlesbury, Lancashire. Of Yoxall, Staffords
2 CONC hire. Guardian of Garendon Abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son and Heir of Robert de Holand and Maud la Zouche. Husband of Elizabeth, thought to be an illegitiamte daughter of Guillame III, le Bon, Count of Hainhault (Holland). They had four sons and one possible daughter; Robert, Thomas,
2 CONC  Gilbert, a cleric, Sir John and Margaret.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a reward for his services in Scotland, Robert was awarded Chelveston, Northamptonshire in 1333. In 1340 he received a lease for life from his brother, Thomas de Hoaldn, the manor of Horden, Durham. He accompanied Thomas de Beau
2 CONC champ in the wars of France, the King in 1347, and assisted Sir John Dalton in the abduction of a wealthy widow, Margery de la Beche from her home at Beaumes at Reading, Berkshire. Robert was summoned to Parliament from 1363 to hi
2 CONC s death in 1373.
2 CONT
