1 NAME John /Holand/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Holand
2 _MARNM Holand
2 NICK Holland
2 NICK de Holand
1 NAME John Holand, Knt, of Thorpe Waterville & Achurch
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1348
2 ADDR
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1409
1 OCCU Knt., of Thorpe Waterville and Achurch (both in Thorpe Achurch), Chelveston and Caldecote, Northamptonshire, Dalbury Lees, Derbyshire, and Breightme (in Bolton-le-Moors), Golborne, Haydock (in Winwick), Over Darwen, and Torrisholm
2 CONC e, Lancashire
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Holand-62
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. II, p. 542. ROYAL ANCESTRY by Douglas Richardson Vol. III, page 297 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Robert de Holand, Knt., by Elizabeth _______ .
2 CONT
2 CONT i. ROBERT DE HOLAND 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. '''JOHN HOLAND''', Knt., younger son but heir male, born about 1347-9. He married (1st) by marriage contract dated 7 Sept 1372 ELIZABETH GREENE. They had no issue. He married (2nd) MARGARET ____ . They had one son, John, Knt.,
2 CONC  and two daughters, Elizabeth and Margaret. SIR JOHN HOLAND was living in 1409. He died sometime before 1417.
2 CONT
2 CONT # ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 1.4 Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 5 vols., ed. Kimball G. Everingham, (Salt Lake City, Utah: the author, 2013), Volume III, pp 296-8 HOLAND #12 Robert de Holand,
2 CONC  Knt.
2 CONT # Where John was born is not noted by Richardson. His father died in Northamptonshire in 1372. I used Lancashire for the datafield because, in 1343, his parents "settled the manor of Nether Kellet, Lancashire, the balliwick of the
2 CONC  wapentake of Lonsdale, and the bailiwicks of Cartmel and Fourneys, which Edmund de Neville, Knt. held for life, on themselves for life following the said Edmund's death, with reversion to Thomas, son of the said Robert de Holand.
2 CONC " (#Richardson)
2 CONT # VCH Northampton 3 (1930): 136-137 (confuses this John Holand and his son, Sir John Holand, with their cousins, also John Holand, father and son, who were Earls of Huntingdon and Dukes of Exeter); 4 (1937): 8 (correctly identifie
2 CONC s John Holand as heir male to his father, Robert Holand, 2nd Lord Holand).
2 CONT # Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, Royal Ancestry series, 2nd edition, 4 vols., ed. Kimball G. Everingham (Salt Lake City, Utah: the author, 2011)
2 CONT *See also: Sir John Holand, "Our Royal, Titled, Noble, and Commoner Ancestors and Cousins" (website, compiled by Mr. Marlyn Lewis, Portland, OR; accessed November 20, 2015)
2 CONT * George Baker's History of Northampton, Vol I, Page 32 <[https://archive.org/details/HistoryAndAntiquitiesOfTheCountyOfNorthamptonBakerVol1/page/n33/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org]>
