1 NOTE Edward assumed effective power in 1330 after imprisoning his mother and executing her lover, Roger I de Mortimer, who had murdered his father. Thereafter his reign was dominated by military adventures. His victory in Scotland, esp
2 CONC ecially at Haildon Hill in 1333, encouraged him to plan (1363) the union of England and Scotland. Through his mother, he claimed the French throne, thus starting (1337) the Hundred Years War. His son, John of Gaunt, dominated the 
2 CONC government during his last years. He died of a stroke.
