1 NOTE "OF WOODSTOCK"; DUKE OF GLOUCESTER; BEARER OF THE SWAN BADGE; KG; GUARDIAN OF
2 CONT THE KINGDOM; EARL OF BUCKINGHAM; INHERITED TITLES CONSTABLE OF ENGLAND AND EARL
2 CONT OF ESSEX FROM WIFE; MURDERED BY RIVAL CLAIMANT TO THE THRONE
1 NOTE DIED YOUNG
1 NOTE Thomas of Woodstock, first Duke of Gloucester (1355-97), seventh and youngest son of Edward III, distinguished himself by service at sea; having conspired against his nephew, Richard II, he was put to death at Calais by the king�s
2 CONC  order or connivance. [World Wide Illustrated Encyclopedia, 1935]
2 CONT
2 CONT Appointed Constable of England. He was murdered at Calais. {Burke�s Peerage} [GADD.GED]
1 NOTE Possibly murdered by Richard II or on his behalf
2 CONT 1st Duke of Glouchester (Jan 7 1355 - Sept 8/9 1397)
2 CONT 13th and youngest child of King Edward III of England and Queen Philppa of Hainault.
2 CONT Fifth of five sons to survive to adulthood.
2 CONT Earl of Essex, inherited from father-in-law, Humphrey de Bohun, 7th Earl of Hereford.
2 CONT Earl of Buckingham, age of 22, 1377
2 CONT Duke of Aumale in 1385
