2 TITL D. Pedro e Inês de Castro Casamento2 PT-TT-GAV-15-20-10_c0002.TIF
1 NOTE KNOWN AS "THE SEVERE"; KING OF PORTUGAL
1 NOTE Helped King Alfonso XI of Castile combat against Moroccan Caliphs in the reconquest of Algeciras in 1344. Called, El de Punyalet, The One of the Little Dagger, also known as El Ceremonioso.
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT Historia de los Pueblos de Espana, Volz, Los Antiguos Territorios de la Corona de Aragon, Ed. Argos Vergona, Barcelona, 1984
2 CONT Pedro's story as far as love is concerned is a sad one and very romantic.
2 CONT When he first met his beloved, Ines de Castro, they had an affair. Because of Pedro's love for Ines Pedro's father, Afonso IV ordered Ines' death after banishing her from the court. Pedro had been installing Ines' brothers and fam
2 CONC ily into important positions at court, Afonso didn't take to the idea too well because he didn't want anyone from Castile influencing or getting power in the Portuguese Court.
2 CONT Afonso IV sent three assasins to the Monastary of Santa Clara o Velho in Coimbra where she was essentially inprisoned to kill her; Pero Coelho, Alvaro Gonzalves and Diogo Lopes Pacheco.
2 CONT Pedro angered, rebelled against his father and civil war came to the land. Pedro gained the name, El Punyalet and El Justiciero by personally killing the three assassins. See Ines' scroll for more data
2 CONT Isabel I de Castile was the great, great, grandaughter of Pedro I and his mistress, teresa de Lourenzo..
