2 DATE BEF 1418
1 OCCU statesman, soldier and privateer, [milite, Hakem De Malte 1365]
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giacomo_de_Pellegrino - Viene da una nobile famiglia di Messina. In data sconosciuta, '''sposa Margherita d'Aragona (...-1418)''', - Avevano almeno 3 ragazze: 
2 CONT #Francia, 
2 CONT #Cesarea 
2 CONT #Eleonora.
2 CONT --------
2 CONT Taken from Maltese Notarial Acts:
2 CONT * Giacomo 'Milite' fils de Giovanni Capitan del Castello nel 1360
2 CONT * Giacomo 'Soldier' son of Giovanni and Capitan of Castello (possibly referring to Mdina) in 1360 
2 CONT
2 CONT G.F. Abela also confirms that Giacomo's father was Giovanni Pellegrino from Messina 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT "Giacomo de Pellegrino, a Messinese who had settled in Malta, and who from 1356 to 1372 holding various titles and administrative positions along with a lucrative cotton cloth warehouse along with a privateering business took over
2 CONC  the politics of the fiefdom. He was finally removed from power after an invasion of Malta from an allied force of Genoese and Sicilian navies and a 2-month siege of Mdina by both these forces and Maltese rebels from both peasants
2 CONC  and other noblemen. his power in local politics and administration made him many enemies on the islands and with the Sicilian claimants to the county, while his privateering business made him enemies in both Sicily and Genoa"
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [milite, Hakem De Malte 1365] 
