2 CONT One Ügyek; m.Emese, dau.of Pr Önedbelia of Dentümoger; they had a son: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Álmos, *820, +Transylvania ca 895, had a son: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Árpád, Prince of Hungary, +907; he settled in what is now Hungary in about 900, though they continued to ravage western Europe til their defeat by Emperor Otto I in 955. He had issue: 
2 CONT * ...
2 CONT *A5. Zaltas (Zoltán), Prince of Hungary (907-948)
2 CONT **B1. Taksony, Prince of Hungary (955-ca 972), *ca 905, +ca 972
2 CONT ***C1. Géza, Great Prince of Hungary (ca 972-997), *ca 945, +1.2.997; 1m: ca 967 Sarolta (repudiated shortly after 975, +after 988), dau.of Prince Gyula of Transylvania; 2m: ca 985 Adelajda (+after 997), widow of his brother Micha
2 CONC el
2 CONT ****D1. [1m.] Judith, +after 987; m.985 (div 987) King Boleslav I of Poland (*967 +17.6.1025)
2 CONT ****D2. [1m.] a daughter; m.shortly before 985 Sizzo, Count in Thuringia
2 CONT ****D3. [1m.] '''a daughter, +after 988'''; m.987 (he repudiated her 988) Gabriel-Radomir, Tsar of the Bulgarians
2 CONT ****D4. [1m.] Saint István I (Stephen I), Prince of Hungary (997-1000), in 1000 became King of Hungary (1000-38) and the first Hungarian ruler to become a Christian, cr 25.12.1000/1.1.1001, canonised 20.8.1083, *969/75, +15.8.1038
2 CONC , bur Székesfehérvár; m.996 Gisela of Bavaria (*985, +7.5.1065)
2 CONT ***** ...
2 CONT ****D5. [2m.] Skolasztika, a nun
2 CONT ****D6. Maria, +1026; m.1009 Otone Orseolo, Doge of Venice
2 CONT ****D7. [2m.] a daughter; m.1005/10 Sámuel Aba, King of Hungary (1041-44), +murdered 1044, bur Abasár
2 CONT ***** ...
2 CONT ***C2. Mihály (Michael), Duke between March and Gran, +ca 978/before 997; m.Adelajda of Poland (+after 997) dau./sister of Pr Mieszko I of Poland
2 CONT
