1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zavida
2 CONT -------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SERBIA.htm#ZavidB
2 CONT
2 CONT ZAVID, [son of UROŠ I Grand Župan of Serbia] & his wife [Anna Diogene].  Zavid’s supposed parentage, and the fact that he was the father of the four children shown below, is deduced from a combination of information.  Miroslav nam
2 CONC es his father as Zavid in a gospel which he wrote[80].  Other sources consistently name Tihomir, Stracimir, Miroslav and Nemanja as brothers, although it is not specified that they all shared the same father and mother.  According
2 CONC  to a charter written in 1198 by Nemanja, his great-grandfather and grandfather had "ruled the land".  (“Stephanus Nemanja, Serbiæ magnus županus” visited Mount Athos, charter dated 2 Nov 1198[81], Serbian text not consulted).  Th
2 CONC is statement is also found in the biographies of Nemanja written by his sons.  The deduction is that Nemanja's father, Zavid, was another son of Uroš I Grand Župan of Serbia (Chapter 2.C).  Emperor Manuel I's choice of Tihomir as 
2 CONC new ruler of Serbia in [1166] also makes more sense if he was closely related to the former dynasty rather than an outsider, as such a choice is more likely to have been acceptable to Serbia's leaders.  Zavid presumably rebelled i
2 CONC n some way against his [presumed] father or oldest brother, as Zavid's son Nemanja was born while his father was exiled in Zeta[82]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Zavid's wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Zavid & his wife had four children:
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT * According to Tibor Zivkovic (Portreti srpskih vladara, Beograd, 2006) '''zupan Zavida was the only son of Vukan.''' 
2 CONT * Other version of his father: '''Урош I / Uroš I''' (see: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uro%C5%A1_I_of_Rascia)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/balkan/balkan5.html
2 CONT
2 CONT The Nemanjiden One Zupan Zavida, whose 4 sons divided Serbia up and fought with each other:
2 CONT * A1. Tihomir, Duke of Serbia (ca 1166-ca 1171), +k.a.1169
2 CONT
2 CONT ** B1. Stefan Prvoslav, Zupan
2 CONT
2 CONT * A2. Stracimir, ruled in northern Serbia west of the Moldau (ca 1168-71), +after 25.12.1189
2 CONT
2 CONT * A3. Miroslav, Duke of Zahumlje (Hercegovina) (ca 1168-71), +1196/99; m.N, a sister of Ban Kulin of Bosnia
2 CONT
2 CONT ** B1. Toljen I; m.N, a dau.of Duke Berthold von Meran, Margrave of Istria; he may have been father of
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C1. Toljen II, Duke of North Zahumlje, +1239
2 CONT
2 CONT **** D1. Petar
2 CONT
2 CONT ***** E1. Nikola, Zupan of Zahumlje; m.before 1338 Katarina Kotromanic
2 CONT
2 CONT ****** F1. Boghiscia
2 CONT
2 CONT ****** F2. Vladislav
2 CONT
2 CONT ** B2. Petar, Duke of Zahumlje (1198-1227), Ct of Split (1222-25)
2 CONT
2 CONT ** B3. Andrija, Knez in Primorje, Duke in southern Zahumlje, +ca 1250
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C1. Bogdan, Zupan of Zahumlje 1249, +after 1252
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C2. Djordje, living 1280
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C3. Radoslav, Zupan of Zahumlje 1249, +after 22.5.1254
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C4. Vukoslava; m.Barbo di Crossio, patrician of Dubrovnik
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C5. Dragoslava; m.Drago de Mare
2 CONT
2 CONT * A4. Stefan Nemanja, Duke of all Serbia (1195-96), including Zahumlje and Diocleia, *1113, +as the monk Simeon on Holy Mount Athos 1200; m.Ana N (+as the nun Anastasia)
2 CONT
2 CONT ** B1. Vukan, King of Diocleia and Dalmatia, Duke of Serbia (1202-03), +ca 1208; m.N, a relative of Pope Innocent III
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C1. Djordje, Knez of Diocleia 1242, +after 21.8.1242
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C2. Bladinus, living 1208
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C3. Stefan
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C4. Demetrius, a monk
2 CONT
2 CONT ** B2. Stefan Prvovencani "the First-Crowned", Duke of all Serbia (1196-1217), crowned by papal legate as King of Raska (Serbia) (1217-27), +as the monk Simon 1227; 1m: 1191 (repudiated 1201/02) Eudoxia Angelina; 2m: 1204/07 NN; 3
2 CONC m: 1216/7 Anna (+ca 1264) dau.of Rainero Dandolo, Procurator of San Marco
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C1. [1m.] Stefan Radoslav III Dukas, King of Raska (1224-34), +as the monk Jovan after 1235; m.1219/20 (separated 1234) Anna Dukaina of Byzantia (+ca 1258)
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C2. [1m.] Kominia; 1m: Dimitri Progonovic, Archon of Albania (+1215); 2m: 1215 Grgur Kamonas, Archon of Kroja and Elassan
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C3. [1m.] a daughter, m.Alexander N, an official related to the Tsar of Bulgaria
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C4. [2m./3m.] Predislav, Archbishop of Serbia (1263-70)
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C5. [2m./3m.] Stefan Vladislav, King of Raska (1233-43), King in Scutari (1243-64), +ca 1269; m.ca 1233 Beloslava of Bulgaria (+after 1285)
2 CONT
2 CONT **** D1. Stefan
2 CONT
2 CONT **** D2. Desa, living 1285
2 CONT
2 CONT **** D3. a daughter, m.Djure Kacic, Knez of Omis
2 CONT
2 CONT *** C6. [3m.] Saint King Stepan Uros I "the Great" of Raska (Serbia) (1243-76) abdicated, +as the monk Simon 1280, bur Sopocani; m.ca 1250 Jelena (+as a nun at Skodra 1314), believed to be related to the Kings of Naples
2 CONT
2 CONT **** D1. Stepan IV Dragutin, King of Serbia (1276-82), Ban of Macva-Bosnia, +as a monk 1316; m.before 1271 Katalin of Hungary (*ca 1256)
2 CONT
2 CONT ***** E1. Vladislav; he spent his life trying to gain the thrones of Serbia and Hungary, but was unsuccessful in both quests; +in Hungary after 1326; 1m: ca 1293 Constanza, dau.of Michele Morosoni; 2m: 1309 N, a dau.of the Voivode
2 CONC  Ladislaus of Siebenbuergen; he had issue of whom I have no details
2 CONT
2 CONT ***** E2. Urosic, a monk, +ca 1306
2 CONT
2 CONT ***** E3. Jelisaveta, *ca 1270, +1331; m.after 1283 Stefan Kotroman, Ban of Bosnia (+1314/16)
2 CONT
2 CONT **** D2. Stepan Uros II Milutin, King of Serbia (1282-1321), *ca 1253, +Castle Nerodimlja 29.10.1321, bur Sofia; 1m: 1273/76 (repudiated 1283) Helene Angelina, dau.of Joannes Dukas Angelos, Sebastokrator in Neopatros; 2m: 1284 (re
2 CONC pudiated ca 1294) Ana, dau.of Tsar George Terter of Bulgaria; 3m: ca 1295 (repudiated 1298/9) Elizabeth of Hungary (*1255, +1313/26); 4m: ca 1300 Simonida Palaiologina (*1292/93, +after 1336)
2 CONT
2 CONT ***** E1. [2m.] Stepan Konstantin, Knez of Zahumlje, pretender to the Serbian throne, +k.a.1323
2 CONT
2 CONT ***** E2. [maternity uncertain] Ana, +after 1346; she was engaged 1308 to Charles, Cte de Valois, but never married him; m.after 1308 Tsar Mihailo III Shishman of Bulgaria (+1330)
2 CONT
2 CONT ***** E3. [illegitimate] Stefan Uros III, King of Serbia (1321-31), *ca 1276, +1331; 1m: ca 1293 Teodora (+1322), dau.of Tsar Smilec of Bulgaria; 2m: 1325/26 Maria Palaiologina (*1313/14, +1355)
2 CONT
2 CONT ****** F1. [1m.] Stefan Uros IV Dusan "The Strong", King of Serbia (1331-55), *ca 1308, +1355; m.1332 Jelena (+1374), sister of Tsar Ivan Asen Alexander of Bulgaria
2 CONT
2 CONT ******* G1. Stefan Uros V "The Weak", King of Serbia (1355-71), *1336/37, +4.12.1371; m.VII.1360 Ana Basaraba
2 CONT
2 CONT ****** F2. [1m.] Dusica
2 CONT
2 CONT ****** F3. [2m.] Simeon Uros Palaiologos, Tsar of the Serbs, Greeks and Albania (1356-69/72), *1324/26, +1369/72; m.before 1349 Tomaida Orsini, dau.of Joannes Orsini, Despot of Epirus
2 CONT
2 CONT ******* G1. Jovan Uros Dukas Palaiologos, Lord of the Thessalonians, *ca 1349, +1423
2 CONT
2 CONT ******* G2. Stefan Dukas, Lord of Pharsalos and Domokos, +1397; m.ca 1386 Maria (+murdered 1395) dau.of Luiz Fadrique de Aragon, Lord of Zituni, Cte di Salona
2 CONT
2 CONT ******* G3. Marija Angelina Dukaina Palaiologina, Lady of Jannina, *1350/51, +1394; 1m: Toma Preljubovic, Despot of Jannina (+murdered 1384); 2m: 1385 Isaul Buondelmonti-Acciaiuoli, Despot of Jannina (+1411)
2 CONT
2 CONT ****** F4. [2m.] Teodora, *1330, +after 1381; m.ca 1347 Dejan, Stattholder of Macedonia
2 CONT
2 CONT ****** F5. [?] Jelena; m.Mladen III Subich (+1348)
2 CONT
2 CONT **** D3. Brnca; m.Zupan Djordje
2 CONT
2 CONT ** B3. Rastko, became a monk and the first Archbishop of the independent Serbian Church, he was called Sava and was, soon after his death, recognized as St.Sava, *1174, +Trnovo 1235/26
2 CONT
2 CONT ** B4. Efimija; m.ca 1216 Manuel Angelos Dukas, Regent of Thesaloniki (+1241)
2 CONT
2 CONT ** B5. a daughter, m.Tich Boljar of Skopje
2 CONT
