1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reginald_of_Sidon
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Reginald Grenier''' (1130s – 1202; also '''Reynald''' or '''Renaud''') was lord of Sidon and an important noble in the late-12th century Kingdom of Jerusalem. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/JERUSALEM%20NOBILITY.htm#RenaudSidondied12001204B
2 CONT
2 CONT RENAUD Garnier of Sidon, son of GERARD Garnier Lord of Sidon & his wife Agnes of Bures-Tiberias (-[Nov 1200/1204]).  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Estace et Renaut" as the two sons of "Gerard de Garnier"[971].  William of Tyre nam
2 CONC es "Rainaldus" as the son of "Agnetem…domini Wilelmi de Buris neptem" by her second husband "Girardus Sydoniensis"[972].  "Girardus dominus Sidonis" donated property to the church of St Marie, Josaphat, with the consent of "Raynal
2 CONC di filii et heredum", by charter dated 4 Jan 1164[973].  Lord of Sidon and Beaufort.  He visited Saladin's court, hinting that he would convert to Islam, but meanwhile ordered the strengthening of the fortifications of the castle 
2 CONC of Beaufort against attack.  When his ruse was discovered, he was imprisoned in Damascus [Sep] 1189[974]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (before 1171, repudiated before 1174) as her fourth husband, AGNES de Courtenay, widow (firstly) of RENAUD Lord of Marash, divorced wife (secondly) of AMAURY I King of Jerusalem, widow (thirdly) of HUGUES Ibelin Lo
2 CONC rd of Rama, daughter of JOSCELIN II de Courtenay Count of Edessa & his wife Béatrice --- (1133-[Sep 1184/1 Feb 1185]).  William of Tyre names her husband and his father when he records this marriage and the couple's divorce on the
2 CONC  grounds of consanguinity (although he does not provide the factual basis for the claim)[975].  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Agnes, qui avoit esté feme dou rei Amauri et Hue de Ybelin…" as wife of "Renaut de Garnier"[976]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (before 1189) as her first husband, HELVIS Ibelin, daughter of BALIAN II Ibelin Lord of Nablus & his wife Maria Komnene (-before 1 Jun 1216).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "uxorem Renaldi de S
2 CONC idone" as the daughter of "Bethuliani de Guibelin" & his wife and her second husband "Guido de Monteforti", but does not name her[977].  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "une fille…Heloys, et un fiz Johan et une autre fille
2 CONC  Marguerite, et un fiz Phelippe" as children of "Belleem de Ybelin" & his wife, stating that "Heloys" was wife firstly of "Renaut seignor de Seete" and secondly of "Gui de Monfort"[978].  She married secondly ([1204]) as his first
2 CONC  wife, Guy de Montfort Seigneur de la Ferté-Alais et de Castres-en-Albegeois.  The Chronicle of Ernoul records the arrival of "li quens Simons de Montfort, et Guis ses freres" in Palestine [in 1204] and that "Guis prist à feme le 
2 CONC dame de Saiete"[979]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Renaud & his second wife had three children:
