2 CONT '''m''' (1228) MARGUERITE [Ida][981] de Reynel, daughter of ARNOUD de Reynel [Risnel] & his wife Ide de Brienne (-5 Jun [1254]).  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Marguerite, la niece dou rei Johan" as wife of "Bellin…seignor de Seet
2 CONC e"[982].  She is named as niece of Jean de Brienne by William of Tyre (Continuator), who also names her parents when he records her marriage[983].  Cousin of Yolande Queen of Jerusalem, it was alleged that Queen Yolande's husband 
2 CONC Emperor Friedrich II King of Germany seduced her on their wedding night 9 Nov 1225[984].  She is named "la gentile dame de Sayete, dame Margarite" in the contract dated 1252 relating to the marriage of her son (see below)[985].  T
2 CONC he Chronicle of Amadi records the death 5 Jun, in 1254 from the context, of "Margarita dama de Saeto"[986]. 
2 CONT
