1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melisende_of_Arsuf
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT Melisende
2 CONT Lady of Arsuf and Beirut
2 CONT
2 CONT Arsuf fortress, in Israel, home of the Crusader Lords of Arsuf
2 CONT Born	before 1177
2 CONT Died	Unknown
2 CONT Holy Land
2 CONT Spouse(s)	Thierry d'Orca
2 CONT John of Ibelin, the Old Lord of Beirut
2 CONT Issue	
2 CONT Balian, Lord of Beirut
2 CONT John, Lord of Arsuf
2 CONT Raoul of Ibelin
2 CONT Hugh of Ibelin
2 CONT Baldwin, Seneschal of Cyprus
2 CONT Guy, Constable of Cyprus
2 CONT Isabelle of Ibelin
2 CONT Father	Guy, Lord of Arsuf
2 CONT Mother	Unknown
2 CONT Melisende (born before 1177 – died after 1215) was the hereditary Lady of Arsuf from 1177 and the second wife of the powerful nobleman John, Old Lord of Beirut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT She was born sometime before 1177, the eldest daughter of Guy, Lord of Arsuf. Her mother's name is unknown. She had a brother, Lord Jean, who married Helvis de Brie.[1] When Jean died childless, Melisende inherited the lordship of
2 CONC  Arsuf.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT On an unknown date, Melisende married firstly Thierry d'Orca.[1] In 1207, she married secondly John of Ibelin, Lord of Beirut, former Constable of Jerusalem,[1] and Regent in Acre for his half-niece Queen Maria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon their marriage, Melisende passed the lordship of Arsuf to John, increasing his territory in the Kingdom of Jerusalem. Beirut was effectively an independent state under his rule, while remaining a vassal of the Sovereign. Afte
2 CONC r rebuilding the city which had been destroyed by the forces of Saladin, during the latter's conquest of the Crusader kingdom, Ibelin constructed a magnificent palace.
2 CONT
2 CONT John of Ibelin and Melisende had six sons and one daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT Balian of Ibelin (1210 – 4 September 1247 Askalon), in 1230, he married Eschiva de Montfaucon,[3] daughter of Walter de Montfaucon de Montbéliard and Bourgogne de Lusignan of Cyprus.
2 CONT
2 CONT John of Ibelin (1212 – December 1258), Lord of Arsuf, Constable of Jerusalem. Married Alix of Caiphas, daughter of Rohart of Caiphas and Aiglantine of Nephim.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Raoul of Ibelin
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh of Ibelin (1213–1238)[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Baldwin of Ibelin, Seneschal of Cyprus, (died 21 February 1267)[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy of Ibelin, constable of Cyprus (c. 1215 – May 1255), married Philippa, daughter of Aimery Berlais.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle of Ibelin, became a nun
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT Melisende died on an unknown date.
