2 CONT === B.      IBELIN - DESCENDANTS of BAUDOUIN IBELIN SENESCHAL of CYPRUS
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CYPRUS.htm#BaudouinIbelindied1267B<br/>
2 CONT BAUDOUIN Ibelin, son of JEAN Ibelin Lord of Beirut & his second wife Mélisende of Arsur (-21 Feb 1267).  The Chronicle of Philippe de Novare names "messier Balian…conestable de Chipre et seignor de Baruth…[et] messier Bauduyn…cene
2 CONC schal de Chipre" as the two sons of "monseignor de Baruth"[639].  He fought at the battle of Agridi in 1232.  He was appointed Seneschal of Cyprus in [1246].  He was taken prisoner at the battle of Mansurah in 1250[640].  The Chro
2 CONC nicle of Amadi records the death 21 Feb, in 1266 (old-style, presumably) from the context, of "Baduin de Iblim senescalco de Cypro"[641]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([1230]) ALIX of Bethsan, daughter of GAUTHIER [II] Lord of Bethsan & his second wife Theodora Komnene.  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Aalis la Seneschalece" as daughter of "Gautier" son of "Gremont le seignor de Bessan" a
2 CONC nd his wife "Latomena"[642].  Another manuscript of the Lignages names "Aalis et Femie" as the two daughters of Gauthier de Bethsan and his wife "une dame de Romanie, qui avoit nom Thodore Lathoumena", stating that Alix married "B
2 CONC auduin de Ybelin seneschal de Chipre"[643]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Baudouin & his wife had six children: 
