2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Manuel, Lord of Villena
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT For another Juan Manuel of Castile, the son of this person, see Juan Manuel, Duke of Peñafiel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Manuel (Carrion de los Condes, 1234 – Peñafiel, December 25, 1283, sometimes called only Manuel) was the son of Ferdinand III of Castile and his wife Elisabeth of Hohenstaufen. The name Manuel was given to him to commemorate 
2 CONC his maternal grandmother's roots in Imperial Byzantium[citation needed]. He was Lord of Escalona, Peñafiel and Villena.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married twice. His first wife, whom he married in 1260 in Soria was Constança of Aragon (1239-1269?), daughter of James I of Aragon. Two children were born of this marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfonso (born 1260/1261, died in Montepellier, France in 1276) Died without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Violante Manuel (born 1265, died in Lisbon, Portugal in 1314), lady of Elche and Medellin. Married circa 1287 to Affonso of Portugal, son of Alfonso III of Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT His second marriage after Constaca's death was in 1274/1275 to Beatrice of Savoy (d. 23 February 1292), daughter of Amadeus IV of Savoy. One child was born of this marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Manuel (1282-1348), Duke of Penafiel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children from other women include:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho Manuel (1283-after 1345), Lord of Infantado and Carrion. First married Maria Rodriguez de Castañeda, Second married Ines Dias de Toledo. With issues in both marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrique Manuel (born circa 1272)
2 CONT
2 CONT Branca Manuel (born circa 1273)
