1 NOTE Otho IV (1174-1218), Holy Roman emperor, was the son of Henry the Lion, Duke of Bavaria, and Matilda, daughter of Henry II of England. He was in 1197 chosen German king. Otho was elected emperor, and was crowned at Rome by Pope In
2 CONC nocent III in 1209. [The Home University Encyclopedia, 1946]
1 NOTE Origianally, he was Duke of Saxony.
