1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Son of King MANFRED von Hohenstaufen and his second wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SICILY.htm#Beatricedied1307
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. '''FEDERICO of Sicily''' (-after 2 Jun 1312). He suffered the same fate as his brother Enrico. A charter dated 9 Jan [1295] names "Henrici, Frederici ac Anselmi fratrum filiorum naturalium quondam Manfridi principis Tarentini i
2 CONC n castri…sancte Marie de Monte Carcere"[694]. A charter dated 26 Apr [1297] names "Henricum Fredericum et Aczolinum filios quondam principis Manfridi qui in dicto Castro [=castri Sancte Marie de Monte]…detinentur"[695]. A charter 
2 CONC dated 25 Jun 1299 names "Henricum Fredericum et Encium filios quondam Manfridi…principis Tarentini"[696]. According to Haverkamp, he escaped from prison in the early 1300s, stayed at various European courts and supposedly died in 
2 CONC Egypt in 1312[697].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Medlands (and other sources I have seen) do not address the issue of whether, after his escape from prison; did Federico marry and have children?
2 CONT
2 CONT There are many on-line family trees that  contend that he married Giovanna Di Antiochia and had a son and a daughter.  I believe many (or all) of these references originate from an entry in Malta Genealology, a source of dubious q
2 CONC uality.  Still investigating.
2 CONT
2 CONT /!\ https://www.maltagenealogy.com/hohenstaufen /!\ 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.1.1.2.1.3.2. '''Federico di Siciliano''', d.after 2 Jun 1312, married Giovanna di Antiochia, (See on this page), with issue.
2 CONT 1.1.1.2.1.3.2.1. Helene di Siciliano, 1305 - 48., married to Conradin von Sueva, (See on this page).
2 CONT 1.1.1.2.1.3.2.2. Manfredo di Siciliano 1303 - 51., married to Marianna di Chieti, (See on this page), with issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
