1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexios_Raoul
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTINE%20NOBILITY.htm#AlexiosRauldied1258
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.       '''  ALEXIOS Raoul''' ( -[1258] ).  Protobestiarios 1242/1256.  Georgios Akropolites names "…Raulus Alexius protovestiarius…" among the important nobles at the court of Emperor Ioannes Batatzes[610].  Hegemon in Thessalon
2 CONC iki 1253, deposed 1256 by Emperor Theodoros II.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' --- Batatzaina, daughter of --- Batatzes & his wife ---.  Her origin and marriage are referred to by Pachymeres who records that the "avia paterna [ …coniux protovestiarii Raulis Alexii]" of "coniux Porphyrogeniti" was "St
2 CONC rategopulinæ neptis ex fratre", clarifying that "Strategopulinæ" was born "ex fratre imperatoris dignitate sebastocratore", and that "eius vero avia" (which presumably refers back to "avia paterna") was "…ex ipsius altero germano"
2 CONC [611].  The passage appears to indicate that the wife of Alexios Raoul was the child of another brother of Emperor Ioannes III.  If this is correct, "neptis", in relation to "Strategopulinæ", must be interpreted as "cousin" rather
2 CONC  than "niece".  The chronology of the various families involved suggests that the wife of Alexios Raoul belonged to the same generation of the Batatzes family as the wife of Konstantinos Strategopoulous, although if this is correc
2 CONC t "neptis" must mean "first cousin" rather than "second cousin".  It should be emphasised that the passages in Pachymeres are complex and it is uncertain that the interpretation set out here is the only possible one.  In a recent 
2 CONC article, Estangüi Gómez adopts the same interpretation of this passage in Pachymeres[612].  Georgius Akropolites names "protovestiario Alexio, Raulo neptis marito", referring to Emperor Ioannes III[613].  
2 CONT
2 CONT    Alexios Raoul & his wife had [six] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/byzant/byzant7.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Batatzes family===
2 CONT
2 CONT One Basileios Batatzes, Duke of Thrace, +1193; m.a dau.of Isaakios Angelos; they had issue: 
2 CONT *A1. Isaakios Dukas Batatzes, +1261; m.NN 
2 CONT **B1. Ioannes Batatzes, *1215; m.Eudokia Angelina 
2 CONT ***C1. Theodora Batatzaina, *1240, +1303; m.1253 Emperor Michaél VIII Palaiologos (+1282) 
2 CONT ***C2. Maria Batatzaina; m.Michael Dukas Glabas Tarchaneiotes, military goveror of Thrace
2 CONT **B2. a daughter; m.Konstantinos Strategopulos
2 CONT *A2. a son; m.NN 
2 CONT **B1. a daughter; m.'''Alexios Raul (+1258)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
