1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Semen Sopiha - historically, the first confirmed ancestor of the Sapieha family. He was a writer and Grand Duke of Lithuania Casimir from 1441 to 1449. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Very little is known about Simon Sapiega's life. According to the legendary genealogy of the Sapiega family (Historia Domus Sapiehianae), Simon was the son of Sungaila, the great-great-grandson of Lithuanian Grand Duke Gediminas, 
2 CONC who adopted the "Lis" coat of arms during the Union of Horodlo. In the 19th century, genealogist Stadnicki found that Sungaila had died childless.
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon Sapiega came from Polotsk nobility, and his prominent estates were in Smolensk.
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon Sapiega was married to Anastasia Pava and had four sons; two of them, Bogdan and Ivashko, gave rise to two branches of the Sapiega family: Cherey and Koden.
