2 CONT
2 CONT Born 	1362 or 1365
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 	30 December 1435 (aged 69-70)
2 CONT
2 CONT Carlat
2 CONT
2 CONT Bonne of Berry (1362/1365 - 30 December 1435) was the daughter of John, Duke of Berry and Joanna of Armagnac. Through her father, she was a granddaughter of John II of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [show]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 1 First marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 2 Second marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 3 Ancestry
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 4 References
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 5 Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] First marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Her first married was to Amadeus VII, Count of Savoy. Their marriage contract is dated 7 May 1372 and they married in 18 January 1377, but she wouldn't arrive in Savoy until 1381.[1] They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Amadeus VIII, Duke of Savoy (1383 - 1439); married Mary of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Bonne of Savoy (1388 - 1432); married Louis of Piedmont.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Jeanne of Savoy (unknown - 1460; married Giangiacomo Paleologo, marquis of Montferrat.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Amadeus' death in 1391, a regency dispute over their son Amadeus VIII ensued after her husband passed over Bonne in favor of his mother Bonne of Bourbon. This conflict would only be resolved by an agreement, signed on 8 May 
2 CONC 1393.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Second marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Her second marriage was to Bernard VII of Armagnac. Their marriage contract is dated on 2 December 1393.[2] They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * John IV of Armagnac (1396 - 1450); married (1) Blanche of Brittany (2) Isabella d' Évreux
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Marie (1397), died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Bonne d'Armagnac (1399 - 1415); married Charles, Duke of Orléans.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Bernard d'Armagnac, Count of Pardiac (1400 - 1462); married Eleanor of Bourbon-La Marche.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Anne of Armagnac (1402 - before 1473); married Charles II of Albret.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Jeanne (1403), died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Béatrix (1406), died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. ^ Crawley, Medieval Lands
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. ^ Crawley, Medieval Lands
2 CONT
