2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1412 he married Joanna of Savoy, sister of Duke Amadeus VIII, who gave him numerous children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amadeus VII (1360 – November 1, 1391), surnamed the Red Count, was Count of Savoy from 1383 to 1391.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Bonne of Berry, daughter of John, Duke of Berry who was the younger brother of Charles V of France. They had three children: Amedeo VIII; Bonne (d. 1432, married to Louis, the final of the Savoy-Archaea Branch; see also
2 CONC  Thomas II of Savoy); and Joan (d. 1460, married to Giangiacomo Paleologo, marquis of Montferrat, a descendant of the Byzantine emperor Andronicus II Palaeologus).
