2 CONC d which "ameras" [the emir, unspecified] had given to “Isaacio Asani” who had later given it to “Georgio Philanthropeno genero [γαμβρω] suo” who, in turn had given it to “Comneno consobrino [ανεψιω], Cantacuzeni protostratoris gen
2 CONC ero [γαμβρω]”, adding that the latter “Galatam fugientem” [fleeing to Galata] had been captured by Phrantzes’s brother (who had been granted the horse as a reward)[582].  Theodoros Spandounes names "signore Emanuel Cantacusino fra
