1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Esau de' Buondelmonti (Greek: Ησαύ Μπουοντελμόντ) was the ruler of Ioannina and its surrounding area (central Epirus) from 1385 until his death in 1411, with the Byzantine title of Despot.
