1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Friedrich  "der Sanftmütige" Kurfürst von Sachsen===
2 CONT ===Frederick "the Gentle" of Saxony===
2 CONT *Friedrich fought the so called Saxon Brother war with his brother William III 1446-1451 
2 CONT *Afterwards Saxon was divided between Frederick I and William III
2 CONT *When William died 1482, without issues, Thuringa fell back to Frederick II's two sons
2 CONT *By his death the country was divided between his two sons Ernst I and Albert founder of two new branches of the house of Wettin named Ernestiner and Albertiner
2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p11391.htm#i113907 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/D/per_page.php?id=52931 Geneall]
2 CONT *'''Wikipedia:'''  [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_II,_Elector_of_Saxony English ][http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friedrich_II._(Sachsen)_ Deutsch ] [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Division_of_Altenburg Division of Altenburg]
2 CONT *'''Elector of Saxony''' Reign 4. January 1428 – 7. September 1464 
2 CONT >'''Predecessor''' [http://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000001534995483 Frederick I] '''Successor''' [http://www.geni.com/people/index/6000000001534949474 Ernest] 
2 CONT *'''Landgrave of Thuringia''' Reign 7. May 1440 - 1445 
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000001534995483 Frederick  IV] '''Successor'''  [http://www.geni.com/people/index/6000000003858686083 William II]
2 CONT *'''Margrave of Meissen and Duke of Saxony''' Reign 4. January 1428 – 7. September 1464 >'''Predecessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000001534995483 Frederick IV/I] '''Successor:'''  [http://www.geni.com/people/index
