1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Katherina von Sachsen, Kurfürstin zu Brandenburg=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Friedrich I "den Stridbare" von Sachsen and Katharina Welf, Markgräfin zu Meißen, Pfalzgräfin und Kurfürstin zu Sachsen
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXONY.htm#FriedrichIVMeissenISaxonydied1428B Project MedLands, Chapter 8.   ELECTORS of SAXONY (WETTIN)]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''FRIEDRICH von Meissen, son of FRIEDRICH III "der Strenge" joint Markgraf von Meissen & his wife Katharina von Henneberg (11 Apr 1370-Altenburg 4 Jan 1428, bur Meissen Cathedral).'''  The Annales Veterocellenses record the birth
2 CONC  "1370 in cena Domini" of "Fridericus filius Friderici marchioni Misniensis"[726].  He succeeded his father in 1381 as FRIEDRICH IV "der Streitbare" Markgraf von Meissen and Landgraf of Thuringia, jointly with his brothers.  From 
2 CONC 1382 im Osterland Landsberg.  '''He was installed in 1423 by the Emperor as FRIEDRICH I Herzog von Sachsen, Elector of Saxony, in succession to Albrecht IV last Elector of Saxony of the Askanier family who had died in 1422.'''  ''
2 CONC 'Married  (8 Feb 1402) KATHARINA von Braunschweig, daughter of HEINRICH Herzog von Braunschweig in Lüneburg & his first wife Sophie von Pommern''' (-Grimma 28 Dec 1442, bur Meissen Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Pic
2 CONC turatum names “Katherina”, who married “Marggreven Frederiken to Myssen”, as the daughter of “Hertoghe Hinrick, Hertoghe Magnus sone to Brunswick unde Lunenborch” and his first wife[727]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elector Friedrich I & his wife KATHARINA von Braunschweig had seven children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''KATHARINA''' (-young, bur Altzelle). 
2 CONT * 2.         '''FRIEDRICH''' (Leipzig 1412-Leipzig 1464, bur Meissen Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Frederick...eyn Korforste des Romeschen Rikes” first of the three sons of “Marggreve Frederick to
2 CONC  Myssen, Lantgreve to Döringh” and his wife[728].  '''He succeeded his father in 1428 as FRIEDRICH II "der Sanftmütige" Elector of Saxony, Joint Herzog zu Sachsen jointly with his brothers.'''
2 CONT * 3.         '''SIGISMUND''' (Grimma 3 Mar 1416-in prison in Rochlitz 24 Dec 1471, bur Meissen Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Sygemunt...Bischopp to Würtzburgk” third of the three sons of “Marggrev
2 CONC e Frederick to Myssen, Lantgreve to Döringh” and his wife[729].  Canon at Köln cathedral 1437.  Bishop of Würzburg 1440, resigned 1443.  
2 CONT * 4.         '''ANNA''' (5 Jun 1420-17 Sep 1462, bur Spangenberg Stadtkirche).  '''married  (Kassel 8 Sep 1433) LUDWIG III "der Friedsame" Landgraf Herr von Hessen, son of HERMANN II "der Gelehrte" Landgraf Herr von Hessen & his s
2 CONC econd wife Margareta von Nürnberg (-Spangenberg 17 Jan 1458, bur Marburg Elisabethkirche).''' 
2 CONT * 5.         '''KATHARINA''' (1421-Berlin 23 Aug 1476, bur Kloster Lehnin).  Nun at Seusslitz 1428/1429.  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum records that “Marggreve Frederick de elder, Marggreve Frederikes sone to Branden
2 CONC borch” married “Katherinam, Hertoghen Frederikes unde Wilhelms suster to Sassen...”[730].  '''married  (Wittenberg 11 Jun 1441) FRIEDRICH II Elector of Brandenburg, son of FRIEDRICH I Markgraf and Elector von Brandenburg & his wif
2 CONC e Elisabeth von Bayern-Landshut''' (Tangermünde 19 Nov 1413-Neustadt am Aisch 10 Feb 1471, bur Heilsbronn).
2 CONT * 6.         '''HEINRICH''' (Meissen 21 May 1422-Dresden 22 Jul 1435, bur Dresden Cathedral).  
2 CONT * 7.         '''WILHELM''' (Meissen 30 Apr 1425-Weimar 17 Sep 1482, bur Weimar Franziskanerkirche).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Wilhelm...Lantgreve to Doringh...ein Hertoghe to Sassen” second of the three s
2 CONC ons of “Marggreve Frederick to Myssen, Lantgreve to Döringh” and his wife[731].  Herzog von Luxemburg 1439-1443, and 1457-1469.  He succeeded in 1440 as WILHELM III "der Tapfere" Joint Landgraf of Thuringia, jointly with his broth
2 CONC er.  His brother relinquished Thuringia to Wilhelm as sole Landgraf in 1445.  '''married  firstly (Jena 20 Jun 1446) ANNA Archduchess of Austria, daughter of ALBRECHT V Duke of Austria [ALBRECHT II King of the Romans, ALBERT King 
2 CONC of Hungary, ALBRECHT King of Bohemia] & his wife Elisabeth Pss of Bohemia and Hungary [Luxembourg] (Vienna 12 Apr 1432-Eckartsberga 13 Nov 1462, bur Reinhardsbrunn).'''  The Necrologium Austriacum names Anna as older daughter of D
2 CONC uke Albrecht[732].  The Catalogus abbatum Sanganensium records that one daughter of "Albertus dux Austrie" married "Wilhelmo lantgravio Thuringie"[733].  '''married  secondly (Weimar 6 Jul 1463) KATHARINA von Brandenstein, daughte
2 CONC r of EBERHARD von Brandenstein zu Oppurg und Brandenstein & his wife Jutta''' --- (-Saalfeld 2 Nov 1492, bur Weimar St Peter & Paul).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Landgraf Wilhelm & his first wife had two children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* a)         '''MARGARETA''' (Weimar 1449-Spandau 13 Jul 1501, bur Berlin Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Margareta”, who married “Marggreve Hans to Brandenborch, Marggreven Albrechtes sone”, a
2 CONC s the daughter of “Hertoghe Wilhelm to Sassen, Marggreve to Myssen unde Lantgreve to Döringh” and his wife[734].  '''married  (Berlin 26 Aug 1476) JOHANN CICERO von Brandenburg, son of ALBRECHT ACHILLES Elector of Brandenburg & hi
2 CONC s first wife Margareta von Baden (Ansbach 2 Aug 1455-Schloß Arneburg 9 Jan 1499, bur Berlin Cathedral).'''  '''He succeeded his father in 1486 as JOHANN CICERO Elector of Brandenburg.''' 
2 CONT >>>>>* b)         '''KATHARINA''' (1453-17 Jan 1534).  '''married  (26 Feb 1471) HEINRICH II "Hynek" Duke of Münsterberg Graf von Glatz, son of JIŘI von Podiebrad King of Bohemia & his second wife Johanna von Rožmital zu Blatna (1
2 CONC 7 May 1452-11 Jul 1492, bur Glatz).  Herr zu Podiebrad und Kolin 1472.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRANDENBURG,%20PRUSSIA.htm#Dorotheadied1519 Project MedLands, Chapter 6. ELECTORS of BRANDENBURG (HOHENZOLLERN)]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''FRIEDRICH von Nürnberg, son of FRIEDRICH V joint Burggraf von Nürnberg & his wife Elisabeth von Meissen''' ([6 Aug/26 Nov] 1371-Schloß Kadolzburg 20 Sep 1440, bur Kloster Heilsbronn).  '''He succeeded on the abdication of his f
2 CONC ather in 1397 as FRIEDRICH VI joint Burggraf von Nürnberg, jointly with his brother.'''  Oberster Verweser (Chief Administrator) der Mark at Ofen 8 Jul 1411, pawned to him by Emperor Sigismund.  The emperor was unable to redeem th
2 CONC e pledge and created him FRIEDRICH I Markgraf and Elector of Brandenburg by Imperial Order at Konstanz 30 Apr 1415, solemn investiture 1417.  He sold his castle of Nürnberg in 1427 to Nürnberg town.  The necrology of Kaisheim reco
2 CONC rds the death "XII Kal Oct" of "Fridericus marchio de Brandenburg senior, defensor noster"[345]. '''Married (Schongau am Lech 18 Sep 1401) ELISABETH von Bayern-Landshut, daughter of FRIEDRICH Duke of Bavaria in Landshut & his seco
2 CONC nd wife Maddalena Visconti (1383-Schloß Ansbach 13 Nov 1442, bur Kloster Heilsbronn).'''  Andreas von Regensburg’s early 15th century Chronica names “Heinricum tenentem iam principatum in Lanczhuet et Elyzabet uxorem Friderici mar
2 CONC chionis Branburgensis qui et burgravius Nürnbergensis” as the children of “Fridericus” and his wife “[filia] domini Mediolanensis”[346]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elector Friedrich I & his wife Elizabeth von Bayern-Landshut had ten children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''ELISABETH''' ([1 May/29 Sep] 1403-Liegnitz 31 Oct 1449, bur Liegnitz Kartause).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Elizabeth”, who married “Hertoghen Lodewich to Legenitze unde to fem Bryge”, as ol
2 CONC dest of the five daughters of “Marggreve Frederick to Brandenborch unde Borggreve to Nurenbarge” and his wife[347].  '''married firstly (Konstanz 9 Apr 1418) as his second wife, LUDWIG II Duke of Brieg and Liegnitz, son of HEINRIC
2 CONC H VII Herzog von Lüben und Brieg & his second wife Małgorzata of Mazovia ([1380/85]-30 May 1436).  married secondly ([9 Dec 1438/5 Feb 1439]) WENZEL I Duke of Teschen, son of BOLKO I Duke of Auschwitz und Teschen [Piast] & his sec
2 CONC ond wife Euphemia of Mazovia [Piast] ([1413/18]-1474).'''
2 CONT * 2.         '''JOHANN "der Alchymist"''' (1406-Baiersdorf 16 Nov 1464, bur Heilsbronn).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Hans” as third (called eldest son in a later passage) of the four sons of “Marggreve Fred
2 CONC erick to Brandenborch unde Borggreve to Nurenbarge” and his wife[348].  Verweser der Mark until 1437.  He renounced his rights of succession on the death of his father.  Verweser von Bayreuth in 1440, to which he renounced his rig
2 CONC hts in 1457.  '''married  (contract 25 Aug 1411, before 26 May 1416) BARBARA von Sachsen, daughter of RUDOLF III Elector of Saxony & his second wife Barbara von Liegnitz [Piast]''' (after 1406-Bayreuth 10 Oct 1465, bur Bayreuth Pf
2 CONC arrkirche).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Barbara”, who married “Marggreve Hans to Brandeborch”, as daughter of “Hertoghe Roleff, Hertoghen Wenslaus sone to Sassen, eyn Korforste des Romeschen Rikes” and his 
2 CONC wife “Barbaram, des Hertoghen dochter van Legenitze unde van dem Bryge”[349].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johann & his wife Barbara von Sachsen had four children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* a)         '''BARBARA''' (1423-Mantua 7 Nov 1481, bur Mantua San Francesco).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Elizabeth”, who married “den Marggreven to Mantaw”, second of the three daughters of “Marggrev
2 CONC e Hans, Marggreven Frederikes to Brandenborch...eledeste sone” and his wife[350].  '''married  (Mantua 12 Nov 1433) LODOVICO di Gonzaga di Mantua, son of GIANFRANCESCO Gonzaga Marchese di Mantua & his wife Paula Malatesta''' (5 Ju
2 CONC n 1414-12 Jun 1478).  He succeeded his father in 1444 as LODOVICO III Marchese di Mantua. 
2 CONT >>>>>* b)         '''RUDOLF''' (Trebitz, Saxony 2 Feb 1424-Oct 1424).
2 CONT >>>>>* c)         '''ELISABETH''' (1425-after 13 Jan 1465).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Barbara”, who married “Hertoghen Werstleyff to Pomeren”, third of the three daughters of “Marggreve Hans, Marggreven F
2 CONC rederikes to Brandenborch...eledeste sone” and his wife[351].  '''married firstly (29 Sep 1440) JOACHIM Duke of Pomerania, son of KASIMIR V Duke of Pomerania in Stettin & his first wife Katharina von Braunschweig-Lüneburg''' ([142
2 CONC 7]-1451 after 8 Sep).  '''married secondly (5 Mar 1454) as his first wife, WARTISLAW X Duke of Pomerania, son of WARTISLAW IX Duke of Pomerania & his wife Sophie von Sachsen-Lauenburg (-17 Dec 1478).'''
2 CONT >>>>>* d)         '''DOROTHEA''' (1430-Kalundborg 25 Nov 1495, bur Roskilde Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Dorothea”, who married “Konigh Cristoff to Dennemarcke” and secondly “Greven Karsten to Ol
2 CONC denborch...Konigh...to Dennemarcke”, first of the three daughters of “Marggreve Hans, Marggreven Frederikes to Brandenborch...eledeste sone” and his wife[352].  '''married firstly (Copenhagen 12 Sep 1445) CHRISTOPHER III King of D
2 CONC enmark Norway and Sweden Pfalzgraf von Neunburg und Neumarkt, son of JOHANN Pfalzgraf von Neuburg vorm Wald und in Neumarkt & his first wife Katharina von Pommern-Stolp''' (26 Feb 1416-Helsingborg 5/6 Jan 1448, bur Roskilde Cathed
2 CONC ral).  '''married secondly (Copenhagen 28 Oct 1449) CHRISTIAN I King of Denmark Norway and Sweden Graf von Oldenburg, son of DIETRICH Graf von Oldenburg & his second wife Hedwig von Schleswig und Holstein''' (Oldenburg Feb 1426-Co
2 CONC penhagen 21 May 1481 bur Roskilde Cathedral). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johann had one illegitimate child by an unknown mistress:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* e)         '''FRITZ''' .  1456. 
2 CONT * 3.         '''CÄCILIE''' (-4 Jan 1449, bur Braunschweig Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Cecilia”, who married “Hertoghen Wilhelm to Brunswick unde Lunenborch”, second of the five daughters of “Mar
2 CONC ggreve Frederick to Brandenborch unde Borggreve to Nurenbarge” and his wife[353].  The Notæ Sancti Blasii name "Cecilia de Brandenburg" as wife of "princeps dominus Wilhelmus in Brunswik et Lunenburg dux"[354].  '''married  (Berli
2 CONC n 30 May 1423) as his first wife, WILHELM I "der Ältere" Herzog von Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Wolfenbüttel, son of HEINRICH II Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg & his first wife Sophie von Pommern''' (1392-Braunschweig 25 Jul 14
2 CONC 82, bur Braunschweig Cathedral).
2 CONT * 4.         '''MARGARETA''' ([1410]-Landshut 27 Jul 1465, bur Kloster Seligenthal).  Betrothed (1423) ALBRECHT V Herzog von Mecklenburg, son of ALBRECHT III joint Herzog von Mecklenburg & his first wife Richardis von Schwerin (-[
2 CONC 1 Jun/6 Dec] 1423, bur Gadebusch).  '''married firstly (Ingolstadt 20 Jul 1441) LUDWIG von Bayern-Ingolstadt, son of LUDWIG VII "der Bärtige" Duke of Bavaria-Ingolstadt & his first wife Anne de Bourbon''' (1 Sep 1403-Ingolstadt 7 
2 CONC Apr 1445, bur Ingolstadt Unsere Liebe Frau).  '''He succeeded his father in 1443 as LUDWIG VIII "der Höckrige" Duke of Bavaria-Ingolstadt.'''  '''married secondly (1446) MARTIN von Waldenfels zu Wartenfels,''' son of --- (-before 
2 CONC 7 May 1471).
2 CONT * 5.         '''MAGDALENA''' ([1412]-Scharnebeck 27 Oct 1454, bur Scharnebeck).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Magdalena”, who married “Hertoghen Frederick to Brunswick unde Lunenborch upp der Heyde”, third of
2 CONC  the five daughters of “Marggreve Frederick to Brandenborch unde Borggreve to Nurenbarge” and his wife[355].  '''married  (Tangermünde 3 Jul 1429, 16 Sep 1430) FRIEDRICH von Braunschweig, son of BERNHARD I Herzog von Braunschweig 
2 CONC und Lüneburg & his wife Margareta von Sachsen-Wittenberg''' (-Celle 19 Mar 1478, bur Celle Grauemönchskloster).  He succeeded his brother in 1445 as FRIEDRICH "der Fromme" Herzog von Braunschweig in Lüneburg. 
2 CONT * 6.         '''FRIEDRICH''' (Tangermünde 19 Nov 1413-Neustadt am Aisch 10 Feb 1471, bur Heilsbronn).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Frederick de olde...Korforste” as oldest of the four sons of “Marggreve Fred
2 CONC erick to Brandenborch unde Borggreve to Nurenbarge” and his wife[356].  Verweser der Mark 1437.  '''He succeeded his father in 1440 as FRIEDRICH II Markgraf and Elector of Brandenburg.'''  He abdicated in 1470 in favour of his bro
2 CONC ther, in return for the principality of Kulmbach.  '''married  (Wittenberg 11 Jun 1441) KATHARINA von Sachsen, daughter of FRIEDRICH I "der Streitbare" Elector of Saxony & his wife Katharina von Braunschweig''' (1421-Berlin 23 Aug
2 CONC  1476, bur Kloster Lehnin).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum records that “Marggreve Frederick de elder, Marggreve Frederikes sone to Brandenborch” married “Katherinam, Hertoghen Frederikes unde Wilhelms suster to Sass
2 CONC en...”[357].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elector Friedrich II & his wife Katharina von Sachsen had four children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* a)         '''DOROTHEA''' (1448-1519 before 20 Mar, bur Ratzeburg).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Dorothea”, who married “Hertoghen Hans te Loenborch”, second of the two daughters of “Marggreve Frederi
2 CONC ck de elder, Marggreve Frederikes sone to Brandenborch” and his wife[358].  '''married  (Lüneburg 12 Feb 1464) JOHANN V Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg, son of BERNHARD II Herzog von Sachsen in Lauenburg und Ratzeburg & his wife Adel
2 CONC heid von Pommern (18 Jul 1439-15 Aug 1507, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).'''
2 CONT >>>>>* b)         '''MARGARETA''' ([1447/52]-1489, bur Wolgast).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Margareta”, who married “Hertoghen Bucksleff to Stettyn”, first of the two daughters of “Marggreve Frederick de e
2 CONC lder, Marggreve Frederikes sone to Brandenborch” and his wife[359].  '''married  (Prenzlau 21 Sep 1477) as his first wife, BOGISLAW X "der Grosse" Duke of Pomerania, son of ERICH II Duke of Pomerania-Wolgast & his wife Sophie von 
2 CONC Pommern (Stolp 3 Jul 1454-Stettin 5 Oct 1523, bur Stettin).'''
2 CONT >>>>>* c)         '''JOHANN''' (before 13 Dec 1452-before 1454).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Hans unde...Erasmus” as the two sons of “Marggreve Frederick de elder, Marggreve Frederikes sone to Brandenborch”
2 CONC  and his wife[360]. 
2 CONT >>>>>* d)         '''ERASMUS''' (after 1453-[1464/65]).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Hans unde...Erasmus” as the two sons of “Marggreve Frederick de elder, Marggreve Frederikes sone to Brandenborch” and his 
2 CONC wife[361]. 
2 CONT * 7.         '''ALBRECHT ACHILLES''' (Tangermünde 29 Nov 1414-Frankfurt am Main 11 Mar 1486, bur Heilsbronn).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Albrecht...Korforste” as second of the four sons of “Marggreve Frede
2 CONC rick to Brandenborch unde Borggreve to Nurenbarge” and his wife[362].  He succeeded in 1440 in Ansbach.  He succeeded in 1457 in Bayreuth, on the abdication of his brother Johann.  '''He succeeded on the abdication of his brother 
2 CONC in 1470 as ALBRECHT ACHILLES Elector of Brandenburg.''' 
2 CONT * 8.         '''SOPHIE''' (Nürnberg [1 May/29 Sep] 1416-[1416/17]).
2 CONT * 9.         '''DOROTHEA''' (Berlin 9 Feb 1420-Kloster Rehna 19 Jan 1491, bur Gadebusch).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Dorothea”, who married “Hertoghen Hinrick to Mekelenborch”, fourth of the five daughters
2 CONC  of “Marggreve Frederick to Brandenborch unde Borggreve to Nurenbarge” and his wife[363].  '''married  (1432) HEINRICH IV "der Fette" Herzog von Mecklenburg, son of JOHANN IV Herzog von Mecklenburg & his second wife Katharina von 
2 CONC Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (1417-9 Mar 1477).
2 CONT * 10.      '''FRIEDRICH "der Jüngere/der Fette"''' ([1424]-Tangermünde 6 Oct 1463).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Frederick de junge...in der olden Marckewas to Soltweddel” as fourth of the four sons of “Marg
2 CONC greve Frederick to Brandenborch unde Borggreve to Nurenbarge” and his wife[364].  Herr der Altmark und Priegnitz 1447.  '''married (Tangermünde 9 Feb 1449) as her first husband, AGNES von Pommern, daughter of BARNIM VIII Duke of P
2 CONC omerania & his wife Agnes von Wunstorf''' ([1436]-Bernburg 9 May 1512, bur Ballenstedt).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum records that “Marggreve Frederick de junger, Marggreven Frederikes sone to Brandenborg...” marri
2 CONC ed “Angenese, des Hertoghen dochter to Bart unde Pomeren”[365].  '''She married secondly (1478) Georg II Fürst von Anhalt-Zerbst.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Friedrich & his wife Agnes von Pommern had one child:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* a)         '''MAGDALENE''' (1460-Burg Hohenzollern 17 Jun 1496, bur Hechingen).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Magdalena”, who married “Greve Eytel-Fritze von Hogentzorn”, as the daughter of “Marggreve 
2 CONC Frederick de junger, Marggreven Frederikes sone to Brandenborg...” and his wife[366].  '''married  (Berlin Schloß 17 Feb 1482) EITEL FRIEDRICH [II] Graf von Zollern, son of JOST NIKOLAUS [II] Graf von Zollern & his wife Agnes von 
2 CONC Werdenberg (1452-Trier 18 Jun 1512).''' 
2 CONT
