1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Anna Wettin, Countess of Hesse=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Friedrich I "den Stridbare" of Saxony and Katharina Welf, Margravine of Meißen, Countess Palatine and Electress of Saxony 
2 CONT * Anna was the eldest daughter of Elector Friedrich I of Saxony (1370–1428) from his marriage to Katharina (1395–1442), daughter of Duke Heinrich I of Braunschweig .
2 CONT * Anna, endowed with a dowry of 19,000 Rhenish gold guilders, married Landgrave Ludwig I of Hesse on September 8, 1433 in Kassel . The engagement was announced on the occasion of the hereditary brotherhood of both houses in Rotenb
2 CONC urg an der Fulda in 1431 . Through his marriage, Ludwig expanded his territory considerably. Anna received it back from Anna's brother Friedrich II. Eschwege and Sontra from Saxon property; Frederick II also waived his rights to W
2 CONC anfried .
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXONY.htm#FriedrichIVMeissenISaxonydied1428B Project MedLands, Chapter 8.   ELECTORS of SAXONY (WETTIN)]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''FRIEDRICH von Meissen, son of FRIEDRICH III "der Strenge" joint Markgraf von Meissen & his wife Katharina von Henneberg (11 Apr 1370-Altenburg 4 Jan 1428, bur Meissen Cathedral).'''  The Annales Veterocellenses record the birth
2 CONC  "1370 in cena Domini" of "Fridericus filius Friderici marchioni Misniensis"[726].  He succeeded his father in 1381 as FRIEDRICH IV "der Streitbare" Markgraf von Meissen and Landgraf of Thuringia, jointly with his brothers.  From 
2 CONC 1382 im Osterland Landsberg.  '''He was installed in 1423 by the Emperor as FRIEDRICH I Herzog von Sachsen, Elector of Saxony, in succession to Albrecht IV last Elector of Saxony of the Askanier family who had died in 1422.'''  ''
2 CONC 'Married  (8 Feb 1402) KATHARINA von Braunschweig, daughter of HEINRICH Herzog von Braunschweig in Lüneburg & his first wife Sophie von Pommern''' (-Grimma 28 Dec 1442, bur Meissen Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Pic
2 CONC turatum names “Katherina”, who married “Marggreven Frederiken to Myssen”, as the daughter of “Hertoghe Hinrick, Hertoghe Magnus sone to Brunswick unde Lunenborch” and his first wife[727]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elector Friedrich I & his wife KATHARINA von Braunschweig had seven children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''KATHARINA''' (-young, bur Altzelle). 
2 CONT * 2.         '''FRIEDRICH''' (Leipzig 1412-Leipzig 1464, bur Meissen Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Frederick...eyn Korforste des Romeschen Rikes” first of the three sons of “Marggreve Frederick to
2 CONC  Myssen, Lantgreve to Döringh” and his wife[728].  '''He succeeded his father in 1428 as FRIEDRICH II "der Sanftmütige" Elector of Saxony, Joint Herzog zu Sachsen jointly with his brothers.'''
2 CONT * 3.         '''SIGISMUND''' (Grimma 3 Mar 1416-in prison in Rochlitz 24 Dec 1471, bur Meissen Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Sygemunt...Bischopp to Würtzburgk” third of the three sons of “Marggrev
2 CONC e Frederick to Myssen, Lantgreve to Döringh” and his wife[729].  Canon at Köln cathedral 1437.  Bishop of Würzburg 1440, resigned 1443.  
2 CONT * 4.         '''ANNA''' (5 Jun 1420-17 Sep 1462, bur Spangenberg Stadtkirche).  '''married  (Kassel 8 Sep 1433) LUDWIG III "der Friedsame" Landgraf Herr von Hessen, son of HERMANN II "der Gelehrte" Landgraf Herr von Hessen & his s
2 CONC econd wife Margareta von Nürnberg (-Spangenberg 17 Jan 1458, bur Marburg Elisabethkirche).''' 
2 CONT * 5.         '''KATHARINA''' (1421-Berlin 23 Aug 1476, bur Kloster Lehnin).  Nun at Seusslitz 1428/1429.  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum records that “Marggreve Frederick de elder, Marggreve Frederikes sone to Branden
2 CONC borch” married “Katherinam, Hertoghen Frederikes unde Wilhelms suster to Sassen...”[730].  '''married  (Wittenberg 11 Jun 1441) FRIEDRICH II Elector of Brandenburg, son of FRIEDRICH I Markgraf and Elector von Brandenburg & his wif
2 CONC e Elisabeth von Bayern-Landshut''' (Tangermünde 19 Nov 1413-Neustadt am Aisch 10 Feb 1471, bur Heilsbronn).
2 CONT * 6.         '''HEINRICH''' (Meissen 21 May 1422-Dresden 22 Jul 1435, bur Dresden Cathedral).  
2 CONT * 7.         '''WILHELM''' (Meissen 30 Apr 1425-Weimar 17 Sep 1482, bur Weimar Franziskanerkirche).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Wilhelm...Lantgreve to Doringh...ein Hertoghe to Sassen” second of the three s
2 CONC ons of “Marggreve Frederick to Myssen, Lantgreve to Döringh” and his wife[731].  Herzog von Luxemburg 1439-1443, and 1457-1469.  He succeeded in 1440 as WILHELM III "der Tapfere" Joint Landgraf of Thuringia, jointly with his broth
2 CONC er.  His brother relinquished Thuringia to Wilhelm as sole Landgraf in 1445.  '''married  firstly (Jena 20 Jun 1446) ANNA Archduchess of Austria, daughter of ALBRECHT V Duke of Austria [ALBRECHT II King of the Romans, ALBERT King 
2 CONC of Hungary, ALBRECHT King of Bohemia] & his wife Elisabeth Pss of Bohemia and Hungary [Luxembourg] (Vienna 12 Apr 1432-Eckartsberga 13 Nov 1462, bur Reinhardsbrunn).'''  The Necrologium Austriacum names Anna as older daughter of D
2 CONC uke Albrecht[732].  The Catalogus abbatum Sanganensium records that one daughter of "Albertus dux Austrie" married "Wilhelmo lantgravio Thuringie"[733].  '''married  secondly (Weimar 6 Jul 1463) KATHARINA von Brandenstein, daughte
2 CONC r of EBERHARD von Brandenstein zu Oppurg und Brandenstein & his wife Jutta''' --- (-Saalfeld 2 Nov 1492, bur Weimar St Peter & Paul).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Landgraf Wilhelm & his first wife had two children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* a)         '''MARGARETA''' (Weimar 1449-Spandau 13 Jul 1501, bur Berlin Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Margareta”, who married “Marggreve Hans to Brandenborch, Marggreven Albrechtes sone”, a
2 CONC s the daughter of “Hertoghe Wilhelm to Sassen, Marggreve to Myssen unde Lantgreve to Döringh” and his wife[734].  '''married  (Berlin 26 Aug 1476) JOHANN CICERO von Brandenburg, son of ALBRECHT ACHILLES Elector of Brandenburg & hi
2 CONC s first wife Margareta von Baden (Ansbach 2 Aug 1455-Schloß Arneburg 9 Jan 1499, bur Berlin Cathedral).'''  '''He succeeded his father in 1486 as JOHANN CICERO Elector of Brandenburg.''' 
2 CONT >>>>>* b)         '''KATHARINA''' (1453-17 Jan 1534).  '''married  (26 Feb 1471) HEINRICH II "Hynek" Duke of Münsterberg Graf von Glatz, son of JIŘI von Podiebrad King of Bohemia & his second wife Johanna von Rožmital zu Blatna (1
2 CONC 7 May 1452-11 Jul 1492, bur Glatz).  Herr zu Podiebrad und Kolin 1472.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p343.htm#i3422 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/D/per_page.php?id=60895 Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anna_of_Saxony_(d._1462)_ Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Karl Wilhelm Böttiger: History of the Electoral State and Kingdom of Saxony, p. 378
2 CONT * Carl Lorenz Collmann: History of the old mountain town of Sontra in Niederhessen, p. 28
2 CONT * Karl Florentin Leidenfrost : Elector Friedrich II and his brothers, Duke Sigismund and Duke Wilhelm ..., p. 31
