1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/provnice.htm#LouisLascarisMGriffetteGrimaldi
2 CONT
2 CONT e)         VENECIA Lascaris .  The testament of “dominus Raynerius de Grimaldis...dominus Mentoni necnon dominus Rochebrune”, dated 8 Jun 1407, bequeathed property to “...Petrum, Reynerium, Anthonium et Veneciam Lascaros ex comiti
2 CONC bus Ventimilii condominos Brige eius nepotes et filios quondam domine Grifete eius filie...domino Ludovico quondam patri eorum”[1036].  Cais de Pierlas names the father of Jean Solaro and says that Jean married “la sœur de Pierre 
2 CONC Lascaris de la Brigue” [assumed to be Venecia, although Cais de Pierlas does not name her][1037].  This is consistent with the 13 Jul 1426 charter quoted above, asssuming that “avunculus” in that document was not used in its stric
2 CONC t sense of maternal uncle. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' [m''' JEAN de Solaro co-Seigneur de Châteauneuf [d’Ascros], daughter of ANTOINE de Solaro Châtelain de Pigna et d’Eze & his wife --- (-before 29 May 1448).  Cais de Pierlas says that Jean Solaro and his [older] brother Jacques
2 CONC  were named “seigneurs de Châteauneuf” in 1421 (no source cited)[1038].''']''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Jean & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *i)          BONNE de Solaro (-after 4 Apr 1465).
