2 CONT '''Marie du Berry'''1,2,3,4
2 CONT Last Edited	15 Feb 2012
2 CONT F, #18472, '''b. 1367, d. June 1434'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	John de Valois, Duke du Berry3 b. 1340, d. 15 Jun 1416
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Johanna d' Armagnac b. c 1346, d. 15 Mar 1387
2 CONT Charts	
2 CONT 14 Generation Pedigree of George III, King of Great Britain & Ireland (#1)
2 CONT 14 Generation Pedigree of George III, King of Great Britain & Ireland (#2)
2 CONT 14 Generation Pedigree of Friedrich Wilhelm III, King of Prussia
2 CONT '''     Marie du Berry was born in 1367.3 She married Louis II de Chatillon, Comte de Dunois, Seigneur de Romorantin''', son of Guy II de Chatillon, Comte de Soissons & Blois, Seigneur d'Argies, Baume, Tongre, Chimay, Trelon, & d'
2 CONC Avesnes and Marie de Namur, '''on 29 March 1386 at Burgos, Castile-Leon, Spain.5,6,3 Marie du Berry married Philippe d' Artois, Comte d'Eu''', son of Sir Jean 'Sans Terre', Comte d'Eu, Seigneur de St. Valery & d'Ault and Isabeau d
2 CONC e Melun, '''on 27 January 1393 at Paris, Ile-de-France, France.7,3,4 Marie du Berry married Jean I, 4th Duke de Bourbon, Duke d'Auverge, Comte de Clermont & Montpensier''', son of Louis II, 3rd Duke de Bourbon and Anne d' Auvergne
2 CONC , '''on 24 June 1400 at Paris, Ile-de-France, France.3 Marie du Berry died in June 1434 at Lyon, Rhône, Rhône-Alpes, France; Buried at Souvigny-en-Bourbonnais.'''3,4
2 CONT '''Family 1'''
2 CONT '''Philippe d' Artois, Comte d'Eu''' b. c 1358, d. 16 Jun 1397
2 CONT '''Children	'''
2 CONT *Charles d' Artois, Comte d'Eu, Seigneur de St. Valéry & Houdain-en-Artois, Governor of Paris, Guyenne, & Normandy7 b. c Jan 1394, d. 25 Jul 1472
2 CONT *Bonne d' Artois+8 b. c 1396, d. 17 Sep 1425
2 CONT *Catherine d' Artois7 b. c 1397, d. bt 1418 - 1422
2 CONT '''Family 2'''
2 CONT '''Jean I, 4th Duke de Bourbon, Duke d'Auverge, Comte de Clermont & Montpensier''' b. Mar 1381, d. 5 Feb 1434
2 CONT '''Children'''	
2 CONT *Louis III 'the Good', Comte de Bourbon-Montpensier+9 d. May 1486
2 CONT *Charles, Duke of Bourbon, Duke d'Auvergne, Grand Marshal of France, Governor of Languedoc, Count of Clermont+ b. 1401, d. 4 Dec 1456
