0 @N6000000002322323060@ NOTE Her father, Casimir III, having had no legal heir of the throne of Poland,
1 CONT married his daughters, and later the grandchildren were married into several
1 CONT important contemporary dynasties: the Wittlelsbachs, the Anjous, the
1 CONT Luxembourgs, and the Lithuanians (later as the Jagiellons). Casimir also had
1 CONT many mistresses, about whom little is known; the most famous of them, the
1 CONT beautiful Jewess, Esther, may have been invented by the chroniclers to
1 CONT explain the King's notable friendliness towards the Jews.
