0 @N6000000002244410867@ NOTE The third marriage? No legal heirs. By then, the question of successor
1 CONT was one of the king's main problems. Finally, Casimir designated his nephew,
1 CONT Louis of Hungary, but Louis had no sons. Then he named as his second choice
1 CONT Casimir of western Pomerania, a son of "his" eldest daughter. "His"
1 CONT apparently meaning his first wife, or even his third wife at least, bore
1 CONT daughters, but no sons. Likely, the "daughters" were of the first wife who
1 CONT died "leaving no sons". For this family tree, we'll assume this apparent fact.
