1 CONC  superb politician who brought with her an intimate knowledge of the intricacies of court life. When her husband died, leaving her with a three-year-old son, she took the title "Imperator Augustus" and defended her son Otto III’s 
1 CONC title for seven years from those who challenged him. For seven years Theophano with tact and firmness administered the empire in her son's name. A contemporary called her "a woman of discreet and firm character...with truly mascul
1 CONC ine strength."  Sometimes she used the male title "imperator Augustus
