0 @N6000000002322320710@ NOTE The second son of his father's 4th wife, as King, Casimir IV, by patience but
1 CONT tenacious policy, sought to preserve the political union between Poland and
1 CONT Lithuania and to recover the lost lands of old Poland. The great triumph of
1 CONT his reign was the final subjugation of the Teutonic Knights in 1466. Casimir
1 CONT was neither a splendid ruler nor a good and wise administrator, but a
1 CONT mistrusting, cautious, and sober head of a large family who regarded
