0 @N6000000003097932010@ NOTE Garter, Order of the   Edward III (born 1312, ruled 1327-77) became king at the age of 15 when his father, Edward II, was overthrown. He proved himself a chivalrous knight rather than a great ruler. He loved warfare, like so many 
1 CONC of his line, and tried to give it the glamour of the "good old days" by setting up a Round Table at Windsor Castle in imitation of King Arthur. He also organized the most famous of the English chivalric orders of knighthood, the O
1 CONC rder of the Garter. He gained temporary glory but no lasting profit through prolonged fighting in Scotland and in France, where he began the Hundred Years' War ( see Hundred Years' War ).  During Edward's reign a terrible plague, 
1 CONC called the Black Death, wiped out from one third to one half of the country's population and caused great social and economic changes (see Bubonic Plague ).
