1 CONT Edward III's eldest son, also called Edward, was known as the Black Prince because of the colour of his armour. He was born in 1330 and won his spurs at the Battle of Crecy in 1346. The victor of Poitiers in 1356, he became the mo
1 CONC st feared military commander in Europe, but while fighting in Spain, he caught an infection that slowly debilitated him and he predeceased his father by one year, in 1376.
