1 CONT
1 CONT John of Gaunt died on February 3, 1399.  After Lancaster's death Richard seized his estates, which caused Lancaster's son, Henry of Bolingbroke, to claim the throne as Henry IV. The children of his last marriage, known as the Beau
1 CONC forts by patent in 1397, were the line through which Henry Tudor (Henry VII) claimed the throne.
1 CONT <http://www.middle-ages.org.uk/john-of-gaunt.htm>
