0 @N6000000007329696780@ NOTE [Collier, fidonet July '95] : John  of Gaunt First Duke of   Lancaster,
1 CONT Knight of the Garter,  King of Castile and Leon, was born on 24 June
1 CONT 1340  and  died on 3  Feb. 1399.  He married Katherine, a d/o Payne
1 CONT Roelt, as   his  third  wife. Their daughter:
1 CONT Joan Roelt married, being his second wife, Ralph de Nevill, who  was a
1 CONT Knight   of the Garter and the first Earl of  Westmoreland  (1364-1425).
1 CONT Their third  son was:
1 CONT George  de Nevill, Lord Latimer. His wife was Elizabeth, a d/o Richard
1 CONT de   Beauchamp and his wife Elizabeth Berkley. He died  on  30 Dec. 1649.
1 CONT Their  son:
1 CONT Sir Henry Neville married Joan, a d/o John Bouchier, who was Baron
1 CONT Berners.  Their son:
1 CONT Richard Neville, Baron Latimer, married Ann, a d/o Sir Humphrey
1 CONT Stafford.  Their son:
1 CONT William  Neville of Wyke married Elizabeth, a d/o Sir  Giles Greville.
1 CONT Their  son:
1 CONT Richard  Neville  of Wyke (d-1590), married Barbara, a  d/o  Thomas
1 CONT Arden  of  Park Hall in County Warwick. Their son:
1 CONT Edmund  Neville  called  himself the 7th Earl  of  Westmoreland.  He
1 CONT married  Jane  Smythe  who in her will, probated  in  1647,  styled
1 CONT herself   as the  Countess of Westmoreland. Their son:
1 CONT Ralph  Neville (1588-1643) married Elizabeth Hautrey. He  considered
1 CONT himself  to be the 8th Earl of Westmoreland. Their son:
1 CONT Richard Neville, b-1607, came to Virginia in 1650. He died in 1706  in
1 CONT King  William County as Richard Westmoreland. His son:
1 CONT Richard Westmoreland lived in Prince George Co., VA. His son:  Thomas
1 CONT Westmoreland, b-ca 1700, married (3) Edith Nipper/Napier. He   died  in
1 CONT Dinwiddie Co., VA before 1784.  Their daughter:
1 CONT Sarah  Westmoreland, (1760-1832) married William Wells Nov. 1785  in
1 CONT Brunswick Co., VA and moved to Giles Co., TN with her brothers and at
1 CONT least  one sister. Their daughter: continued...
