0 @N6000000002187893016@ NOTE Vukan, veliki zupan Rashka1
1 CONT b. circa 1054?, #8904
1 CONT Pedigree 
1 CONT      Vukan, veliki zupan Rashka was older brother of Marko.2 He was described by Anna Comnena as a man "accomplished in word and deed".2 He was a Croat from Ribnica near modern Titograd, Duklja, Balkan Peninsula.2 He was a relativ
1 CONC e (family member) of King Bodin of Zeta (Duklja).3,4,5 He was born circa 1054?. He was the son of Petrislav, Grand Zupan of Rassa.2 Grand Zupan of Raska in (Serbia), Balkan Peninsula, between 1083 and 1122.5 He raided and ravaged 
1 CONC Byzantine territory as far as Skoplje several times.2 He was forced by the Emperor Alexius to acknowledge Byzantine suzerainty, and as part of the agreement had to hand over twenty hostages to the emperor, among them his nephews U
1 CONC ros and Stjepan Vuk in 1094.2 He managed - through a combination of military actions, timely (if often broken) promises and other diplomacy - to spin off from the declining Zeta and successfully resist the Byzantines, occassionall
1 CONC y expanding to the south and east.4  
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT      Children of Vukan, veliki zupan Rashka: 
1 CONT   N. N. Vukanovici+ 
1 CONT   Urosh I, veliki zupan Rashka+   b. c 1084?, d. 1145? 
1 CONT
1 CONT [S1021] Milun Jevremoviæ (e-mail address), Re: Serbian line in "Re: Serbian line", newsgroup message to soc.genealogy.medieval, 1999/02/23. Printout dated read 15 July 2001. Hereinafter cited as Re: Serbian line. 
