1 CONC  med sin far överSverige i två år, innan Albrekt av Mecklenburg kom till makten. Håkan Magnusson av Norge kröntes till kung efter sin far 1364 och fängslade sin far men släppte honom strax igen. hans far Magnus Eriksson hjälpte ho
1 CONC nom regera tills han dog år 1288? Förlovad 1362 med Elisabet av Holstein gifte sig istället Håkan 1363 med Valdemar Atterdags dotter Margareta som var endast elva år vid bröllopet.Barn:Olof III, dog i lunginflammation på Falsterbo
1 CONC  hus i unga år, varvid Margareta ärvde kronanspråken, men den dynastiska unionen mellan de tre länderna tog egentligen slut med Olof, kallad Olav IV i Norge. 
0 @N6000000002188018476@ NOTE Albert II of Mecklenburg
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Albrecht II Duke of Mecklenburg (Schwerin c. 1318 – February 18, 1379)) was a feudal lord in Northern Germany, on the shores of the Baltic Sea. He reigned as the head of the House of Mecklenburg, and since 1350's his princely seat
1 CONC  was located in Schwerin.
1 CONT
1 CONT Albrecht was born as the second, but finally the eldest surviving, son of Duke Henry II of Mecklenburg (c 1266-1329), lord of Stargard (Starij Gorod), of the old Vendic princely clan of the Obotrites, and his second wife Princess 
1 CONC Anna of Saxony-Wittenberg (d 1327), of the Princely Ascanian House.
1 CONT
1 CONT Duke Albert succeeded his father as reigning Prince (or Lord) of Mecklenburg in 1329. He was also deeply interested in obtaining some power in Scandinavia, e.g fiefs or income. The Holy Roman Emperor elevated Mecklenburg as Duchy 
1 CONC 1 July 1347, through which (togerher with his younger brother) he became the 1st Duke of Mecklenburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT April 10, 1336 he married a kinswoman, a Scandinavian heiress Euphemia of Sweden and Norway (born 1317 and died 1370). Her father was Eric of Sweden who was the Duke of Sudermannia and of Halland, and her mother was Princess Ingeb
1 CONC org of Norway, the heiress and the only legitimate daughter of King Haakon V of Norway. Through the marriage, Albrecht gained a position in Sweden, using his wife's hereditary estates etc. The duke participated in internal politic
1 CONC s of Scandinavia. Later, Albert got the nickname "Fox of Mecklenburg" from Swedes, to reflect his intrigues as well as avarice.
1 CONT
1 CONT Albert arranged his eldest son, the future Henry III of Mecklenburg, to marry the eldest daughter and potential heiress of King Waldemar IV of Denmark. Prince Henry married Ingeborg of Denmark sometime around 1362, and their infan
1 CONC t son was soon offered as Heir to Denmark, in which pursuit the Mecklenburgs then faced the contrary interests of Waldemar's youngest daughter, Queen Margaret of Norway, the future ruler of the Kalmar Union.
1 CONT
1 CONT His brother-in-law King Magnus was drawn into grave difficulties beginning from 1350's. Mighty nobles attempted to curb the concentration of royal power, and firstly put Magnus's own elder son Eric as rival king in Sweden. After y
1 CONC oung Eric's death, Albert's second son and namesake became nobility party's next puppet claimant.
1 CONT
1 CONT Duke Albert was deeply involved in making his son king in Sweden, and pursued towards becoming himself the real power behind the throne. Younger Albert deposed his uncle from the Swedish throne, and ascend as King Albert of Sweden
1 CONC .
1 CONT
1 CONT Already in Albert's and Eufemia's lifetime it was easy to see that her genealogical position was to become a pivotal point to many future claims to the Scandinavian thrones.
1 CONT
1 CONT When his first wife died, Duke Albrecht married secondly, countess Adelheid of Hohenstein, daughter of count Ulrich of Hohenstein. That marriage apparently was childless.
1 CONT
1 CONT Duke Albert had five surviving children born of the marriage with Euphemia: sons Henry, Albert and Magnus, as well as daughters Ingeborg and Anna. For his issue, see the pertinent genealogical section in Euphemia of Sweden.
1 CONT
1 CONT Already based on his very own ancestry, Albert felt himself entitled to pursue for inheritance in Sweden: He was a descendant and the heir of two women whom legends tied to Swedish royal houses as daughters of kings.
1 CONT
1 CONT Albert's father's paternal great-grandmother, a Scandinavian noblewoman named Christina, who was the wife of Henry Borwin II of Mecklenburg, was claimed at least by later tradition to have been a daughter of King Sverker II of Swe
1 CONC den. (However, Swedish sources attest that king Sverker II had a son, John, and one daughter, Helena, who married a Swedish nobleman. No further children seem to be attested in sources close to Sweden of that time.) Christina was 
1 CONC the mother of John I of Mecklenburg, whose son was Henry I of Mecklenburg. 
1 CONT Albert's father's maternal grandmother, a Scandinavian noblewoman named Marianna, who was the first wife of Duke Barnim I of Pomerania (d 1278), lord of Wolgast, was claimed to have been a daughter of King Eric X of Sweden and his
1 CONC  wife Richeza of Denmark. (However, sources of the time are scarce, and there is not much attestation of marriages, fates and precise names of those slighted daughters of Eric X.) Marianna had given birth to an only surviving chil
1 CONC d, daughter named Anastasia of Pomerania, who then became the wife of Henry I of Mecklenburg and mother of Henry I
1 CONT The Sverker dynasty had long been extinct, having lost the throne ultimately to Eric XI. The male dynasty of Eric X was also now extinct, and his other daughters had been sidestepped by Birger Jarl, the husband of his (possibly yo
1 CONC ungest) daughter, Ingeborg, who took care to secure the kingship to his own sons. Duke Albert helped the said legends of his foremothers' Swedish royalty to embellish and spread, and used them as pretexts for the royal aspirations
1 CONC .
0 @N6000000006127699208@ NOTE Albrekt II av Mecklenburg, hertig av Mecklenburg. Född 1318, död 1379. Gift år 1336 med Eufemia Eriksdotter av Sverige. Albrekt strävade efter att öka Mecklenburgs inflytande i Norden; hans äldste son fick gifta sig med en dotter 
1 CONC till Valdemar Atterdag, och han försökte bl.a. vinna den danska kronan åt sonsonen. Själv hade han gift sig med en syster till densvenske kungen, Eufemia. När hans andre son, Albrekt, kallades till Sverige 1363 följde han med, och
1 CONC  han var i själva verket den drivande kraften i sonens politik. 
