0 @N6000000002187840055@ NOTE Margaret III, Countess of Flanders
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Margaret of Dampierre (1350–1405) was Countess of Flanders and twice Duchess of Burgundy. Through her mother (Margaret of Brabant, daughter of John III, Duke of Brabant), the younger Margaret was also a heiress of the Duchies of B
1 CONC rabant and Limburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was the daughter and heir of Louis de Mâle, Count of Flanders, Count of Nevers, and Count of Rethel (1346–1384); and his wife Margaret of Brabant. Through his mother Margaret of France, Louis was also Count of Burgundy and Cou
1 CONC nt of Artois (1382–1384).
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1357, at the age of seven, the youngest Margaret, then seven, married Philip of Rouvres, grandson and heir of Eudes IV, Duke of Burgundy. Philip was eleven years old and her second cousin. He was count of Burgundy and Artois (1
1 CONC 347–1361), Duke of Burgundy (1350–1361), and became yet Count of Auvergne and Boulogne (1360–1361).
1 CONT
1 CONT Margaret was widowed in 1361, and with the death of her husband the duchy of Burgundy was inherited by John II of France. In 1363 Philip the Bold, John's youngest son, was granted the duchy, and subsequently married its former duc
1 CONC hess in 1369. Philip had earlier been Duke of Touraine (1359–1363), and became later also count of Charolais (1390–1404). When Margaret's father died in 1384, she and Philip inherited the counties of Artois, Burgundy, Flanders, Ne
1 CONC vers, and Rethel. Philip died in 1404, and Margaret died the next year.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her eldest son, John the Fearless, succeeded her in 1405 as Duke of Burgundy, Count of Burgundy, Count of Artois, and Count of Flanders. In 1406 her younger son Anthony inherited Brabant and Limburg. Nevers was at first, in her li
1 CONC fetime, given to their eldest son John, but after his accession to duchy, went later to her youngest son Philippe, thus comte de Nevers.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Louis II Countess of Rethel
1 CONT 1384–1402 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Anthony 
1 CONT Countess of Nevers
1 CONT 1384 Succeeded by:
1 CONT John 
1 CONT Countess of Artois and Flanders
1 CONT 1384–1405 
