0 @N6000000002240778481@ NOTE His reign was marked by national disunity and strife, the younger son of
1 CONT Edward, Prince of Wales (the Black Prince), and Joan, called the Fair Maid of
1 CONT Kent (1328-1385). He succeeded his grandfather, Edward III in 1377. Richard
1 CONT abdicated on September 30, 1399 and was confined to Pontefract Castle where
1 CONT he either died of starvation or was murdered in February of 1400. John of
1 CONT Gaunt, aka Henry IV, would become his successor (4th son of Edward III).
0 @N6000000002244389296@ NOTE His reign was marked by national disunity and strife, the younger son of
